msgid "How to authenticate using ``REMOTE_USER``"
msgstr "Conas fíordheimhniú ag baint úsáide as ``REMOTE_USER``"

msgid ""
"This document describes how to make use of external authentication sources "
"(where the web server sets the ``REMOTE_USER`` environment variable) in your "
"Django applications.  This type of authentication solution is typically seen "
"on intranet sites, with single sign-on solutions such as IIS and Integrated "
"Windows Authentication or Apache and `mod_authnz_ldap`_, `CAS`_, `WebAuth`_, "
"`mod_auth_sspi`_, etc."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an doiciméad seo cur síos ar conas foinsí fíordheimhnithe "
"seachtracha a úsáid (áit a shocraíonn an freastalaí gréasáin an athróg "
"timpeallachta ``REMOTE_USER``) i d'iarratais Django. Is gnách go bhfeictear "
"an cineál réiteach fíordheimhnithe seo ar shuíomhanna inlín, le réitigh "
"sínithe aonair mar IIS agus Fíordheimhniú Comhtháite Windows nó Apache agus "
"`mod_authnz_ldap`_, `CAS`_, `WebAuth`_, `mod_auth_sspi`_, srl."

msgid ""
"When the web server takes care of authentication it typically sets the "
"``REMOTE_USER`` environment variable for use in the underlying application.  "
"In Django, ``REMOTE_USER`` is made available in the :attr:`request.META "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.META>` attribute.  Django can be configured to make "
"use of the ``REMOTE_USER`` value using the ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` or "
"``PersistentRemoteUserMiddleware``, "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.RemoteUserBackend` classes found "
"in :mod:`django.contrib.auth`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a thugann an freastalaí gréasáin aire d'fhíordheimhniú de ghnáth "
"socraíonn sé an t-athróg timpeallachta ``REMOTE_USER`` le húsáid san "
"fheidhmchlár bunúsach. <django.http.HttpRequest.META>I Django, cuirtear "
"``REMOTE_USER`` ar fáil sa tréith: attr: `Request.meta `. Is féidir Django a "
"chumrú chun úsáid a bhaint as an luach ``REMOTE_USER`` ag baint úsáide as na "
"ranganna ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` nó ``PersistentRemoteUserMiddleware``, "
"agus:class: `~django.contrib.auth.backends.remoteUserBackend` atá le fáil "
"in:mod: `django.contrib.auth`."

msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Cumraíocht"

msgid ""
"First, you must add "
"the :class:`django.contrib.auth.middleware.RemoteUserMiddleware` to "
"the :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting **after** "
"the :class:`django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`::"
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, ní mór duit an:class: "
"`django.contrib.auth.middleware.remoteUserMiddleware` a chur leis an "
"socrú:setting: `MIDDLEWARE` **tar éis ** an:class: "
"`django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`::"

msgid ""
"Next, you must replace "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend` "
"with :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.RemoteUserBackend` in "
"the :setting:`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` setting::"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, ní mór duit:class: `~django.contrib.auth.backends.modelBackend` a "
"chur in ionad la:class: `~django.contrib.auth.backends.remoteUserBackend` sa "
"socrú: `AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS`::"

msgid ""
"With this setup, ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` will detect the username in "
"``request.META['REMOTE_USER']`` and will authenticate and auto-login that "
"user using the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.RemoteUserBackend`."
msgstr ""
"Leis an socrú seo, braithfidh ``RemoteUserMiddleWare`` an t-ainm úsáideora "
"in ``request.meta ['REMOTE_USER'] ``agus déanfaidh sé fíordheimhniú agus "
"logáil isteach go huathoibríoch an t-úsáideoir sin ag baint úsáide as an: "
"class: `~django.contrib.auth.backends.remoteUserBackend`."

msgid ""
"Be aware that this particular setup disables authentication with the default "
"``ModelBackend``. This means that if the ``REMOTE_USER`` value is not set "
"then the user is unable to log in, even using Django's admin interface. "
"Adding ``'django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend'`` to the "
"``AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS`` list will use ``ModelBackend`` as a fallback if "
"``REMOTE_USER`` is absent, which will solve these issues."
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas go ndíchumasaíonn an socrú áirithe seo fíordheimhniú leis an "
"réamhshocraithe ``ModelBackend``. Ciallaíonn sé seo mura socraítear an luach "
"`REMOTE_USER`` ansin níl an t-úsáideoir in ann logáil isteach, fiú ag baint "
"úsáide as comhéadan riaracháin Django. Ag cur "
"```Django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend'`` leis an liosta "
"``AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS``, úsáidfear ``ModelBackend`` mar fhillback má tá "
"``REMOTE_USER`` as láthair, rud a réiteoidh na saincheisteanna seo."

msgid ""
"Django's user management, such as the views in ``contrib.admin`` and "
"the :djadmin:`createsuperuser` management command, doesn't integrate with "
"remote users. These interfaces work with users stored in the database "
"regardless of ``AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS``."
msgstr ""
"Ní chomhtháthaíonn bainistíocht úsáideora Django, mar shampla na tuairimí i "
"`contrib.admin ``agus an t-ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `createsuperuser`, "
"le húsáideoirí iargúlta. Oibríonn na comhéadain seo le húsáideoirí atá "
"stóráilte sa bhunachar sonraí beag beann ar ``AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS`."

msgid ""
"Since the ``RemoteUserBackend`` inherits from ``ModelBackend``, you will "
"still have all of the same permissions checking that is implemented in "
"``ModelBackend``."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go dtagann an `RemoteUserBackend`` oidhreacht ó ``ModelBackend``, "
"beidh na ceadanna céanna go léir agat fós a chuirtear i bhfeidhm i "
"``ModelBackend``."

msgid ""
"Users with :attr:`is_active=False "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_active>` won't be allowed to "
"authenticate. "
"Use :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.AllowAllUsersRemoteUserBackend` if "
"you want to allow them to."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_active>Ní cheadfar d'úsáideoirí le:attr: "
"`is_active=false `fíordheimhniú. Úsáid:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.allowAllUsersRemoteUserBackend` más mian leat "
"ligean dóibh."

msgid ""
"If your authentication mechanism uses a custom HTTP header and not "
"``REMOTE_USER``, you can subclass ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` and set the "
"``header`` attribute to the desired ``request.META`` key.  For example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "``mysite/middleware.py``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This custom middleware is then used in the :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting "
"instead of :class:`django.contrib.auth.middleware.RemoteUserMiddleware`::"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Be very careful if using a ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` subclass with a custom "
"HTTP header. You must be sure that your front-end web server always sets or "
"strips that header based on the appropriate authentication checks, never "
"permitting an end-user to submit a fake (or \"spoofed\") header value. Since "
"the HTTP headers ``X-Auth-User`` and ``X-Auth_User`` (for example) both "
"normalize to the ``HTTP_X_AUTH_USER`` key in ``request.META``, you must also "
"check that your web server doesn't allow a spoofed header using underscores "
"in place of dashes."
msgstr ""
"Bí an-chúramach má úsáideann tú fo-aicme ``RemoteUserMiddleware` le "
"ceannteideal saincheaptha HTTP. Caithfidh tú a bheith cinnte go socraíonn nó "
"stiallann do fhreastalaí gréasáin tosaigh an ceannteideal sin bunaithe ar na "
"seiceálacha fíordheimhnithe cuí, gan ligean riamh d'úsáideoir deiridh luach "
"ceanntásc bréige (nó “spoofed”) a chur isteach. Ós rud é go ndéanann na "
"ceannteidil HTTP ``X-Auth-User`` agus ``X-Auth_User`` (mar shampla) normalú "
"go eochair `HTTP_X_AUTH_USER`` i `Request.meta``, ní mór duit a sheiceáil "
"freisin nach gceadaíonn do fhreastalaí gréasáin ceanntásc foláraithe ag "
"úsáid béim in áit na dtaitíní."

msgid ""
"This warning doesn't apply to ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` in its default "
"configuration with ``header = 'REMOTE_USER'``, since a key that doesn't "
"start with ``HTTP_`` in ``request.META`` can only be set by your WSGI "
"server, not directly from an HTTP request header."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann an rabhadh seo le `RemoteUserMiddleware`` ina chumraíocht "
"réamhshocraithe le ``header = 'REMOTE_USER'`, ós rud é nach féidir le "
"eochair nach dtosaíonn le `HTTP_`` i `request.meta`` a shocrú ach ag do "
"fhreastalaí WSGI, ní go díreach ó cheannteideal iarratais HTTP."

msgid ""
"If you need more control, you can create your own authentication backend "
"that inherits from :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.RemoteUserBackend` "
"and override one or more of its attributes and methods."
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn níos mó smachta uait, is féidir leat do chúltaca "
"fíordheimhnithe féin a chruthú a fhaigheann oidhreacht ó:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.remoteUserBackend` agus ceann amháin nó níos "
"mó dá thréithe agus modhanna a shárú."

msgid "Using ``REMOTE_USER`` on login pages only"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as ``REMOTE_USER`` ar leathanaigh logála isteach amháin"

msgid ""
"The ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` authentication middleware assumes that the HTTP "
"request header ``REMOTE_USER`` is present with all authenticated requests. "
"That might be expected and practical when Basic HTTP Auth with ``htpasswd`` "
"or similar mechanisms are used, but with Negotiate (GSSAPI/Kerberos) or "
"other resource intensive authentication methods, the authentication in the "
"front-end HTTP server is usually only set up for one or a few login URLs, "
"and after successful authentication, the application is supposed to maintain "
"the authenticated session itself."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an middleware fíordheimhnithe ``RemoteUserMiddleware`` go bhfuil an "
"ceannteideal iarratais HTTP ``REMOTE_USER`` i láthair le gach iarratas "
"fíordheimhnithe. D'fhéadfaí súil leis sin agus praiticiúil nuair a úsáidtear "
"Basic HTTP Auth le `htpasswd` nó meicníochtaí den chineál céanna, ach le "
"Negoate (GSSAPI/KerberOS) nó modhanna fíordheimhnithe dian-acmhainní eile, "
"de ghnáth ní bhunaítear an fíordheimhniú sa bhfreastalaí HTTP tosaigh ach le "
"haghaidh URL amháin nó cúpla URL, agus tar éis fíordheimhniú rathúil, "
"ceaptar an feidhmchlár an seisiún fíordheimhnithe féin a choinneáil."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.PersistentRemoteUserMiddleware` "
"provides support for this use case. It will maintain the authenticated "
"session until explicit logout by the user. The class can be used as a drop-"
"in replacement "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.RemoteUserMiddleware` in the "
"documentation above."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.auth.middleware.persistentRemoteUserMiddleware` "
"tacaíocht ar fáil don chás úsáide seo. Coinneoidh sé an seisiún "
"fíordheimhnithe go dtí go ndéanfaidh an t-úsáideoir logáil amach follasach. "
"Is féidir an rang a úsáid mar athsholáthar titim isteach de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.remoteUserMiddleware` sa dhoiciméadú thuas."

msgid "How to use Django's CSRF protection"
msgstr "Conas cosaint CSRF Django a úsáid"

msgid "To take advantage of CSRF protection in your views, follow these steps:"
msgstr ""
"Chun leas a bhaint as cosaint CSRF i do thuairimí, lean na céimeanna seo:"

msgid ""
"The CSRF middleware is activated by default in the :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` "
"setting. If you override that setting, remember that "
"``'django.middleware.csrf.CsrfViewMiddleware'`` should come before any view "
"middleware that assume that CSRF attacks have been dealt with."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an middleware CSRF i ngníomh de réir réamhshocraithe sa shocrú:: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`. Má sháraigh tú an socrú sin, cuimhnigh gur chóir go dtiocfadh "
"``django.middleware.csrf.csrfviewMiddleware'` roimh aon mheán dearcadh a "
"ghlacann leis gur déileáladh le hionsaithe CSRF."

msgid ""
"If you disabled it, which is not recommended, you can "
"use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` on particular views "
"you want to protect (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Má dhíchumasaigh tú é, nach moltar, is féidir leat: func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` a úsáid ar thuairimí áirithe ar "
"mhaith leat a chosaint (féach thíos)."

msgid ""
"In any template that uses a POST form, use the :ttag:`csrf_token` tag inside "
"the ``<form>`` element if the form is for an internal URL, e.g.:"
msgstr ""
"In aon teimpléad a úsáideann foirm POST, bain úsáid as an clibe:ttag: "
"`csrf_token` taobh istigh den eilimint ```má tá an fhoirm le haghaidh URL "
"inmheánach, <form>m.sh.:"

msgid ""
"This should not be done for POST forms that target external URLs, since that "
"would cause the CSRF token to be leaked, leading to a vulnerability."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart é seo a dhéanamh le haghaidh foirmeacha POST a dhíríonn ar "
"URLanna seachtracha, mar go mbeadh sé sin ina chúis le sceitheadh ​​an "
"chomhartha CSRF, rud a d’fhágfadh go mbeadh leochaileacht ann."

msgid ""
"In the corresponding view functions, ensure "
"that :class:`~django.template.RequestContext` is used to render the response "
"so that ``{% csrf_token %}`` will work properly. If you're using "
"the :func:`~django.shortcuts.render` function, generic views, or contrib "
"apps, you are covered already since these all use ``RequestContext``."
msgstr ""
"Sna feidhmeanna amharc comhfhreagracha, cinntigh go n-úsáidtear: class: "
"`~django.template.requestContext` chun an freagra a thabhairt ionas go n-"
"oibreoidh ``{% csrf_token%} `i gceart. Má tá tú ag úsáid an fheidhme:func: "
"`~django.shortcuts.render`, tuairimí cineálacha, nó aipeanna contrib, tá tú "
"clúdaithe cheana ós rud é go n-úsáideann siad seo go léir ``RequestContext``."

msgid "Using CSRF protection with AJAX"
msgstr "Cosaint CSRF a úsáid le AJAX"

msgid ""
"While the above method can be used for AJAX POST requests, it has some "
"inconveniences: you have to remember to pass the CSRF token in as POST data "
"with every POST request. For this reason, there is an alternative method: on "
"each XMLHttpRequest, set a custom ``X-CSRFToken`` header (as specified by "
"the :setting:`CSRF_HEADER_NAME` setting) to the value of the CSRF token. "
"This is often easier because many JavaScript frameworks provide hooks that "
"allow headers to be set on every request."
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir an modh thuas a úsáid le haghaidh iarratais AJAX POST, tá "
"roinnt míchompordach aige: caithfidh tú cuimhneamh an comhartha CSRF a chur "
"isteach mar shonraí POST le gach iarratas POST. Ar an gcúis seo, tá modh "
"malartach ann: ar gach XMLHttpRequest, socraigh ceannteideal saincheaptha "
"``X-CSRFToken` (mar a shonraítear leis an socrú:setting: `CSRF_HEADER_NAME`) "
"le luach an chomhartha CSRF. Is minic a bhíonn sé seo níos éasca toisc go "
"soláthraíonn go leor creataí JavaScript crúcaí a cheadaíonn ceanntásca a "
"shocrú ar gach iarratas."

msgid ""
"First, you must get the CSRF token. How to do that depends on whether or not "
"the :setting:`CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` and :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` "
"settings are enabled."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, ní mór duit an comhartha CSRF a fháil. Braitheann conas é sin a "
"dhéanamh ar an bhfuil na socruithe: 'CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` agus:setting: "
"`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` cumasaithe nó nach bhfuil."

msgid ""
"Acquiring the token if :setting:`CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` "
"and :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` are ``False``"
msgstr ""
"An comhartha a fháil má tá: socrú: `CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` agus:setting: "
"`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` ``False``"

msgid ""
"The recommended source for the token is the ``csrftoken`` cookie, which will "
"be set if you've enabled CSRF protection for your views as outlined above."
msgstr ""
"Is é an fhoinse molta don chomhartha an fianán `csrftoken``, a shocrófar má "
"chuir tú cosaint CSRF ar chumas do do thuairimí mar a leagtar amach thuas."

msgid ""
"The CSRF token cookie is named ``csrftoken`` by default, but you can control "
"the cookie name via the :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_NAME` setting."
msgstr ""
"Ainmnítear “csrftoken`` ar an bhfianán comhartha CSRF de réir "
"réamhshocraithe, ach is féidir leat ainm na fianán a rialú tríd an "
"socrú:setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_NAME`."

msgid "You can acquire the token like this:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat an comhartha a fháil mar seo:"

msgid ""
"The above code could be simplified by using the `JavaScript Cookie library "
"<https://github.com/js-cookie/js-cookie/>`_ to replace ``getCookie``:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfaí an cód thuas a shimpliú trí úsáid a bhaint as an leabharlann "
"`JavaScript Cookie <https://github.com/js-cookie/js-cookie/>`_ chun "
"``getCookie`` a chur in ionad:"

msgid ""
"The CSRF token is also present in the DOM in a masked form, but only if "
"explicitly included using :ttag:`csrf_token` in a template. The cookie "
"contains the canonical, unmasked token. "
"The :class:`~django.middleware.csrf.CsrfViewMiddleware` will accept either. "
"However, in order to protect against `BREACH`_ attacks, it's recommended to "
"use a masked token."
msgstr ""
"Tá an comhartha CSRF i láthair sa DOM i bhfoirm masctha freisin, ach amháin "
"má chuirtear san áireamh go sainráite ag baint úsáidea:ttag: `csrf_token` i "
"dteimpléad. Tá an comhartha canónach, neamhchumtha sa fhianán. Glacfaidh an: "
"Class: `~django.middleware.csrf.csrfViewMiddleware` ceachtar acu. Mar sin "
"féin, d'fhonn cosaint a dhéanamh ar ionsaithe `BREACH`_, moltar comhartha "
"masctha a úsáid."

msgid ""
"If your view is not rendering a template containing the :ttag:`csrf_token` "
"template tag, Django might not set the CSRF token cookie. This is common in "
"cases where forms are dynamically added to the page. To address this case, "
"Django provides a view decorator which forces setting of the "
"cookie: :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.ensure_csrf_cookie`."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil teimpléad á rindreáil ag d'amharc ina bhfuil an clib "
"teimpléad:ttag: `csrf_token`, b'fhéidir nach socraíonn Django an fianán "
"comhartha CSRF. Tá sé seo coitianta i gcásanna ina gcuirtear foirmeacha go "
"dinimiciúil leis an leathanach. Chun aghaidh a thabhairt ar an gcás seo, "
"soláthraíonn Django maisitheoir amharc a chuireann iallach ar an bhfianán a "
"shocrú: :func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.ensure_csrf_cookie`."

msgid ""
"Acquiring the token if :setting:`CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` "
"or :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` is ``True``"
msgstr ""
"An comhartha a fháil más:socrú: `CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` nó:setting: "
"`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` ``True``"

msgid ""
"If you activate :setting:`CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` "
"or :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY`, you must include the CSRF token in your "
"HTML and read the token from the DOM with JavaScript:"
msgstr ""
"Má ghníomhachtaí:setting: `CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` nó:setting: "
"`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY`, ní mór duit an comhartha CSRF a áireamh i do HTML "
"agus an comhartha ón DOM a léamh le JavaScript:"

msgid "Setting the token on the AJAX request"
msgstr "An comhartha a shocrú ar an iarratas AJAX"

msgid ""
"Finally, you'll need to set the header on your AJAX request. Using the "
"`fetch()`_ API:"
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, beidh ort an ceanntásc a shocrú ar d'iarratas AJAX. Ag baint "
"úsáide as an API `fetch () `_:"

msgid "Using CSRF protection in Jinja2 templates"
msgstr "Cosaint CSRF a úsáid i dteimpléid Jinja2"

msgid ""
"Django's :class:`~django.template.backends.jinja2.Jinja2` template backend "
"adds ``{{ csrf_input }}`` to the context of all templates which is "
"equivalent to ``{% csrf_token %}`` in the Django template language. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Django's:class: `~django.template.backends.jinja2.jinja2` cuireann cúltaca "
"teimpléad ``{{csrf_input}}`` le comhthéacs na teimpléid go léir atá "
"comhionann le ``{% csrf_token%}`` sa teanga teimpléid Django. Mar shampla:"

msgid "Using the decorator method"
msgstr "An modh maisitheora a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Rather than adding ``CsrfViewMiddleware`` as a blanket protection, you can "
"use the :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` decorator, which "
"has exactly the same functionality, on particular views that need the "
"protection. It must be used **both** on views that insert the CSRF token in "
"the output, and on those that accept the POST form data. (These are often "
"the same view function, but not always)."
msgstr ""
"Seachas ``csrfViewMiddleware` a chur leis mar chosaint blaincéid, is féidir "
"leat an maisitheoir: func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` a "
"úsáid, a bhfuil an fheidhmiúlacht chéanna díreach aige, ar thuairimí áirithe "
"a dteastaíonn an cosaint uathu. Caithfear é a úsáid**an bheath** ar "
"thuairimí a chuireann an comhartha CSRF isteach san aschur, agus ar na "
"tuairimí a ghlacann leis na sonraí foirme POST. (Is minic gurb iad seo an "
"fheidhm radharc céanna, ach ní i gcónaí)."

msgid ""
"Use of the decorator by itself is **not recommended**, since if you forget "
"to use it, you will have a security hole. The 'belt and braces' strategy of "
"using both is fine, and will incur minimal overhead."
msgstr ""
"Ní mholtar an maisitheoir a úsáid leis féin **, ós rud é má dhéanann tú "
"dearmad é a úsáid, beidh poll slándála agat. Tá an straitéis 'crios agus "
"brísea' chun an dá cheann a úsáid go breá, agus beidh lasbhreas íosta ann."

msgid "Handling rejected requests"
msgstr "Iarrataí a dhiúltaithe"

msgid ""
"By default, a '403 Forbidden' response is sent to the user if an incoming "
"request fails the checks performed by ``CsrfViewMiddleware``. This should "
"usually only be seen when there is a genuine Cross Site Request Forgery, or "
"when, due to a programming error, the CSRF token has not been included with "
"a POST form."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, seoltar freagra '403 Forbidden' chuig an úsáideoir "
"má theipeann ar iarratas isteach ar na seiceálacha a dhéanann "
"``CSRFViewMiddleware`. Níor cheart é seo a fheiceáil de ghnáth ach nuair a "
"bhíonn fíorbhóideacht Iarratas Tras-Láithreáin ann, nó nuair nach bhfuil an "
"comhartha CSRF san áireamh le foirm POST mar gheall ar earráid cláraithe."

msgid ""
"The error page, however, is not very friendly, so you may want to provide "
"your own view for handling this condition. To do this, set "
"the :setting:`CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW` setting."
msgstr ""
"Níl an leathanach earráide an-chairdiúil, áfach, mar sin b'fhéidir gur "
"mhaith leat do dhearcadh féin a sholáthar chun an riocht seo a láimhseáil. "
"Chun seo a dhéanamh, socraigh an socrú: setting: `CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW`."

msgid ""
"CSRF failures are logged as warnings to the :ref:`django.security.csrf "
"<django-security-logger>` logger."
msgstr ""
"<django-security-logger>Déantar teipeanna CSRF a logáil mar rabhaidh don "
"logger: ref: `django.security.csrf `."

msgid "Using CSRF protection with caching"
msgstr "Cosaint CSRF a úsáid le caching"

msgid ""
"If the :ttag:`csrf_token` template tag is used by a template (or the "
"``get_token`` function is called some other way), ``CsrfViewMiddleware`` "
"will add a cookie and a ``Vary: Cookie`` header to the response. This means "
"that the middleware will play well with the cache middleware if it is used "
"as instructed (``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` goes before all other middleware)."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann teimpléad an chlib teimpléad:ttag: `csrf_token` (nó tugtar "
"bealach eile ar an bhfeidhm ``get_token``), cuirfidh `CSRFViewMiddleware`` "
"fianán agus ceannteideal ``Vary: Cookie`` leis an bhfreagra. Ciallaíonn sé "
"seo go n-imrífidh an middleware go maith leis an middleware taisce má "
"úsáidtear é mar a threoraítear (téann ``UpdateCacheMiddleware` roimh gach "
"meán-earraí eile)."

msgid ""
"However, if you use cache decorators on individual views, the CSRF "
"middleware will not yet have been able to set the Vary header or the CSRF "
"cookie, and the response will be cached without either one. In this case, on "
"any views that will require a CSRF token to be inserted you should use "
"the :func:`django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` decorator first::"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má úsáideann tú maisitheoirí taisce ar thuairimí aonair, ní "
"bheidh an middleware CSRF in ann an ceannteideal Vary nó an fianán CSRF a "
"shocrú fós, agus cuirfear an freagra a chosc gan ceachtar ceann amháin. Sa "
"chás seo, ar aon tuairimí a éilíonn comhartha CSRF a chur isteach ba chóir "
"duit an maisitheoir: func: `django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` a "
"úsáid ar dtús::"

msgid ""
"If you are using class-based views, you can refer to :ref:`Decorating class-"
"based views<decorating-class-based-views>`."
msgstr ""
"<decorating-class-based-views>Má tá tuairimí bunaithe ar rang-bhunaithe á "
"úsáid agat, is féidir leat tagairt a thabhairt do:ref: `Tuairimí "
"rangbhunaithe a mhaisiú `."

msgid "Testing and CSRF protection"
msgstr "Tástáil agus cosaint CSRF"

msgid ""
"The ``CsrfViewMiddleware`` will usually be a big hindrance to testing view "
"functions, due to the need for the CSRF token which must be sent with every "
"POST request. For this reason, Django's HTTP client for tests has been "
"modified to set a flag on requests which relaxes the middleware and the "
"``csrf_protect`` decorator so that they no longer rejects requests. In every "
"other respect (e.g. sending cookies etc.), they behave the same."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth beidh an `CSRFViewMiddleware` 'ina bhac mór ar fheidhmeanna "
"radhairc a thástáil, mar gheall ar an ngá atá leis an gcomhartha CSRF nach "
"mór a sheoladh le gach iarratas POST. Ar an gcúis seo, modhnaíodh cliant "
"HTTP Django le haghaidh tástálacha chun bratach a shocrú ar iarratais a "
"mhaolann an middleware agus an maisitheoir `csrf_protect`` ionas nach "
"dhiúltaíonn siad iarratais a thuilleadh. I ngach leith eile (m.sh. fianáin a "
"sheoladh srl.), iompraíonn siad mar an gcéanna."

msgid ""
"If, for some reason, you *want* the test client to perform CSRF checks, you "
"can create an instance of the test client that enforces CSRF checks:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat, ar chúis éigin, * an cliant tástála seiceálacha CSRF a "
"dhéanamh, is féidir leat sampla den chliant tástála a chruthú a "
"fhorfheidhmíonn seiceálacha CSRF:"

msgid "Edge cases"
msgstr "Cásanna imeall"

msgid ""
"Certain views can have unusual requirements that mean they don't fit the "
"normal pattern envisaged here. A number of utilities can be useful in these "
"situations. The scenarios they might be needed in are described in the "
"following section."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir go mbeadh riachtanais neamhghnácha ag tuairimí áirithe a "
"chiallaíonn nach n-oireann siad don ghnáthphatrún Is féidir le roinnt "
"fóntais a bheith úsáideach sna cásanna seo. Déantar cur síos ar na cásanna a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith ag teastáil iontu sa chuid seo a leanas."

msgid "Disabling CSRF protection for just a few views"
msgstr "Cosaint CSRF a dhíchumasú le haghaidh ach cúpla tuairim"

msgid "Most views requires CSRF protection, but a few do not."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn cosaint CSRF ar an gcuid is mó de na tuairimí, ach níl cúpla ceann "
"acu."

msgid ""
"Solution: rather than disabling the middleware and applying ``csrf_protect`` "
"to all the views that need it, enable the middleware and "
"use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt`."
msgstr ""
"Réiteach: seachas an middleware a dhíchumasú agus `csrf_protect`` a chur i "
"bhfeidhm ar na tuairimí go léir a theastaíonn uathu, cumasaigh an middleware "
"agus úsáide:func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt`."

msgid ""
"Setting the token when ``CsrfViewMiddleware.process_view()`` is not used"
msgstr ""
"An comhartha a shocrú nuair nach n-úsáidtear "
"``CSRFViewMiddleware.process_view () ``"

msgid ""
"There are cases when ``CsrfViewMiddleware.process_view`` may not have run "
"before your view is run - 404 and 500 handlers, for example - but you still "
"need the CSRF token in a form."
msgstr ""
"Tá cásanna ann nuair nach raibh `CSRFViewMiddleware.process_view`` rith sula "
"ndéantar do radharc a reáchtáil - 404 agus 500 láimhseálaí, mar shampla - "
"ach teastaíonn an comhartha CSRF uait fós i bhfoirm."

msgid "Solution: use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.requires_csrf_token`"
msgstr ""
"Réiteach: úsáid: func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.requires_csrf_token`"

msgid "Including the CSRF token in an unprotected view"
msgstr "An comhartha CSRF san áireamh i radharc gan chosaint"

msgid ""
"There may be some views that are unprotected and have been exempted by "
"``csrf_exempt``, but still need to include the CSRF token."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh roinnt tuairimí ann nach bhfuil gan chosaint agus a "
"bhfuil díolmhaithe orthu ag `csrf_exempt``, ach ní mór an comhartha CSRF a "
"áireamh fós."

msgid ""
"Solution: use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` followed "
"by :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.requires_csrf_token`. (i.e. "
"``requires_csrf_token`` should be the innermost decorator)."
msgstr ""
"Réiteach: úsáid: func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` ina "
"dhiaidh sin: func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.requires_csrf_token`. (ie, "
"ba chóir go mbeadh `requires_csrf_token`` an maisitheoir is istigh)."

msgid "Protecting a view for only one path"
msgstr "Radharc a chosaint le haghaidh cosán amháin amháin"

msgid ""
"A view needs CSRF protection under one set of conditions only, and mustn't "
"have it for the rest of the time."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn cosaint CSRF ó dhearcadh faoi shraith amháin coinníollacha "
"amháin, agus níor cheart dó é a bheith aige don chuid eile den am."

msgid ""
"Solution: use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` for the "
"whole view function, and :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` "
"for the path within it that needs protection. Example::"
msgstr ""
"Réiteach: úsáid: func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` don "
"fheidhm amharc iomlán, agus:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` don chosán laistigh de dhíth a "
"chosaint air. Sampla::"

msgid "Protecting a page that uses AJAX without an HTML form"
msgstr "Leathanach a chosaint a úsáideann AJAX gan foirm HTML"

msgid ""
"A page makes a POST request via AJAX, and the page does not have an HTML "
"form with a :ttag:`csrf_token` that would cause the required CSRF cookie to "
"be sent."
msgstr ""
"Déanann leathanach iarratas POST trí AJAX, agus níl foirm HTML ag an "
"leathanach le a:ttag: `csrf_token` a chuirfeadh an fianán CSRF riachtanach a "
"sheoladh."

msgid ""
"Solution: use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.ensure_csrf_cookie` on "
"the view that sends the page."
msgstr ""
"Réiteach: úsáid: func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.ensure_csrf_cookie` ar "
"an radharc a sheolann an leathanach."

msgid "CSRF protection in reusable applications"
msgstr "Cosaint CSRF in iarratais in-athúsáidte"

msgid ""
"Because it is possible for the developer to turn off the "
"``CsrfViewMiddleware``, all relevant views in contrib apps use the "
"``csrf_protect`` decorator to ensure the security of these applications "
"against CSRF. It is recommended that the developers of other reusable apps "
"that want the same guarantees also use the ``csrf_protect`` decorator on "
"their views."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go bhfuil sé indéanta don fhorbróir an `CSRFViewMiddleware` a "
"mhúchadh, úsáideann gach tuairim ábhartha in aipeanna contrib an maisitheoir "
"`csrf_protect`` chun slándáil na bhfeidhmchlár seo i gcoinne CSRF a "
"chinntiú. Moltar go n-úsáideann forbróirí aipeanna in-athúsáidte eile a "
"dteastaíonn na ráthaíochtaí céanna uathu an maisitheoir `csrf_protect`` ar a "
"dtuairimí."

msgid "How to write a custom storage class"
msgstr "Conas rang stórála saincheaptha a scríobh"

msgid ""
"If you need to provide custom file storage -- a common example is storing "
"files on some remote system -- you can do so by defining a custom storage "
"class. You'll need to follow these steps:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit stóráil comhaid saincheaptha a sholáthar - sampla coitianta ná "
"comhaid a stóráil ar chóras iargúlta éigin - is féidir leat é sin a dhéanamh "
"trí rang stórála saincheaptha a shainiú. Beidh ort na céimeanna seo a "
"leanúint:"

msgid ""
"Your custom storage system must be a subclass of "
"``django.core.files.storage.Storage``::"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh do chóras stórála saincheaptha a bheith ina fho-aicme de "
"``Django.Core.Files.Storage.Storage``:"

msgid ""
"Django must be able to instantiate your storage system without any "
"arguments. This means that any settings should be taken from "
"``django.conf.settings``::"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh Django a bheith in ann do chóras stórála a dhéanamh gan aon "
"argóintí. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur chóir aon socruithe a thógáil ó "
"``django.conf.settings``:"

msgid ""
"Your storage class must implement the :meth:`_open()` and :meth:`_save()` "
"methods, along with any other methods appropriate to your storage class. See "
"below for more on these methods."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór do rang stórála na modhanna: meth: `_open () `agus:meth: `_save ()` a "
"chur i bhfeidhm, mar aon le haon mhodhanna eile atá oiriúnach do do rang "
"stórála. Féach thíos le haghaidh tuilleadh faoi na modhanna seo."

msgid ""
"In addition, if your class provides local file storage, it must override the "
"``path()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, má sholáthraíonn do rang stóráil comhad áitiúil, caithfidh "
"sé an modh ``path () `a shárú."

msgid ""
"Your storage class must be :ref:`deconstructible <custom-deconstruct-"
"method>` so it can be serialized when it's used on a field in a migration. "
"As long as your field has arguments that are themselves :ref:`serializable "
"<migration-serializing>`, you can use the "
"``django.utils.deconstruct.deconstructible`` class decorator for this "
"(that's what Django uses on FileSystemStorage)."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh do rang stórála a bheith: ref: `dífhoirmithe <custom-deconstruct-"
"method>`ionas gur féidir é a shraitheadh nuair a úsáidtear é ar réimse in "
"imirce. Chomh fada agus a bhíonn argóintí ag do réimse atá féin:ref: "
"`serializable <migration-serializing>`, is féidir leat an maisitheoir aicme "
"``django.utils.deconstruct.deconstructible`` a úsáid chuige seo (sin an rud "
"a úsáideann Django ar FileSystemStorage)."

msgid ""
"By default, the following methods raise ``NotImplementedError`` and will "
"typically have to be overridden:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ardaíonn na modhanna seo a leanas "
"`NotImplementederror`` agus is gnách go gcaithfear iad a shárú:"

msgid ":meth:`Storage.delete`"
msgstr ":meth: `Stóráil.delete`"

msgid ":meth:`Storage.exists`"
msgstr ":meth: `Storage.exists`"

msgid ":meth:`Storage.listdir`"
msgstr ":meth: `Storage.listDir`"

msgid ":meth:`Storage.size`"
msgstr ":meth: `Stóráil.size`"

msgid ":meth:`Storage.url`"
msgstr ":meth: `Storage.url`"

msgid ""
"Note however that not all these methods are required and may be deliberately "
"omitted. As it happens, it is possible to leave each method unimplemented "
"and still have a working Storage."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, áfach, nach bhfuil na modhanna seo uile ag teastáil agus "
"gur féidir iad a fhágáil d'aon ghnó. Mar a tharlaíonn sé, is féidir gach "
"modh a fhágáil gan cur i bhfeidhm agus Stóráil oibre a bheith agat fós."

msgid ""
"By way of example, if listing the contents of certain storage backends turns "
"out to be expensive, you might decide not to implement ``Storage.listdir()``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má bhíonn sé daor ábhar cúltaca stórála áirithe a liostáil, "
"b'fhéidir go gcinneann tú gan `Storage.listDir () `a chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"Another example would be a backend that only handles writing to files. In "
"this case, you would not need to implement any of the above methods."
msgstr ""
"Sampla eile ba ea cúltaca nach láimhseálann ach scríbhneoireacht chuig "
"comhaid. Sa chás seo, ní bheadh ort aon cheann de na modhanna thuas a chur i "
"bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"Ultimately, which of these methods are implemented is up to you. Leaving "
"some methods unimplemented will result in a partial (possibly broken) "
"interface."
msgstr ""
"I ndeireadh na dála, is fútsa atá cé acu de na modhanna seo a chuirtear i "
"bhfeidhm. Beidh comhéadan páirteach (briste b'fhéidir) mar thoradh ar roinnt "
"modhanna gan cur i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"You'll also usually want to use hooks specifically designed for custom "
"storage objects. These are:"
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth beidh tú ag iarraidh crúcaí a úsáid atá deartha go sonrach le "
"haghaidh rudaí stórála saincheaptha Seo iad seo:"

msgid "**Required**."
msgstr "**Riachtanáil**."

msgid ""
"Called by ``Storage.open()``, this is the actual mechanism the storage class "
"uses to open the file. This must return a ``File`` object, though in most "
"cases, you'll want to return some subclass here that implements logic "
"specific to the backend storage system. The :exc:`FileNotFoundError` "
"exception should be raised when a file doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar air ag ``Storage.open () ``, is é seo an meicníocht iarbhír a "
"úsáideann an rang stórála chun an comhad a oscailt. Caithfidh sé seo réad "
"``Comhad ``a thabhairt ar ais, cé i bhformhór na gcásanna, beidh tú ag "
"iarraidh roinnt fo-aicme a thabhairt ar ais anseo a chuireann loighic go "
"sonrach don chóras stórála cúltaca i bhfeidhm. Ba chóir an eisceacht: EXC: "
"`FileNotFoundError` a ardú nuair nach bhfuil comhad ann."

msgid ""
"Called by ``Storage.save()``. The ``name`` will already have gone through "
"``get_valid_name()`` and ``get_available_name()``, and the ``content`` will "
"be a ``File`` object itself."
msgstr ""
"Glaoigh ``Storage.save () ``. Beidh an ``ainm ``imithe cheana féin trí "
"``get_valid_name ()`` agus ``get_available_name () ``, agus is réad "
"``Comhad`` féin a bheidh an ``content``."

msgid ""
"Should return the actual name of the file saved (usually the ``name`` passed "
"in, but if the storage needs to change the file name return the new name "
"instead)."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir ainm iarbhír an chomhaid a shábháiltear a thabhairt ar ais (de "
"ghnáth an ``ainm ``a chuirtear isteach, ach más gá don stóráil ainm an "
"chomhaid a athrú, cuir an t-ainm nua ar ais ina ionad)."

msgid ""
"Returns a filename suitable for use with the underlying storage system. The "
"``name`` argument passed to this method is either the original filename sent "
"to the server or, if ``upload_to`` is a callable, the filename returned by "
"that method after any path information is removed. Override this to "
"customize how non-standard characters are converted to safe filenames."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé ainm comhaid atá oiriúnach le húsáid leis an gcóras stórála "
"bunúsach. Is é an argóint ``name`` a cuireadh ar aghaidh chuig an modh seo "
"ná an bunainm comhaid a seoladh chuig an bhfreastalaí nó, má tá "
"``upload_to`` inghlaoite, cuirtear ainm an chomhaid ar ais ar an modh sin "
"tar éis aon fhaisnéis cosán a bhaint. Sáraigh é seo chun an chaoi a "
"dtiontaítear carachtair neamhchaighdeánacha go comhadainmneacha sábháilte a "
"shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"The code provided on ``Storage`` retains only alpha-numeric characters, "
"periods and underscores from the original filename, removing everything else."
msgstr ""
"Ní choimeádann an cód a chuirtear ar `Stóráil ``ach carachtair, tréimhsí "
"agus béim alfa-uimhriúla ón ainm comhaid bunaidh, ag baint gach rud eile."

msgid ""
"Returns an alternative filename based on the ``file_root`` and ``file_ext`` "
"parameters. By default, an underscore plus a random 7 character alphanumeric "
"string is appended to the filename before the extension."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ainm comhaid malartach ar ais bunaithe ar na paraiméadair "
"`file_root`` agus ``file_ext``. De réir réamhshocraithe, cuirtear béim móide "
"sreang alfauméireach randamach 7 charachtar leis an ainm comhaid roimh an "
"síneadh."

msgid ""
"Returns a filename that is available in the storage mechanism, possibly "
"taking the provided filename into account. The ``name`` argument passed to "
"this method will have already cleaned to a filename valid for the storage "
"system, according to the ``get_valid_name()`` method described above."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ainm comhaid atá ar fáil sa mheicníocht stórála, agus b'fhéidir ag "
"cur an ainm comhaid a chuirtear ar fáil san áireamh. Beidh an argóint ``ainm "
"``a chuirtear chuig an modh seo glan cheana féin chuig ainm comhaid atá "
"bailí don chóras stórála, de réir an mhodha ``get_valid_name ()`` a "
"thuairiscítear thuas."

msgid ""
"The length of the filename will not exceed ``max_length``, if provided. If a "
"free unique filename cannot be found, a :exc:`SuspiciousFileOperation "
"<django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation>` exception is raised."
msgstr ""
"Ní rachaidh fad an ainm comhaid thar ``max_length ``, má chuirtear ar fáil. "
"<django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation>Mura féidir ainm comhaid uathúil "
"saor in aisce a fháil, ardaítear eisceacht a: exc: `SuspiciousFileOperation "
"`."

msgid ""
"If a file with ``name`` already exists, ``get_alternative_name()`` is called "
"to obtain an alternative name."
msgstr ""
"Má tá comhad le ``ainm ``ann cheana féin, tugtar ``get_alternative_name ()`` "
"chun ainm malartach a fháil."

msgid "Use your custom storage engine"
msgstr "Úsáid d'inneall stórála saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"The first step to using your custom storage with Django is to tell Django "
"about the file storage backend you'll be using. This is done using "
"the :setting:`STORAGES` setting. This setting maps storage aliases, which "
"are a way to refer to a specific storage throughout Django, to a dictionary "
"of settings for that specific storage backend. The settings in the inner "
"dictionaries are described fully in the :setting:`STORAGES` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad chéim chun do stóráil saincheaptha a úsáid le Django ná insint "
"do Django faoin gcúltaca stórála comhaid a bheidh á úsáid agat. Déantar é "
"seo ag baint úsáide as an socrú:setting: `STORAGES`. Déanann an socrú seo "
"mapáil ainmneacha stórála, ar bealach iad chun tagairt a dhéanamh do stóráil "
"ar leith ar fud Django, chuig foclóir socruithe don chúlcheann stórála "
"sonrach sin. Déantar cur síos iomlán ar na socruithe sna foclóirí istigh sa "
"doiciméadach:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"Storages are then accessed by alias from "
"the :data:`django.core.files.storage.storages` dictionary::"
msgstr ""
"Ansin déantar rochtain ar stórálaí ag ainm ón bhfoclóir:data: "
"`django.core.files.storage.storages`:"

msgid "How to write custom lookups"
msgstr "Conas cuardaigh saincheaptha a scríobh"

msgid ""
"Django offers a wide variety of :ref:`built-in lookups <field-lookups>` for "
"filtering (for example, ``exact`` and ``icontains``). This documentation "
"explains how to write custom lookups and how to alter the working of "
"existing lookups. For the API references of lookups, see the :doc:`/ref/"
"models/lookups`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django <field-lookups>réimse leathan de: ref: `cuardaigh ionsuite "
"`ar fáil le haghaidh scagadh (mar shampla, ``cruth`` agus ``icontains`). "
"Míníonn an doiciméadú seo conas cuardaigh saincheaptha a scríobh agus conas "
"obair na gcuardaigh atá ann cheana a athrú. Le haghaidh tagairtí API de "
"chuardaigh, féach an:doc: `/ref/models/lookups`."

msgid "A lookup example"
msgstr "Sampla cuardaigh"

msgid ""
"Let's start with a small custom lookup. We will write a custom lookup ``ne`` "
"which works opposite to ``exact``. "
"``Author.objects.filter(name__ne='Jack')`` will translate to the SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Tosaímid le cuardach beag saincheaptha. Scríobhfaimid cuardach saincheaptha "
"``ne`` a oibríonn os coinne ```cruinn ``. Aistreoidh ``Author.Objects.Filter "
"(name__ne='Jack') ``go dtí an SQL:"

msgid ""
"This SQL is backend independent, so we don't need to worry about different "
"databases."
msgstr ""
"Tá an SQL seo neamhspleách ar chúltaca, mar sin ní gá dúinn a bheith buartha "
"faoi bhunachair sonraí éagsúla."

msgid ""
"There are two steps to making this work. Firstly we need to implement the "
"lookup, then we need to tell Django about it::"
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá chéim ann chun an obair seo a dhéanamh. Ar dtús ní mór dúinn an "
"cuardach a chur i bhfeidhm, ansin ní mór dúinn a insint do Django faoi:"

msgid ""
"To register the ``NotEqual`` lookup we will need to call ``register_lookup`` "
"on the field class we want the lookup to be available for. In this case, the "
"lookup makes sense on all ``Field`` subclasses, so we register it with "
"``Field`` directly::"
msgstr ""
"Chun an cuardach ``NoteQual`` a chlárú beidh orainn glaoch ar "
"`register_lookup`` ar an rang réimse a theastaíonn uainn go mbeadh an "
"cuardach ar fáil dó. Sa chás seo, bíonn ciall ag an cuardach ar gach fo-"
"aicme ``Field`, mar sin cláraímid é le ``Field` go díreach:"

msgid "Lookup registration can also be done using a decorator pattern::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir clárú cuardaigh a dhéanamh freisin ag baint úsáide as patrún "
"maisitheora::"

msgid ""
"We can now use ``foo__ne`` for any field ``foo``. You will need to ensure "
"that this registration happens before you try to create any querysets using "
"it. You could place the implementation in a ``models.py`` file, or register "
"the lookup in the ``ready()`` method of an ``AppConfig``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir linn ``foo__ne`` a úsáid anois le haghaidh aon réimse ``foo``. "
"Beidh ort a chinntiú go dtarlaíonn an clárú seo sula ndéanann tú iarracht "
"aon cheisteanna a chruthú ag baint úsáide as. D'fhéadfá an cur i bhfeidhm a "
"chur i gcomhad ``models.py`, nó an cuardach a chlárú sa mhodh ``ready () "
"``de `AppConfig``."

msgid ""
"Taking a closer look at the implementation, the first required attribute is "
"``lookup_name``. This allows the ORM to understand how to interpret "
"``name__ne`` and use ``NotEqual`` to generate the SQL. By convention, these "
"names are always lowercase strings containing only letters, but the only "
"hard requirement is that it must not contain the string ``__``."
msgstr ""
"Ag breathnú níos dlúithe ar an gcur i bhfeidhm, is é `lookup_name`` an chéad "
"tréith riachtanach. Ligeann sé seo don ORM tuiscint a fháil ar conas "
"``name__ne`` a léirmhíniú agus ``NoteQual`` a úsáid chun an SQL a ghiniúint. "
"De réir choinbhinsiúin, is teaghráin bheaga iad na hainmneacha seo i gcónaí "
"nach bhfuil ach litreacha ann, ach is é an t-aon cheanglas crua ná nach "
"gcaithfidh an teaghrán ``__`` a bheith ann."

msgid ""
"We then need to define the ``as_sql`` method. This takes a ``SQLCompiler`` "
"object, called ``compiler``,  and the active database connection. "
"``SQLCompiler`` objects are not documented, but the only thing we need to "
"know about them is that they have a ``compile()`` method which returns a "
"tuple containing an SQL string, and the parameters to be interpolated into "
"that string. In most cases, you don't need to use it directly and can pass "
"it on to ``process_lhs()`` and ``process_rhs()``."
msgstr ""
"Ansin ní mór dúinn an modh ``as_sql`` a shainiú. Tógann sé seo réad "
"``SQLCompiler``, ar a dtugtar ``compiler``, agus an nasc gníomhach bunachar "
"sonraí. Ní dhéantar rudaí `SQLCompiler`` a dhoiciméadú, ach is é an t-aon "
"rud a chaithfimid a bheith ar eolas fúthu ná go bhfuil modh ``compileáil () "
"``acu a thugann tuple ina bhfuil teaghrán SQL, agus na paraiméadair atá le "
"hidirphóladh isteach sa sreang sin. I bhformhór na gcásanna, ní gá duit é a "
"úsáid go díreach agus is féidir leat é a chur ar aghaidh chuig ``process_lhs "
"() ``agus ``process_rhs ()``."

msgid ""
"A ``Lookup`` works against two values, ``lhs`` and ``rhs``, standing for "
"left-hand side and right-hand side. The left-hand side is usually a field "
"reference, but it can be anything implementing the :ref:`query expression "
"API <query-expression>`. The right-hand is the value given by the user. In "
"the example ``Author.objects.filter(name__ne='Jack')``, the left-hand side "
"is a reference to the ``name`` field of the ``Author`` model, and ``'Jack'`` "
"is the right-hand side."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn ``Lookup`` i gcoinne dhá luach, `lhs`` agus ``rhs``, ag seasamh ar "
"thaobh na láimhe clé agus ar dheis. <query-expression>Is tagairt réimse é an "
"taobh na láimhe clé de ghnáth, ach is féidir é a bheith ina rud ar bith a "
"chur i bhfeidhm an:ref: `abairt fiosraithe API `. Is é an lámh dheis an "
"luach a thugann an t-úsáideoir. Sa sampla ``Author.Objects.Filter "
"(name__ne='Jack') ``, is tagairt é an taobh clé don réimse ``ainm`` den "
"tsamhail ``Author ``, agus ``Jack'`` is é an taobh na láimhe deise."

msgid ""
"We call ``process_lhs`` and ``process_rhs`` to convert them into the values "
"we need for SQL using the ``compiler`` object described before. These "
"methods return tuples containing some SQL and the parameters to be "
"interpolated into that SQL, just as we need to return from our ``as_sql`` "
"method. In the above example, ``process_lhs`` returns ``('\"author\"."
"\"name\"', [])`` and ``process_rhs`` returns ``('\"%s\"', ['Jack'])``. In "
"this example there were no parameters for the left hand side, but this would "
"depend on the object we have, so we still need to include them in the "
"parameters we return."
msgstr ""
"Glaoimid ar ``process_lhs`` agus ``process_rhs`` chun iad a thiontú ina "
"luachanna a theastaíonn uainn le haghaidh SQL ag baint úsáide as an réad "
"``compiler`` a thuairiscítear roimhe seo. Tugann na modhanna seo tuples ina "
"bhfuil roinnt SQL agus na paraiméadair atá le hidirphóladh isteach sa SQL "
"sin, díreach mar is gá dúinn filleadh ónár modh `as_sql``. Sa sampla thuas, "
"filleann ``process_lhs`` ``('\"údar”. ainm\"', []) ``agus ``process_rhs`` "
"filleann`` ('\"%s\"', ['Jack']) ``. Sa sampla seo ní raibh aon pharaiméadair "
"ann don taobh clé, ach bheadh sé seo ag brath ar an réad atá againn, mar sin "
"ní mór dúinn iad a áireamh sna paraiméadair a fhilleann muid fós."

msgid ""
"Finally we combine the parts into an SQL expression with ``<>``, and supply "
"all the parameters for the query. We then return a tuple containing the "
"generated SQL string and the parameters."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, déanaimid na codanna a chomhcheangal i abairt SQL le `<>``, "
"agus soláthraímid na paraiméadair go léir don cheist. Ansin cuirimid tuple "
"ar ais ina bhfuil an teaghrán SQL a ghintear agus na paraiméadair."

msgid "A transformer example"
msgstr "Sampla claochladáin"

msgid ""
"The custom lookup above is great, but in some cases you may want to be able "
"to chain lookups together. For example, let's suppose we are building an "
"application where we want to make use of the ``abs()`` operator. We have an "
"``Experiment`` model which records a start value, end value, and the change "
"(start - end). We would like to find all experiments where the change was "
"equal to a certain amount (``Experiment.objects.filter(change__abs=27)``), "
"or where it did not exceed a certain amount "
"(``Experiment.objects.filter(change__abs__lt=27)``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an cuardach saincheaptha thuas iontach, ach i gcásanna áirithe b'fhéidir "
"gur mhaith leat a bheith in ann cuardaigh a shlánú le chéile. Mar shampla, "
"is dóigh linn go bhfuilimid ag tógáil feidhmchlár áit ar mhaith linn úsáid a "
"bhaint as an oibreoir ``abs () ``. Tá samhail ``Turgnamh`` againn a "
"thaifeadann luach tosaigh, luach deiridh, agus an t-athrú (tús - deireadh). "
"Ba mhaith linn gach turgnamh a fháil nuair a bhí an t-athrú cothrom le méid "
"áirithe (`Experiment.Objects.filter (change__abs = 27) ``), nó nuair nár "
"sháraigh sé méid áirithe (``Experiment.Objects.Filter "
"(change__abs__lt=27)``)."

msgid ""
"This example is somewhat contrived, but it nicely demonstrates the range of "
"functionality which is possible in a database backend independent manner, "
"and without duplicating functionality already in Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá an sampla seo dírithe beagán, ach léiríonn sé go deas an raon "
"feidhmiúlachta atá indéanta ar bhealach neamhspleách cúltaca bunachar "
"sonraí, agus gan feidhmiúlacht a dhúbailt cheana féin i Django."

msgid ""
"We will start by writing an ``AbsoluteValue`` transformer. This will use the "
"SQL function ``ABS()`` to transform the value before comparison::"
msgstr ""
"Tosóimid trí chlaochladán ``Absolutevalue`` a scríobh. Úsáidfidh sé seo an "
"fheidhm SQL ``ABS () ``chun an luach a athrú roimh chomparáid:"

msgid "Next, let's register it for ``IntegerField``::"
msgstr "Ansin, déanaimis é a chlárú le haghaidh ``IntegerField``:"

msgid ""
"We can now run the queries we had before. "
"``Experiment.objects.filter(change__abs=27)`` will generate the following "
"SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir linn anois na ceisteanna a bhí againn roimhe seo a rith. Ghinfidh "
"``Experiment.Objects.Filter (change__abs = 27) ``an SQL seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"By using ``Transform`` instead of ``Lookup`` it means we are able to chain "
"further lookups afterward. So "
"``Experiment.objects.filter(change__abs__lt=27)`` will generate the "
"following SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Trí ``Transform`` a úsáid in ionad ``Lookup`` ciallaíonn sé go bhfuilimid in "
"ann cuardaigh breise a shlánú ina dhiaidh sin. Mar sin, ginfidh "
"``Experiment.Objects.filter (change__abs__lt = 27) ``an SQL seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Note that in case there is no other lookup specified, Django interprets "
"``change__abs=27`` as ``change__abs__exact=27``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, i gcás nach bhfuil aon chuardach eile sonraithe ann, "
"léirmhíníonn Django ``change__abs = 27`` mar ``change__abs__exact=27``."

msgid ""
"This also allows the result to be used in ``ORDER BY`` and ``DISTINCT ON`` "
"clauses. For example ``Experiment.objects.order_by('change__abs')`` "
"generates:"
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé seo freisin an toradh a úsáid i gclásail ``ORDER BY`` agus "
"`DISTINCT ON``. Mar shampla ``Experiment.Objects.Order_by ('change__abs') "
"``gineann:"

msgid ""
"And on databases that support distinct on fields (such as PostgreSQL), "
"``Experiment.objects.distinct('change__abs')`` generates:"
msgstr ""
"Agus ar bhunachair sonraí a thacaíonn le réimsí ar leith (mar shampla "
"PostgreSQL), gineann ``Experiment.Objects.Distinct ('change__abs') ``:"

msgid ""
"When looking for which lookups are allowable after the ``Transform`` has "
"been applied, Django uses the ``output_field`` attribute. We didn't need to "
"specify this here as it didn't change, but supposing we were applying "
"``AbsoluteValue`` to some field which represents a more complex type (for "
"example a point relative to an origin, or a complex number) then we may have "
"wanted to specify that the transform returns a ``FloatField`` type for "
"further lookups. This can be done by adding an ``output_field`` attribute to "
"the transform::"
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag lorg cé na cuardaigh atá incheadaithe tar éis an ``Transform` `a "
"chur i bhfeidhm, úsáideann Django an tréith ``output_field`. Ní raibh gá "
"dúinn é seo a shonrú anseo mar níor athraigh sé, ach ag glacadh go raibh "
"“AbsoluteValue” á chur i bhfeidhm ar réimse éigin a léiríonn cineál níos "
"casta (mar shampla pointe i gcoibhneas le bunús, nó uimhir chasta) ansin "
"b'fhéidir gur theastaigh uainn a shonrú go dtugann an claochlú cineál "
"`Floatfield` le haghaidh tuilleadh cuardaigh. Is féidir é seo a dhéanamh trí "
"thréith ``output_field`` a chur leis an gclaochlú:"

msgid ""
"This ensures that further lookups like ``abs__lte`` behave as they would for "
"a ``FloatField``."
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn sé seo go n-iompraíonn cuardaigh breise mar ``abs__lte`` mar a "
"dhéanfaidís do ``Floatfield ``."

msgid "Writing an efficient ``abs__lt`` lookup"
msgstr "Cuardach éifeachtach ``abs__lt`` a scríobh"

msgid ""
"When using the above written ``abs`` lookup, the SQL produced will not use "
"indexes efficiently in some cases. In particular, when we use "
"``change__abs__lt=27``, this is equivalent to ``change__gt=-27`` AND "
"``change__lt=27``. (For the ``lte`` case we could use the SQL ``BETWEEN``)."
msgstr ""
"Agus an cuardach 'abs' scríofa thuas á úsáid agat, ní úsáidfidh an SQL a "
"tháirgtear innéacsanna go héifeachtúil i gcásanna áirithe. Go háirithe, "
"nuair a úsáidimid ``change__abs__lt=27``, tá sé seo comhionann le "
"``change__gt=-27`` AGUS ``change__lt=27``. (Maidir leis an gcás ``lte`` "
"d'fhéadfaimis an SQL ``BETWEEN`` a úsáid)."

msgid ""
"So we would like ``Experiment.objects.filter(change__abs__lt=27)`` to "
"generate the following SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin ba mhaith linn ``Experiment.Objects.filter (change__abs__lt = 27) "
"``an SQL seo a leanas a ghiniúint:"

msgid "The implementation is::"
msgstr "Is é seo a leanas an cur chun feidhme:"

msgid ""
"There are a couple of notable things going on. First, "
"``AbsoluteValueLessThan`` isn't calling ``process_lhs()``. Instead it skips "
"the transformation of the ``lhs`` done by ``AbsoluteValue`` and uses the "
"original ``lhs``. That is, we want to get ``\"experiments\".\"change\"`` not "
"``ABS(\"experiments\".\"change\")``. Referring directly to ``self.lhs.lhs`` "
"is safe as ``AbsoluteValueLessThan`` can be accessed only from the "
"``AbsoluteValue`` lookup, that is the ``lhs`` is always an instance of "
"``AbsoluteValue``."
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla rud suntasach ar siúl. Ar dtús, níl ``Absolutevaluelessthan`` ag "
"glaoch ar ``process_lhs () ``. Ina áit sin scipeann sé claochlú na `lhs`` "
"arna dhéanamh ag ``AbsoluteValue`` agus úsáideann sé an `lhs`` bunaidh. Is é "
"sin, ba mhaith linn “turgnaimh” a fháil.” athraigh “``ní ``ABS "
"(“turgnaimh”.” athrú”) ``. Tá tagairt dhíreach do `self.lhs.lhs`` sábháilte "
"mar ní féidir rochtain a fháil ar ``AbsoluteValuelessthan`` ach ón gcuardach "
"``AbsoluteValue``, is é sin an `lhs`` is sampla de `AbsoluteValue`` i gcónaí."

msgid ""
"Notice also that  as both sides are used multiple times in the query the "
"params need to contain ``lhs_params`` and ``rhs_params`` multiple times."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin toisc go n-úsáidtear an dá thaobh arís agus arís "
"agus arís eile sa cheist go gcaithfidh `lhs_params`` agus `rhs_params`` a "
"bheith sna paramaí arís agus arís eile."

msgid ""
"The final query does the inversion (``27`` to ``-27``) directly in the "
"database. The reason for doing this is that if the ``self.rhs`` is something "
"else than a plain integer value (for example an ``F()`` reference) we can't "
"do the transformations in Python."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an cheist deiridh an t-inbhrú (``27`` go `-27``) go díreach sa "
"bhunachar sonraí. Is é an chúis atá leis seo a dhéanamh ná más rud éigin "
"eile é an ``self.rhs`` seachas luach slámhshláir simplí (mar shampla tagairt "
"``F () `) ní féidir linn na claochlú a dhéanamh i Python."

msgid ""
"In fact, most lookups with ``__abs`` could be implemented as range queries "
"like this, and on most database backends it is likely to be more sensible to "
"do so as you can make use of the indexes. However with PostgreSQL you may "
"want to add an index on ``abs(change)`` which would allow these queries to "
"be very efficient."
msgstr ""
"Déanta na fírinne, d'fhéadfaí an chuid is mó de na cuardaigh le `__abs ``a "
"chur i bhfeidhm mar cheisteanna raon mar seo, agus ar fhormhór na gcúltaca "
"bunachar sonraí is dóichí go mbeidh sé níos ciallmhaire é sin a dhéanamh mar "
"is féidir leat úsáid a bhaint as na hinnéacsanna. Mar sin féin le PostgreSQL "
"b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat innéacs a chur leis ar `abs (athrú) ``a ligfeadh "
"na ceisteanna seo a bheith an-éifeachtach."

msgid "A bilateral transformer example"
msgstr "Sampla claochladáin déthaobh"

msgid ""
"The ``AbsoluteValue`` example we discussed previously is a transformation "
"which applies to the left-hand side of the lookup. There may be some cases "
"where you want the transformation to be applied to both the left-hand side "
"and the right-hand side. For instance, if you want to filter a queryset "
"based on the equality of the left and right-hand side insensitively to some "
"SQL function."
msgstr ""
"Is é an sampla ``AbsoluteValue` a phléamar roimhe seo ná claochlú a "
"bhaineann leis an taobh clé den chuardach. D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh roinnt "
"cásanna ann inar mian leat an claochlú a chur i bhfeidhm ar an taobh clé "
"agus ar an taobh deise araon. Mar shampla, más mian leat tacar fiosrúcháin a "
"scagadh bunaithe ar chomhionannas an taobh clé agus na láimhe deise go "
"neamhíogair do roinnt feidhm SQL."

msgid ""
"Let's examine case-insensitive transformations here. This transformation "
"isn't very useful in practice as Django already comes with a bunch of built-"
"in case-insensitive lookups, but it will be a nice demonstration of "
"bilateral transformations in a database-agnostic way."
msgstr ""
"Déanaimis scrúdú ar chlaochlú cás-neamh-íogair Níl an claochlú seo an-"
"úsáideach go praiticiúil toisc go dtagann dornán cuardaigh cás-neamh-íogair "
"ionsuite le Django cheana féin, ach beidh sé ina léiriú deas ar chlaochlú "
"déthaobhacha ar bhealach agnasach bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"We define an ``UpperCase`` transformer which uses the SQL function "
"``UPPER()`` to transform the values before comparison. We "
"define :attr:`bilateral = True <django.db.models.Transform.bilateral>` to "
"indicate that this transformation should apply to both ``lhs`` and ``rhs``::"
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínímid claochladán ``Uppercase`` a úsáideann an fheidhm SQL ``UPPER () "
"``chun na luachanna a athrú roimh chomparáid. Sainmhínímid: attr: "
"`déthaobhach = Fíor <django.db.models.Transform.bilateral>`chun a léiriú gur "
"chóir go mbeadh feidhm ag an gclaochlú seo le `lhs`` agus `rhs`` araon:"

msgid "Next, let's register it::"
msgstr "Ansin, déanaimis é a chlárú::"

msgid ""
"Now, the queryset ``Author.objects.filter(name__upper=\"doe\")`` will "
"generate a case insensitive query like this:"
msgstr ""
"Anois, ginfidh an tacar ceisteanna `Author.Objects.Filter "
"(name__upper=\"doe”) ``ceist neamh-íogair cás mar seo:"

msgid "Writing alternative implementations for existing lookups"
msgstr "Forfheidhmithe malartacha a scríobh le haghaidh cuardaigh atá ann"

msgid ""
"Sometimes different database vendors require different SQL for the same "
"operation. For this example we will rewrite a custom implementation for "
"MySQL for the NotEqual operator. Instead of ``<>`` we will be using ``!=`` "
"operator. (Note that in reality almost all databases support both, including "
"all the official databases supported by Django)."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta éilíonn díoltóirí bunachar sonraí éagsúla SQL éagsúla don "
"oibríocht chéanna. Mar shampla seo athscríobhfaimid cur i bhfeidhm "
"saincheaptha do MySQL don oibreoir NotEqual. In ionad ``<>`` beimid ag úsáid "
"``!=`` oibreoir. (Tabhair faoi deara i ndáiríre go dtacaíonn beagnach gach "
"bunachar sonraí leis an dá cheann, lena n-áirítear na bunachair shonraí "
"oifigiúla go léir a fhaigheann tacaíocht ó Django)."

msgid ""
"We can change the behavior on a specific backend by creating a subclass of "
"``NotEqual`` with an ``as_mysql`` method::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir linn an t-iompar ar chúltaca ar leith a athrú trí fho-aicme de "
"`NoteQual`` a chruthú le modh `as_mysql``:"

msgid ""
"We can then register it with ``Field``. It takes the place of the original "
"``NotEqual`` class as it has the same ``lookup_name``."
msgstr ""
"Ansin is féidir linn é a chlárú le ``Field`. Tógann sé in áit an aicme "
"bunaidh ``NoteQual`` mar tá an `lookup_name`` céanna aige."

msgid ""
"When compiling a query, Django first looks for ``as_%s % connection.vendor`` "
"methods, and then falls back to ``as_sql``. The vendor names for the in-"
"built backends are ``sqlite``, ``postgresql``, ``oracle`` and ``mysql``."
msgstr ""
"Agus ceist á thiomsú, féachann Django ar dtús modhanna ``as_%s% "
"connection.vendor``, agus ansin titeann sé ar ais chuig ``as_sql``. Is iad "
"na hainmneacha díoltóra do na cúltaca ionsuite ná `sqlite``, `postgresql``, "
"``oracle`` agus ``mysql``."

msgid "How Django determines the lookups and transforms which are used"
msgstr "Conas a chinneann Django na cuardaigh agus na hathshruithe a úsáidtear"

msgid ""
"In some cases you may wish to dynamically change which ``Transform`` or "
"``Lookup`` is returned based on the name passed in, rather than fixing it. "
"As an example, you could have a field which stores coordinates or an "
"arbitrary dimension, and wish to allow a syntax like "
"``.filter(coords__x7=4)`` to return the objects where the 7th coordinate has "
"value 4. In order to do this, you would override ``get_lookup`` with "
"something like::"
msgstr ""
"I gcásanna áirithe b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat a athrú go dinimiciúil cén "
"``Transform`` nó ``Lookup`` ar ais bunaithe ar an ainm a chuirtear isteach, "
"seachas é a shocrú. Mar shampla, d'fhéadfá réimse a bheith agat a "
"stóráilíonn comhordanáidí nó gné treallach, agus ba mhaith leat comhréir mar "
"`.filter (coords__x7=4) `a cheadú chun na rudaí a thabhairt ar ais ina "
"bhfuil luach 4 ag an 7ú comhordú. D'fhonn é seo a dhéanamh, dhéanfá "
"``get_lookup`` a shárú le rud éigin mar:"

msgid ""
"You would then define ``get_coordinate_lookup`` appropriately to return a "
"``Lookup`` subclass which handles the relevant value of ``dimension``."
msgstr ""
"Ansin shainmhíníodh ``get_coordinate_lookup`` go cuí chun fo-aicme "
"``Lookup`` a thabhairt ar ais a dhéileálann luach ábhartha ``tois``."

msgid ""
"There is a similarly named method called ``get_transform()``. "
"``get_lookup()`` should always return a ``Lookup`` subclass, and "
"``get_transform()`` a ``Transform`` subclass. It is important to remember "
"that ``Transform`` objects can be further filtered on, and ``Lookup`` "
"objects cannot."
msgstr ""
"Tá modh ainmnithe mar an gcéanna ar a dtugtar ``get_transformer () ``. Ba "
"chóir go gcuirfeadh ``get_lookup () ``fo-aicme ``Lookup`` a thabhairt ar ais "
"i gcónaí, agus ``get_transformer ()`` fo-aicme ``Transform``. Tá sé "
"tábhachtach a mheabhrú gur féidir rudaí `Transform' a scagadh tuilleadh "
"orthu, agus ní féidir rudaí ``Lookup``."

msgid ""
"When filtering, if there is only one lookup name remaining to be resolved, "
"we will look for a ``Lookup``. If there are multiple names, it will look for "
"a ``Transform``. In the situation where there is only one name and a "
"``Lookup`` is not found, we look for a ``Transform`` and then the ``exact`` "
"lookup on that ``Transform``. All call sequences always end with a "
"``Lookup``. To clarify:"
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag scagadh, mura bhfuil ach ainm cuardaigh amháin fágtha le "
"réiteach, cuirfimid ag lorg ``Lookup``. Má tá ainmneacha iolracha ann, "
"cuardóidh sé ``Transform` `. Sa chás nach bhfuil ach ainm amháin ann agus "
"nach bhfaightear ``Lookup``, cuirimid ag lorg ``Transform`` agus ansin an "
"cuardach ```cruth`` ar an `Transform`` sin. Críochnaíonn gach seicheamh "
"glaonna le ``Lookup`` i gcónaí. Chun soiléiriú:"

msgid ""
"``.filter(myfield__mylookup)`` will call ``myfield.get_lookup('mylookup')``."
msgstr ""
"Glaofar ``.filter (myfield__mylookup) ```myfield.get_lookup ('mylookup')``."

msgid ""
"``.filter(myfield__mytransform__mylookup)`` will call "
"``myfield.get_transform('mytransform')``, and then "
"``mytransform.get_lookup('mylookup')``."
msgstr ""
"Tabharfaidh `.filter (myfield__mytransform__mylookup) ``glaoch ar "
"``myfield.get_transformer ('mytransformer')``, agus ansin "
"``mytransform.get_lookup ('mylookup') ``."

msgid ""
"``.filter(myfield__mytransform)`` will first call "
"``myfield.get_lookup('mytransform')``, which will fail, so it will fall back "
"to calling ``myfield.get_transform('mytransform')`` and then "
"``mytransform.get_lookup('exact')``."
msgstr ""
"Glaofar ``.filter (myfield__mytransformer) ``ar dtús ``myfield.get_lookup "
"('mytransformer')``, a theipeann air, mar sin tithfidh sé ar ais ar "
"``myfield.get_transformer ('mytransformer') ``agus ansin "
"``mytransform.get_lookup ('éacht')``."

msgid "How to create custom ``django-admin`` commands"
msgstr "Conas orduithe saincheaptha ``django-admin ``a chruthú"

msgid ""
"Applications can register their own actions with ``manage.py``. For example, "
"you might want to add a ``manage.py`` action for a Django app that you're "
"distributing. In this document, we will be building a custom ``closepoll`` "
"command for the ``polls`` application from the :doc:`tutorial</intro/"
"tutorial01>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le hiarratais a gcuid gníomhartha féin a chlárú le `manage.py``. "
"Mar shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat gníomh `manage.py` a chur le haghaidh "
"aip Django atá á dháileadh agat. Sa doiciméad seo, beimid ag tógáil ordú "
"saincheaptha ``closepoll`` don iarratas ``polls`` óna:doc: `teagorial@@</"
"intro/tutorial01> `."

msgid ""
"To do this, add a ``management/commands`` directory to the application. "
"Django will register a ``manage.py`` command for each Python module in that "
"directory whose name doesn't begin with an underscore. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Chun seo a dhéanamh, cuir eolaire ``bainistí/orduithe ``leis an "
"bhfeidhmchlár. Cláróidh Django ordú `manage.py`` do gach modúl Python san "
"eolaire sin nach dtosaíonn a ainm le béim. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"In this example, the ``closepoll`` command will be made available to any "
"project that includes the ``polls`` application in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, cuirfear an t-ordú `closepoll`` ar fáil d'aon tionscadal a "
"chuimsíonn an feidhmchlár ``polls`` in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"The ``_private.py`` module will not be available as a management command."
msgstr "Ní bheidh an modúl ``_private.py`` ar fáil mar ordú bainistíochta."

msgid ""
"The ``closepoll.py`` module has only one requirement -- it must define a "
"class ``Command`` that extends :class:`BaseCommand` or one of "
"its :ref:`subclasses<ref-basecommand-subclasses>`."
msgstr ""
"<ref-basecommand-subclasses>Níl ach riachtanas amháin ag an modúl "
"``closepoll.py`` - ní mór dó aicme ``Command`` a shainmhíniú a "
"leathnaí:class: `BaseCommand` nó ceann dá: ref: `fo-aicmí `."

msgid "Standalone scripts"
msgstr "Scripteanna neamhspleácha"

msgid ""
"Custom management commands are especially useful for running standalone "
"scripts or for scripts that are periodically executed from the UNIX crontab "
"or from Windows scheduled tasks control panel."
msgstr ""
"Tá orduithe bainistíochta saincheaptha an-úsáideach chun scripteanna "
"neamhspleácha a rith nó le haghaidh scripteanna a fhorghníomhaítear go "
"tréimhsiúil ó crontab UNIX nó ó phainéal rialaithe tascanna sceidealta "
"Windows."

msgid ""
"To implement the command, edit ``polls/management/commands/closepoll.py`` to "
"look like this::"
msgstr ""
"Chun an t-ordú a chur i bhfeidhm, cuir in eagar `polls/management/commands/"
"closepoll.py`` chun cuma seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"When you are using management commands and wish to provide console output, "
"you should write to ``self.stdout`` and ``self.stderr``, instead of printing "
"to ``stdout`` and ``stderr`` directly. By using these proxies, it becomes "
"much easier to test your custom command. Note also that you don't need to "
"end messages with a newline character, it will be added automatically, "
"unless you specify the ``ending`` parameter::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn orduithe bainistíochta á úsáid agat agus is mian leat aschur "
"consól a sholáthar, ba chóir duit scríobh chuig `self.stdout`` agus "
"``self.stderr``, in ionad priontáil chuig `stdout`` agus `stderr`` go "
"díreach. Trí na seachfhálaí seo a úsáid, bíonn sé i bhfad níos éasca d'ordú "
"saincheaptha a thástáil. Tabhair faoi deara freisin nach gá duit deireadh a "
"chur le teachtaireachtaí le carachtar líne nua, cuirfear leis go "
"huathoibríoch, mura sonraíonn tú an paraiméadar ``deireadh ``:"

msgid ""
"The new custom command can be called using ``python manage.py closepoll "
"<poll_ids>``."
msgstr ""
"<poll_ids>Is féidir an t-ordú saincheaptha nua a ghlaoch ag baint úsáide as "
"``python manage.py closepoll ``."

msgid ""
"The ``handle()`` method takes one or more ``poll_ids`` and sets "
"``poll.opened`` to ``False`` for each one. If the user referenced any "
"nonexistent polls, a :exc:`CommandError` is raised. The ``poll.opened`` "
"attribute does not exist in the :doc:`tutorial</intro/tutorial02>` and was "
"added to ``polls.models.Question`` for this example."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an modh ``handle () ```poll_ids`` amháin nó níos mó agus leagann sé "
"``poll.opened`` go ``False`` do gach ceann amháin. Má thug an t-úsáideoir "
"tagairt do aon vótaíochtaí nach bhfuil ann, ardaítear a:exc: `CommandError`. "
"Níl an tréith ``poll.opened`` ann in:doc: `tutorial` agus cuireadh leis "
"``Polls.Models.Question`` don sampla seo</intro/tutorial02>."

msgid "Accepting optional arguments"
msgstr "Ag glacadh le hargóint"

msgid ""
"The same ``closepoll`` could be easily modified to delete a given poll "
"instead of closing it by accepting additional command line options. These "
"custom options can be added in the :meth:`~BaseCommand.add_arguments` method "
"like this::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfaí an `closepoll`` céanna a mhodhnú go héasca chun vótaíocht ar "
"leith a scriosadh in ionad é a dhúnadh trí ghlacadh le roghanna líne "
"ordaithe breise. Is féidir na roghanna saincheaptha seo a chur leis sa "
"modh:: `~BaseCommand.add_Arguments` mar seo:"

msgid ""
"The option (``delete`` in our example) is available in the options dict "
"parameter of the handle method. See the :py:mod:`argparse` Python "
"documentation for more about ``add_argument`` usage."
msgstr ""
"Tá an rogha (``scrios`` inár sampla) ar fáil i bparaiméadar dict na roghanna "
"den mhodh láimhseála. Féach doiciméadú Python: py:mod: `argparse` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh eolais faoi úsáid ``add_argument ``."

msgid ""
"In addition to being able to add custom command line options, "
"all :doc:`management commands</ref/django-admin>` can accept some default "
"options such as :option:`--verbosity` and :option:`--traceback`."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le bheith in ann roghanna líne ordaithe saincheaptha a chur "
"leis, is féidir le gach: doc: `ordaithe bainistíochta `glacadh le roinnt "
"roghanna réamhshocraithe mar: rogha: `--verbosity`</ref/django-admin> "
"agus:option: `--traceback`."

msgid "Management commands and locales"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta agus áitiúla"

msgid ""
"By default, management commands are executed with the current active locale."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, déantar orduithe bainistíochta a fhorghníomhú leis "
"an locale gníomhach reatha."

msgid ""
"If, for some reason, your custom management command must run without an "
"active locale (for example, to prevent translated content from being "
"inserted into the database), deactivate translations using the "
"``@no_translations`` decorator on your :meth:`~BaseCommand.handle` method::"
msgstr ""
"Más gá, ar chúis éigin, d'ordú bainistíochta saincheaptha a rith gan áit "
"ghníomhach (mar shampla, chun ábhar aistrithe a chosc ó chur isteach sa "
"bhunachar sonraí), díghníomhachtaigh aistriúcháin ag baint úsáide as an "
"maisitheoir ``@no_translations`` ar do mhodh::"

msgid ""
"Since translation deactivation requires access to configured settings, the "
"decorator can't be used for commands that work without configured settings."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go dteastaíonn rochtain ar shocruithe cumraithe chun aistriúchán a "
"dhíghníomhachtú, ní féidir an maisitheoir a úsáid le haghaidh orduithe a "
"oibríonn gan socruithe cumraithe."

msgid "Testing"
msgstr "Tástáil"

msgid ""
"Information on how to test custom management commands can be found in "
"the :ref:`testing docs <topics-testing-management-commands>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-testing-management-commands>Is féidir faisnéis faoi conas orduithe "
"bainistíochta saincheaptha a thástáil in:ref: `testing docs `."

msgid "Overriding commands"
msgstr "Orduithe suntasacha"

msgid ""
"Django registers the built-in commands and then searches for commands "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` in reverse. During the search, if a command "
"name duplicates an already registered command, the newly discovered command "
"overrides the first."
msgstr ""
"Cláraíonn Django na horduithe ionsuite agus ansin déanann sé cuardach ar "
"orduithe in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` ar ais. Le linn an chuardaigh, má "
"dhúbailíonn ainm ordaithe ordú cláraithe cheana féin, cuireann an t-ordú nua-"
"aimsithe ar an gcéad cheann."

msgid ""
"In other words, to override a command, the new command must have the same "
"name and its app must be before the overridden command's app "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""
"Is é sin le rá, chun ordú a shárú, caithfidh an t-ainm céanna a bheith ag an "
"ordú nua agus caithfidh a aip a bheith roimh aip an ordaithe athsháraithe "
"in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"Management commands from third-party apps that have been unintentionally "
"overridden can be made available under a new name by creating a new command "
"in one of your project's apps (ordered before the third-party app "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`) which imports the ``Command`` of the "
"overridden command."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir orduithe bainistíochta ó aipeanna tríú páirtí a cuireadh "
"athshealbhú gan aon ghnó a chur ar fáil faoi ainm nua trí ordú nua a chruthú "
"i gceann de na feidhmchláir do thionscadail (ordaithe roimh an aip tríú "
"páirtí in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`) a allmhairíonn ``Ordú ``den ordú "
"sáraithe."

msgid "Command objects"
msgstr "Rudaí ordaithe"

msgid "The base class from which all management commands ultimately derive."
msgstr "An bunaicme as a dtagann gach ordú bainistíochta sa deireadh."

msgid ""
"Use this class if you want access to all of the mechanisms which parse the "
"command-line arguments and work out what code to call in response; if you "
"don't need to change any of that behavior, consider using one of "
"its :ref:`subclasses<ref-basecommand-subclasses>`."
msgstr ""
"<ref-basecommand-subclasses>Úsáid an rang seo más mian leat rochtain a fháil "
"ar na meicníochtaí go léir a pháirsíonn na hargóintí líne ordaithe agus a "
"oibríonn amach cén cód atá le glaoch mar fhreagra; mura gá duit aon cheann "
"den iompar sin a athrú, smaoinigh ar cheann díobh a úsáid: ref: `fo-aicmí `."

msgid ""
"Subclassing the :class:`BaseCommand` class requires that you implement "
"the :meth:`~BaseCommand.handle` method."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn fo-aicmiú an ranga:class: `BaseCommand` go gcuirfidh tú an modh: "
"`~BaseCommand.Handle` i bhfeidhm."

msgid "Attributes"
msgstr "Tréithe"

msgid ""
"All attributes can be set in your derived class and can be used "
"in :class:`BaseCommand`’s :ref:`subclasses<ref-basecommand-subclasses>`."
msgstr ""
"<ref-basecommand-subclasses>Is féidir na tréithe go léir a shocrú i do rang "
"díorthaithe agus is féidir iad a úsáid in:class: `BaseCommand`:ref: "
"`subclass`."

msgid ""
"A short description of the command, which will be printed in the help "
"message when the user runs the command ``python manage.py help <command>``."
msgstr ""
"<command>Cur síos gairid ar an ordú, a phriontálfar sa teachtaireacht "
"chabhrach nuair a ritheann an t-úsáideoir an t-ordú ``python manage.py help "
"``."

msgid ""
"If your command defines mandatory positional arguments, you can customize "
"the message error returned in the case of missing arguments. The default is "
"output by :py:mod:`argparse` (\"too few arguments\")."
msgstr ""
"Má shainmhíníonn d'ordú argóintí seasaimh éigeantacha, is féidir leat an "
"earráid teachtaireachta a thug ar ais a shaincheapadh i gcás argóint Is é an "
"réamhshocrú aschur ag:py:mod: `argparse` (“ró-bheag argóintí”)."

msgid ""
"A boolean indicating whether the command outputs SQL statements; if "
"``True``, the output will automatically be wrapped with ``BEGIN;`` and "
"``COMMIT;``. Default value is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a thugann le fios an n-aschuireann an t-ordú ráitis SQL; má tá "
"``True``, filteofar an t-aschur go huathoibríoch le ``BEGIN; ``agus "
"``COMMIT;``. Is é luach réamhshocraithe ``False``."

msgid ""
"A boolean; if ``True``, the command prints a warning if the set of "
"migrations on disk don't match the migrations in the database. A warning "
"doesn't prevent the command from executing. Default value is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Boolean; má tá ``True``, priontáil an t-ordú rabhadh mura n-oireann an tacar "
"imirce ar an diosca leis na himirce sa bhunachar sonraí. Ní chuireann "
"rabhadh cosc ar an ordú a fhorghníomhú. Is é luach réamhshocraithe ``False``."

msgid ""
"A list or tuple of tags, e.g. ``[Tags.staticfiles, Tags.models]``. System "
"checks :ref:`registered in the chosen tags <registering-labeling-checks>` "
"will be checked for errors prior to executing the command. The value "
"``'__all__'`` can be used to specify that all system checks should be "
"performed. Default value is ``'__all__'``."
msgstr ""
"Liosta nó cúpla clibeanna, m.sh. ``[Tags.staticFiles, tags.Models]``. "
"Seiceálfar seiceálacha córas:ref: `cláraithe sna clibeanna roghnaithe "
"<registering-labeling-checks>`le haghaidh earráidí sula ndéantar an t-ordú a "
"fhorghníomhú. Is féidir an luach ``'__all__'`` a úsáid chun a shonrú gur "
"chóir gach seiceáil chórais a dhéanamh. Is é luach réamhshocraithe "
"``'__all__'``."

msgid ""
"An instance attribute that helps create colored output when writing to "
"``stdout`` or ``stderr``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tréith sampla a chuidíonn le aschur daite a chruthú agus tú ag scríobh chuig "
"``stdout`` nó ``stderr``. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"See :ref:`syntax-coloring` to learn how to modify the color palette and to "
"see the available styles (use uppercased versions of the \"roles\" described "
"in that section)."
msgstr ""
"Féach: tagairt: `syntax-coloring` chun foghlaim conas an pailéad dathanna a "
"mhodhnú agus na stíleanna atá ar fáil a fheiceáil (bain úsáid as leaganacha "
"uachtaracha de na “róil” a thuairiscítear sa chuid sin)."

msgid ""
"If you pass the :option:`--no-color` option when running your command, all "
"``self.style()`` calls will return the original string uncolored."
msgstr ""
"Má théann tú ar an rogha:: - no-color` agus tú ag rith d'ordú, cuirfidh gach "
"glao `self.style () `ar ais an sreang bunaidh gan daite."

msgid ""
"The default command options to suppress in the help output. This should be a "
"set of option names (e.g. ``'--verbosity'``). The default values for the "
"suppressed options are still passed."
msgstr ""
"Na roghanna ordaithe réamhshocraithe chun cosc a chur san aschur cabhrach. "
"Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo ina shraith d'ainmneacha roghanna (m.sh. ```- "
"verbosity```). Tá na luachanna réamhshocraithe do na roghanna faoi chosc "
"ritheanta fós."

msgid "Methods"
msgstr "Modhanna"

msgid ""
":class:`BaseCommand` has a few methods that can be overridden but only "
"the :meth:`~BaseCommand.handle` method must be implemented."
msgstr ""
":class: Tá cúpla modh ag `BaseCommand` is féidir a shárú ach ní gcaithfear "
"ach an modh:meth: `~BaseCommand.handle` a chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid "Implementing a constructor in a subclass"
msgstr "Tógálaí a chur i bhfeidhm i bhfo-aicme"

msgid ""
"If you implement ``__init__`` in your subclass of :class:`BaseCommand`, you "
"must call :class:`BaseCommand`’s ``__init__``::"
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann tú ``__init__`` i do fho-aicme de:class: `BaseCommand`, ní mór "
"duit glao:class: `BaseCommand` ``__init__``:"

msgid ""
"Returns a ``CommandParser`` instance, which is "
"an :class:`~argparse.ArgumentParser` subclass with a few customizations for "
"Django."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé sampla ``CommandParser``, arb ion:class: "
"`~ArgParse.ArgumentParser` fo-aicme le cúpla saincheapadh do Django."

msgid ""
"You can customize the instance by overriding this method and calling "
"``super()`` with ``kwargs`` of :class:`~argparse.ArgumentParser` parameters."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an sampla a shaincheapadh tríd an modh seo a shárú agus "
"glaoch ar ``super () ```` le paraiméadair ``kwargs ``o:class: "
"`~ArgParse.ArgumentParser`."

msgid ""
"Entry point to add parser arguments to handle command line arguments passed "
"to the command. Custom commands should override this method to add both "
"positional and optional arguments accepted by the command. Calling "
"``super()`` is not needed when directly subclassing ``BaseCommand``."
msgstr ""
"Pointe iontrála chun argóintí parser a chur chun argóintí líne ordaithe a "
"chuirtear chuig an ordú a láimhseáil Ba cheart d'orduithe saincheaptha an "
"modh seo a shárú chun argóintí suímh agus roghnacha a ghlacann an t-ordú "
"leis a chur leis Ní gá glaoch ar ``super () ``nuair a dhéantar "
"`BaseCommand`` a fho-aicmiú go díreach."

msgid ""
"Returns the Django version, which should be correct for all built-in Django "
"commands. User-supplied commands can override this method to return their "
"own version."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an leagan Django, ar chóir go mbeadh sé ceart do gach ordú "
"Django ionsuite. Is féidir le horduithe a sholáthraíonn an úsáideoir an modh "
"seo a shárú chun a leagan féin ar ais."

msgid ""
"Tries to execute this command, performing system checks if needed (as "
"controlled by the :attr:`requires_system_checks` attribute). If the command "
"raises a :exc:`CommandError`, it's intercepted and printed to ``stderr``."
msgstr ""
"Déanann iarracht an t-ordú seo a fhorghníomhú, ag déanamh seiceálacha córais "
"más gá (mar atá á rialú ag an tréith: attr: `requires_system_checks`). Má "
"ardaíonn an t-ordú a:exc: `CommandError`, déantar é a idirghabháil agus a "
"phriontáil chuig ``stderr``."

msgid "Calling a management command in your code"
msgstr "Glaoch ar ordú bainistíochta i do chód"

msgid ""
"``execute()`` should not be called directly from your code to execute a "
"command. Use :func:`~django.core.management.call_command` instead."
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir `execute () ``a ghlaoch go díreach ó do chód chun ordú a "
"fhorghníomhú. Úsáid: func: `~django.core.management.call_command` ina ionad."

msgid "The actual logic of the command. Subclasses must implement this method."
msgstr ""
"An loighic iarbhír an ordaithe. Caithfidh fo-aicmí an modh seo a chur i "
"bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"It may return a string which will be printed to ``stdout`` (wrapped by "
"``BEGIN;`` and ``COMMIT;`` if :attr:`output_transaction` is ``True``)."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh sé teaghrán a chur ar ais a phriontáilfear chuig `stdout`` (fillte "
"le ``BEGIN; ``agus ``COMMIT;`` más: attr: `output_transaction` ```True``)."

msgid ""
"Uses the system check framework to inspect the entire Django project for "
"potential problems. Serious problems are raised as a :exc:`CommandError`; "
"warnings are output to ``stderr``; minor notifications are output to "
"``stdout``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé creat seiceála an chórais chun an tionscadal iomlán Django a "
"iniúchadh le haghaidh fadhbanna a Ardaítear fadhbanna tromchúiseacha mar "
"a:exc: `Commanderror`; aschur rabhaidh chuig `stderr``; aschuirtear "
"mionfhógraí chuig `stdout``."

msgid ""
"If ``app_configs`` and ``tags`` are both ``None``, all system checks are "
"performed except deployment and database related checks. ``tags`` can be a "
"list of check tags, like ``compatibility`` or ``models``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ```app_configs`` agus `tags`` araon ```None ``, déantar gach seiceáil "
"chórais seachas seiceálacha imscartha agus seiceálacha a bhaineann le "
"bunachar sonraí. Is féidir le `tags`` a bheith ina liosta clibeanna "
"seiceála, cosúil le ``comhoiriúnacht ``nó `samhlacha``."

msgid ""
"You can pass ``include_deployment_checks=True`` to also perform deployment "
"checks, and list of database aliases in the ``databases`` to run database "
"related checks against them."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``include_deployment_checks=true`` a rith chun seiceálacha "
"imscartha a dhéanamh freisin, agus liosta d'ainmneacha bunachar sonraí sna "
"`databases`` chun seiceálacha a bhaineann le bunachar sonraí a reáchtáil ina "
"gcoinne."

msgid ""
"Supplies kwargs for the call to :meth:`check`, including transforming the "
"value of :attr:`requires_system_checks` to the ``tag`` kwarg."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Override this method to change the values supplied to :meth:`check`. For "
"example, to opt into database related checks you can override "
"``get_check_kwargs()`` as follows::"
msgstr ""

msgid "``BaseCommand`` subclasses"
msgstr "Fo-aicmí ``BaseCommand``"

msgid ""
"A management command which takes one or more installed application labels as "
"arguments, and does something with each of them."
msgstr ""
"Ordú bainistíochta a thógann lipéad feidhmchláir suiteáilte amháin nó níos "
"mó mar argóintí, agus a dhéanann rud éigin le gach ceann acu."

msgid ""
"Rather than implementing :meth:`~BaseCommand.handle`, subclasses must "
"implement :meth:`~AppCommand.handle_app_config`, which will be called once "
"for each application."
msgstr ""
"Seachas: meth: `~BaseCommand.handle` a chur i bhfeidhm, ní mór do fho-"
"aicmiúint:meth: `~appCommand.handle_app_config` a chur i bhfeidhm, a "
"ghlaofar uair amháin do gach feidhmchlár."

msgid ""
"Perform the command's actions for ``app_config``, which will be "
"an :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` instance corresponding to an application "
"label given on the command line."
msgstr ""
"Déan gníomhartha an ordaithe le haghaidh ``app_config``, a bheidh an:class: "
"`~django.apps.appconfig` sampla a fhreagraíonn do lipéad feidhmchláir a "
"thugtar ar an líne ordaithe."

msgid ""
"A management command which takes one or more arbitrary arguments (labels) on "
"the command line, and does something with each of them."
msgstr ""
"Ordú bainistíochta a thógann argóint treallach amháin nó níos mó (lipéid) ar "
"an líne ordaithe, agus a dhéanann rud éigin le gach ceann acu."

msgid ""
"Rather than implementing :meth:`~BaseCommand.handle`, subclasses must "
"implement :meth:`~LabelCommand.handle_label`, which will be called once for "
"each label."
msgstr ""
"Seachas: meth: `~BaseCommand.Handle` a chur i bhfeidhm, ní mór do fho-"
"aicmi:meth: `~labelCommand.handle_label` a chur i bhfeidhm, a ghlaofar uair "
"amháin do gach lipéad."

msgid ""
"A string describing the arbitrary arguments passed to the command. The "
"string is used in the usage text and error messages of the command. Defaults "
"to ``'label'``."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a chuireann síos ar na hargóintí treallacha a chuirtear chuig an ordú "
"Úsáidtear an teaghrán i dtéacs úsáide agus teachtaireachtaí earráide an "
"ordaithe. Réamhshocraithe go ```lipéad``."

msgid ""
"Perform the command's actions for ``label``, which will be the string as "
"given on the command line."
msgstr ""
"Déan gníomhartha an ordaithe le haghaidh `lipéad``, arb é an teaghrán mar a "
"thugtar ar an líne ordaithe."

msgid "Command exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí ordaithe"

msgid ""
"Exception class indicating a problem while executing a management command."
msgstr ""
"Rang eisceachta a léiríonn fadhb agus ordú bainistíochta á fhorghníomhú."

msgid ""
"If this exception is raised during the execution of a management command "
"from a command line console, it will be caught and turned into a nicely-"
"printed error message to the appropriate output stream (i.e., ``stderr``); "
"as a result, raising this exception (with a sensible description of the "
"error) is the preferred way to indicate that something has gone wrong in the "
"execution of a command. It accepts the optional ``returncode`` argument to "
"customize the exit status for the management command to exit with, "
"using :func:`sys.exit`."
msgstr ""
"Má ardaítear an eisceacht seo le linn ordú bainistíochta a fhorghníomhú ó "
"chonsól líne ordaithe, gabhfar é agus déanfar é teachtaireacht earráide "
"priontáilte go deas chuig an sruth aschuir chuí (ie, `stderr ``); mar "
"thoradh air sin, is é an eisceacht seo a ardú (le cur síos ciallmhar ar an "
"earráid) an bealach is fearr chun a léiriú go bhfuil rud éigin mícheart ag "
"forghníomhú ordaithe. Glacann sé leis an argóint roghnach ``returncode "
"``chun an stádas imeachta a shaincheapadh don ordú bainistíochta imeacht "
"leis, ag baint úsáide as: func: `sys.exit`."

msgid ""
"If a management command is called from code "
"through :func:`~django.core.management.call_command`, it's up to you to "
"catch the exception when needed."
msgstr ""
"Má ghlaofar ordú bainistíochta ón gcód trí:func: "
"`~django.core.management.call_command`, is fútsa atá sé an eisceacht a "
"ghabháil nuair is gá."

msgid "How to create custom model fields"
msgstr "Conas réimsí samhail saincheaptha a chruthú"

msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Réamhrá"

msgid ""
"The :doc:`model reference </topics/db/models>` documentation explains how to "
"use Django's standard field classes "
"-- :class:`~django.db.models.CharField`, :class:`~django.db.models.DateField`, "
"etc. For many purposes, those classes are all you'll need. Sometimes, "
"though, the Django version won't meet your precise requirements, or you'll "
"want to use a field that is entirely different from those shipped with "
"Django."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad:doc: `tagairt samhail` </topics/db/models> conas "
"ranganna réimse caighdeánacha Django a úsáid --:class: "
"`~django.db.models.charfield`, :class: `~django.db.models.datefield`, srl "
"Chun go leor críocha, is iad na ranganna sin gach rud a theastaíonn uait. "
"Uaireanta, áfach, ní chomhlíonfaidh an leagan Django do riachtanais "
"bheachta, nó beidh tú ag iarraidh réimse a úsáid atá go hiomlán difriúil ó "
"na cinn a sheoltar le Django."

msgid ""
"Django's built-in field types don't cover every possible database column "
"type -- only the common types, such as ``VARCHAR`` and ``INTEGER``. For more "
"obscure column types, such as geographic polygons or even user-created types "
"such as `PostgreSQL custom types`_, you can define your own Django ``Field`` "
"subclasses."
msgstr ""
"Ní chlúdaíonn cineálacha réimse ionsuite Django gach cineál colún bunachar "
"sonraí féideartha - ach na cineálacha coitianta, mar shampla ``VARCHAR`` "
"agus ``INTEGER``. Le haghaidh cineálacha colún níos doiléire, mar shampla "
"polagóin gheografacha nó fiú cineálacha cruthaithe ag úsáideoir mar "
"`cineálacha saincheaptha PostgreSQL `_, is féidir leat do fho-aicmí "
"``Field`` Django féin a shainiú."

msgid ""
"Alternatively, you may have a complex Python object that can somehow be "
"serialized to fit into a standard database column type. This is another case "
"where a ``Field`` subclass will help you use your object with your models."
msgstr ""
"De rogha air sin, b'fhéidir go bhfuil réad casta Python agat is féidir a "
"shraitheadh ar bhealach éigin chun oiriúnú i gcineál colún bunachar sonraí "
"caighdeán Is cás eile é seo ina gcabhróidh fo-aicme ``Field` leat do réad a "
"úsáid le do mhúnlaí."

msgid "Our example object"
msgstr "Ár réad samplach"

msgid ""
"Creating custom fields requires a bit of attention to detail. To make things "
"easier to follow, we'll use a consistent example throughout this document: "
"wrapping a Python object representing the deal of cards in a hand of "
"Bridge_. Don't worry, you don't have to know how to play Bridge to follow "
"this example. You only need to know that 52 cards are dealt out equally to "
"four players, who are traditionally called *north*, *east*, *south* and "
"*west*.  Our class looks something like this::"
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn beagán aird ar mhionsonraí réimsí saincheaptha a chruthú. Chun rudaí "
"a dhéanamh níos éasca a leanúint, úsáidfimid sampla comhsheasmhach ar fud an "
"doiciméad seo: timfhilleadh réad Python a léiríonn déileáil na gcártaí i "
"lámh Bridge_. Ná bíodh imní ort, ní gá go mbeadh a fhios agat conas "
"Droichead a imirt chun an sampla seo a leanúint. Ní gá go mbeadh a fhios "
"agat ach go ndéileálfar 52 cárta amach go cothrom le ceithre imreoir, ar a "
"dtugtar go traidisiúnta *thuaidh*, *thoir*, *theas* agus *iarth* orthu. "
"Breathnaíonn ár rang rud éigin mar seo:"

msgid ""
"This is an ordinary Python class, with nothing Django-specific about it. "
"We'd like to be able to do things like this in our models (we assume the "
"``hand`` attribute on the model is an instance of ``Hand``)::"
msgstr ""
"Is gnáth-rang Python é seo, gan aon rud Django-sonrach faoi. Ba mhaith linn "
"a bheith in ann rudaí mar seo a dhéanamh inár samhlacha (glacaimid leis gur "
"sampla de ``Hand`` é an tréith `láimh` ar an tsamhail):"

msgid ""
"We assign to and retrieve from the ``hand`` attribute in our model just like "
"any other Python class. The trick is to tell Django how to handle saving and "
"loading such an object."
msgstr ""
"Sannaímid agus aisghabháil uaidh an tréith ``hand`` inár samhail díreach "
"cosúil le haon rang Python eile. Is é an cleas ná insint le Django conas rud "
"den sórt sin a shábháil agus a luchtú a láimhseáil."

msgid ""
"In order to use the ``Hand`` class in our models, we **do not** have to "
"change this class at all. This is ideal, because it means you can easily "
"write model support for existing classes where you cannot change the source "
"code."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn an rang ``Hand`` a úsáid inár samhlacha, ní gá dúinn** an rang seo a "
"athrú ar chor ar bith. Tá sé seo oiriúnach, mar ciallaíonn sé gur féidir "
"leat tacaíocht mhúnla a scríobh go héasca do ranganna atá ann cheana nach "
"féidir leat an cód foinse a athrú."

msgid ""
"You might only be wanting to take advantage of custom database column types "
"and deal with the data as standard Python types in your models; strings, or "
"floats, for example. This case is similar to our ``Hand`` example and we'll "
"note any differences as we go along."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir nach mbeadh tú ag iarraidh leas a bhaint as cineálacha colún "
"bunachar sonraí saincheaptha agus déileáil leis na sonraí mar chineálacha "
"caighdeánacha Python i do mhúnlaí; teaghráin, nó snámha, mar shampla. Tá an "
"cás seo cosúil lenár sampla ``Hand`` agus tabharfaimid faoi deara aon "
"difríochtaí agus muid ag dul ar aghaidh."

msgid "Background theory"
msgstr "Teoiric chúlra"

msgid "Database storage"
msgstr "Stóráil bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Let's start with model fields. If you break it down, a model field provides "
"a way to take a normal Python object -- string, boolean, ``datetime``, or "
"something more complex like ``Hand`` -- and convert it to and from a format "
"that is useful when dealing with the database. (Such a format is also useful "
"for serialization, but as we'll see later, that is easier once you have the "
"database side under control)."
msgstr ""
"Tosaímid le réimsí samhail. Má bhriseann tú síos é, soláthraíonn réimse "
"samhail bealach chun gnáthrud Python a thógáil - string, boolean, "
"`datetime``, nó rud éigin níos casta cosúil le `Hand`` - agus é a thiontú go "
"formáid atá úsáideach agus tú ag déileáil leis an mbunachar sonraí. (Tá "
"formáid den sórt sin úsáideach freisin le haghaidh sraitheadh, ach mar a "
"fheicfimid níos déanaí, tá sé sin níos éasca nuair a bheidh an taobh "
"bunachar sonraí faoi smacht agat)."

msgid ""
"Fields in a model must somehow be converted to fit into an existing database "
"column type. Different databases provide different sets of valid column "
"types, but the rule is still the same: those are the only types you have to "
"work with. Anything you want to store in the database must fit into one of "
"those types."
msgstr ""
"Caithfear réimsí i samhail a thiontú ar bhealach éigin chun oiriúnú i "
"gcineál colún bunachar sonraí atá ann Soláthraíonn bunachair sonraí éagsúla "
"tacair éagsúla de chineálacha bailí colún, ach tá an riail fós mar an "
"gcéanna: is iad sin na cineálacha amháin a chaithfidh tú oibriú leo. "
"Caithfidh aon rud is mian leat a stóráil sa bhunachar sonraí a bheith "
"oiriúnach i gceann de na cineálacha sin."

msgid ""
"Normally, you're either writing a Django field to match a particular "
"database column type, or you will need a way to convert your data to, say, a "
"string."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, tá réimse Django á scríobh agat chun cineál colún bunachar sonraí "
"áirithe a mheaitseáil, nó beidh bealach ag teastáil uait chun do chuid "
"sonraí a thiontú go, abair, sreang."

msgid ""
"For our ``Hand`` example, we could convert the card data to a string of 104 "
"characters by concatenating all the cards together in a predetermined order "
"-- say, all the *north* cards first, then the *east*, *south* and *west* "
"cards. So ``Hand`` objects can be saved to text or character columns in the "
"database."
msgstr ""
"Maidir lenár sampla ``Hand``, d'fhéadfaimis sonraí na gcárta a thiontú go "
"sreang de 104 carachtar trí na cártaí go léir a chomhcheangal le chéile in "
"ord réamhshocraithe - abair, na cártaí*thuaidh* go léir ar dtús, ansin na "
"cártaí*thoir*, *theas* agus *iarth*. Mar sin is féidir rudaí ``Hand`` a "
"shábháil i gcolúin téacs nó carachtair sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid "What does a field class do?"
msgstr "Cad a dhéanann rang allamuigh?"

msgid ""
"All of Django's fields (and when we say *fields* in this document, we always "
"mean model fields and not :doc:`form fields </ref/forms/fields>`) are "
"subclasses of :class:`django.db.models.Field`. Most of the information that "
"Django records about a field is common to all fields -- name, help text, "
"uniqueness and so forth. Storing all that information is handled by "
"``Field``. We'll get into the precise details of what ``Field`` can do later "
"on; for now, suffice it to say that everything descends from ``Field`` and "
"then customizes key pieces of the class behavior."
msgstr ""
"Is fo-aicmí: `Django.db.Models.Field` iad réimsí uile Django (agus nuair a "
"deirimid *réimsí * sa doiciméad seo, ciallaíonn muid i gcónaí réimsí "
"samhlacha agus ní: doc: `réimsí foirme`). </ref/forms/fields> Tá an chuid is "
"mó den fhaisnéis a thaifeadann Django faoi réimse coitianta do gach réimse - "
"ainm, téacs cabhrach, uathúlacht agus mar sin de. Láimhseálann ``Field` an "
"fhaisnéis sin go léir a stóráil. Téimid isteach sna sonraí beachta faoi na "
"rudaí is féidir le ``Field` a dhéanamh níos déanaí; go dtí seo, is leor a rá "
"go dtagann gach rud as ``Field`` agus ansin saincheapann sé príomhphíosaí "
"d'iompar an ranga."

msgid ""
"It's important to realize that a Django field class is not what is stored in "
"your model attributes. The model attributes contain normal Python objects. "
"The field classes you define in a model are actually stored in the ``Meta`` "
"class when the model class is created (the precise details of how this is "
"done are unimportant here). This is because the field classes aren't "
"necessary when you're just creating and modifying attributes. Instead, they "
"provide the machinery for converting between the attribute value and what is "
"stored in the database or sent to the :doc:`serializer </topics/"
"serialization>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach a thuiscint nach é rang réimse Django an rud a stóráiltear "
"i do thréithe samhail. Tá gnáth-rudaí Python sna tréithe samhail. "
"Stóráiltear na ranganna allamuigh a shainmhíníonn tú i samhail i ndáiríre sa "
"rang ``Meta` nuair a chruthaítear an rang samhail (níl na sonraí beachta "
"faoi conas a dhéantar é seo gan tábhacht anseo). Tá sé seo toisc nach bhfuil "
"na ranganna allamuigh riachtanach nuair nach bhfuil tú ach tréithe a chruthú "
"agus a mhodhnú. Ina áit sin, soláthraíonn siad an t-innealra chun tiontú "
"idir luach na tréithe agus an méid a stóráiltear sa bhunachar sonraí nó a "
"sheoltar chuig:doc: </topics/serialization> `serializer`."

msgid ""
"Keep this in mind when creating your own custom fields. The Django ``Field`` "
"subclass you write provides the machinery for converting between your Python "
"instances and the database/serializer values in various ways (there are "
"differences between storing a value and using a value for lookups, for "
"example). If this sounds a bit tricky, don't worry -- it will become clearer "
"in the examples below. Just remember that you will often end up creating two "
"classes when you want a custom field:"
msgstr ""
"Coinnigh é seo i gcuimhne agus tú ag cruthú do réimsí saincheaptha féin. "
"Soláthraíonn fo-aicme “Field” Django a scríobhann tú an t-innealra chun "
"tiontú idir do chásanna Python agus na luachanna bunachar sonraí/serializer "
"ar bhealaí éagsúla (tá difríochtaí idir luach a stóráil agus luach a úsáid "
"le haghaidh cuardaigh, mar shampla). Má tá sé seo rud beag deacair, ná bíodh "
"imní ort - beidh sé níos soiléire sna samplaí thíos. Cuimhnigh go ndéanfaidh "
"tú dhá rang a chruthú go minic nuair a theastaíonn réimse saincheaptha uait:"

msgid ""
"The first class is the Python object that your users will manipulate. They "
"will assign it to the model attribute, they will read from it for displaying "
"purposes, things like that. This is the ``Hand`` class in our example."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad rang an réad Python a ionramhfaidh d'úsáideoirí. Sannóidh siad "
"é don tréith samhail, léifidh siad uaidh chun críocha a thaispeáint, rudaí "
"mar sin. Seo an rang ``Hand`` inár sampla."

msgid ""
"The second class is the ``Field`` subclass. This is the class that knows how "
"to convert your first class back and forth between its permanent storage "
"form and the Python form."
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara rang an fo-aicme ``Field`. Is é seo an rang a bhfuil a fhios "
"aige conas do chéad rang a thiontú anall agus anall idir a fhoirm stórála "
"buan agus an fhoirm Python."

msgid "Writing a field subclass"
msgstr "Fo-aicme réimse a scríobh"

msgid ""
"When planning your :class:`~django.db.models.Field` subclass, first give "
"some thought to which existing :class:`~django.db.models.Field` class your "
"new field is most similar to. Can you subclass an existing Django field and "
"save yourself some work? If not, you should subclass "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.Field` class, from which everything is "
"descended."
msgstr ""
"Agus do fho-rang: Class: `~Django.db.Models.Field` á phleanáil agat, "
"smaoineamh ar dtús cén aicme: `~django.db.models.field` atá ar do réimse nua "
"is cosúil leis. An féidir leat réimse Django atá ann cheana a fho-aicmiú "
"agus roinnt oibre a shábháil duit féin? Mura bhfuil, ba chóir duit an "
"rang:class: `~Django.db.Models.Field` a fho-aicmiú, as a bhfuil gach rud "
"síos."

msgid ""
"Initializing your new field is a matter of separating out any arguments that "
"are specific to your case from the common arguments and passing the latter "
"to the ``__init__()`` method of :class:`~django.db.models.Field` (or your "
"parent class)."
msgstr ""
"Is ábhar do réimse nua a thionscnamh ná aon argóintí atá sonrach do chás a "
"scaradh ó na hargóintí coitianta agus an dara ceann a chur chuig an modh "
"``__init__ () ``de:class: `~django.db.Models.field` (nó do rang "
"tuismitheora)."

msgid ""
"In our example, we'll call our field ``HandField``. (It's a good idea to "
"call your :class:`~django.db.models.Field` subclass ``<Something>Field``, so "
"it's easily identifiable as a :class:`~django.db.models.Field` subclass.) It "
"doesn't behave like any existing field, so we'll subclass directly "
"from :class:`~django.db.models.Field`::"
msgstr ""
"Inár sampla, glaoimid ar ár réimse ``Handfield`. <Something>(Is smaoineamh "
"maith é glaoch ar do: class: `~django.db.models.field` fo-aicme ``Field`, "
"mar sin is féidir é a aithint go héasca mar a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Field` fo-aicme.) Ní iompraíonn sé cosúil le haon réimse "
"atá ann cheana, mar sin déanfaimid fo-aicme go díreach ó:class: "
"`~django.db.models.field`::"

msgid ""
"Our ``HandField`` accepts most of the standard field options (see the list "
"below), but we ensure it has a fixed length, since it only needs to hold 52 "
"card values plus their suits; 104 characters in total."
msgstr ""
"Glacann ár “Handfield” leis an gcuid is mó de na roghanna caighdeánacha "
"réimse (féach an liosta thíos), ach cinntímid go bhfuil fad seasta aige, ós "
"rud é nach gá dó ach 52 luach cárta móide a gcuid culaith a shealbhú; 104 "
"carachtar san iomlán."

msgid ""
"Many of Django's model fields accept options that they don't do anything "
"with. For example, you can pass "
"both :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.editable` "
"and :attr:`~django.db.models.DateField.auto_now` to "
"a :class:`django.db.models.DateField` and it will ignore "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.editable` parameter "
"(:attr:`~django.db.models.DateField.auto_now` being set implies "
"``editable=False``). No error is raised in this case."
msgstr ""
"Glacann go leor de réimsí samhlacha Django le roghanna nach ndéanann siad "
"aon rud leo. Mar shampla, is féidir leat araon: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.field.editable` agus:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.datefield.auto_now` a rith chuig a:class: "
"`Django.db.Models.DateField` agus déanfaidh sé neamhaird ar pharaiméadar: "
"attr: `~django.db.models.field.editable` (:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.datefield.auto_now` atá socraithe le tuiscint "
"``Editable=False``). Ní ardaítear aon earráid sa chás seo."

msgid ""
"This behavior simplifies the field classes, because they don't need to check "
"for options that aren't necessary. They pass all the options to the parent "
"class and then don't use them later on. It's up to you whether you want your "
"fields to be more strict about the options they select, or to use the more "
"permissive behavior of the current fields."
msgstr ""
