"ref/models/fields>` le haghaidh samplaí agus sonraí."

msgid "Field deconstruction"
msgstr "Dífhoirmiú allamuigh"

msgid ""
"The counterpoint to writing your ``__init__()`` method is writing "
"the :meth:`~.Field.deconstruct` method. It's used during :doc:`model "
"migrations </topics/migrations>` to tell Django how to take an instance of "
"your new field and reduce it to a serialized form - in particular, what "
"arguments to pass to ``__init__()`` to recreate it."
msgstr ""
"Is é an contrárphointe le do mhodh ``__init__ () ``a scríobh ná an "
"modh:meth: `~.field.deconstruct` a scríobh. Úsáidtear é le linn: doc: "
"`imirce samhail` chun a insint le Django conas sampla de do réimse </topics/"
"migrations> nua a thógáil agus é a laghdú go foirm shraitheach - go "
"háirithe, cad iad na hargóintí atá le dul chuig ``__init__ () ``chun é a "
"athchruthú."

msgid ""
"If you haven't added any extra options on top of the field you inherited "
"from, then there's no need to write a new ``deconstruct()`` method. If, "
"however, you're changing the arguments passed in ``__init__()`` (like we are "
"in ``HandField``), you'll need to supplement the values being passed."
msgstr ""
"Mura gcuir tú aon roghanna breise leis ar bharr an réimse a d'oidhreacht "
"uaidh, ansin ní gá modh nua ``deconstruct () `a scríobh. Má tá tú ag athrú, "
"áfach, na hargóintí a rith in ``__init__ () ``(mar atá muid i `Handfield``), "
"beidh ort na luachanna atá á rith a fhorlíonadh."

msgid ""
"``deconstruct()`` returns a tuple of four items: the field's attribute name, "
"the full import path of the field class, the positional arguments (as a "
"list), and the keyword arguments (as a dict). Note this is different from "
"the ``deconstruct()`` method :ref:`for custom classes <custom-deconstruct-"
"method>` which returns a tuple of three things."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``deconstruct () ``cúpla de cheithre mhír ar ais: ainm tréith an "
"réimse, cosán iomlán iompórtála an aicme réimse, na hargóintí suímh (mar "
"liosta), agus na hargóintí eochairfhocal (mar dhic). Tabhair faoi deara go "
"bhfuil sé seo difriúil ón modh ``deconstruct () ``: ref: `d'aicmí "
"saincheaptha <custom-deconstruct-method>`a thugann tuple de thrí rud ar ais."

msgid ""
"As a custom field author, you don't need to care about the first two values; "
"the base ``Field`` class has all the code to work out the field's attribute "
"name and import path. You do, however, have to care about the positional and "
"keyword arguments, as these are likely the things you are changing."
msgstr ""
"Mar údar réimse saincheaptha, ní gá duit aire a thabhairt faoin gcéad dá "
"luach; tá an cód go léir ag an mbonn rang ``Field` chun ainm tréith agus "
"cosán allmhairithe an réimse a oibriú amach. Caithfidh tú, áfach, aire a "
"thabhairt faoi na hargóintí seasaimh agus eochairfhocal, mar is dócha gurb "
"iad seo na rudaí atá á athrú agat."

msgid ""
"For example, in our ``HandField`` class we're always forcibly setting "
"max_length in ``__init__()``. The ``deconstruct()`` method on the base "
"``Field`` class will see this and try to return it in the keyword arguments; "
"thus, we can drop it from the keyword arguments for readability::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, inár rang ``Handfield`` táimid i gcónaí ag socrú go "
"foréigeantach max_length in ``__init__ () ``. Feicfidh an modh `deconstruct "
"() ``ar an rang bonn ``Field` é seo agus déanfaidh sé iarracht é a thabhairt "
"ar ais sna hargóintí eochairfhocal; dá bhrí sin, is féidir linn é a "
"scaoileadh ó na hargóintí eochairfhocal le haghaidh inléiteachta:"

msgid ""
"If you add a new keyword argument, you need to write code in "
"``deconstruct()`` that puts its value into ``kwargs`` yourself. You should "
"also omit the value from ``kwargs`` when it isn't necessary to reconstruct "
"the state of the field, such as when the default value is being used::"
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann tú argóint eochairfhocal nua leis, ní mór duit cód a scríobh i "
"`deconstruct () ``a chuireann a luach isteach i `kwargs`` tú féin. Ba chóir "
"duit an luach ó `kwargs ``a fhágáil freisin nuair nach gá staid an réimse a "
"athchóiriú, mar shampla nuair a bhíonn an luach réamhshocraithe á n-úsáid:"

msgid ""
"More complex examples are beyond the scope of this document, but remember - "
"for any configuration of your Field instance, ``deconstruct()`` must return "
"arguments that you can pass to ``__init__`` to reconstruct that state."
msgstr ""
"Tá samplaí níos casta thar raon feidhme an doiciméad seo, ach cuimhnigh - le "
"haghaidh aon chumraíocht de do shampla Réimse, ní mór ``deconstruct () "
"``argóintí a thabhairt ar ais ar féidir leat a chur chuig ``__init__`` chun "
"an stát sin a athchóiriú."

msgid ""
"Pay extra attention if you set new default values for arguments in the "
"``Field`` superclass; you want to make sure they're always included, rather "
"than disappearing if they take on the old default value."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair aird bhreise má shocraíonn tú luachanna réamhshocraithe nua "
"d'argóintí sa sáraicme ``Field`; ba mhaith leat a chinntiú go bhfuil siad "
"san áireamh i gcónaí, seachas imeacht má ghlacann siad leis an seanluach "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"In addition, try to avoid returning values as positional arguments; where "
"possible, return values as keyword arguments for maximum future "
"compatibility. If you change the names of things more often than their "
"position in the constructor's argument list, you might prefer positional, "
"but bear in mind that people will be reconstructing your field from the "
"serialized version for quite a while (possibly years), depending how long "
"your migrations live for."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, déan iarracht luachanna a thabhairt ar ais mar argóintí "
"seasaimh a sheachaint; nuair is féidir, cuir luachanna ar ais mar argóintí "
"eochairfhocal chun Má athraíonn tú ainmneacha rudaí níos minice ná a seasamh "
"i liosta argóintí an tógálaí, b'fhéidir gur fearr leat suíomh, ach coinnigh "
"i gcuimhne go mbeidh daoine ag athtógáil do réimse ón leagan sraitheach ar "
"feadh tamaill go leor (blianta b'fhéidir), ag brath ar fad a bheidh do "
"imirce."

msgid ""
"You can see the results of deconstruction by looking in migrations that "
"include the field, and you can test deconstruction in unit tests by "
"deconstructing and reconstructing the field::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat torthaí an dífhoirmithe a fheiceáil trí imirce a chuimsíonn "
"an réimse a chuimsíonn, agus is féidir leat dífhoirmiú a thástáil i "
"dtástálacha aonaid tríd an réimse a dhífhoirmiú agus a athchóiriú:"

msgid "Field attributes not affecting database column definition"
msgstr "Tréithe réimse nach mbíonn tionchar ag sainmhíniú"

msgid ""
"You can override ``Field.non_db_attrs`` to customize attributes of a field "
"that don't affect a column definition. It's used during model migrations to "
