msgstr ""
"Mar a pléadh in:ref: `réimsí a bhaint <migrations-removing-model-fields>`, "
"ní mór duit an rang bunaidh `CustomCharfield` a choinneáil chomh fada agus a "
"bhíonn imirceanna agat a thagann tagairt dó."

msgid "Documenting your custom field"
msgstr "Do réimse saincheaptha a dhoiciméadú"

msgid ""
"As always, you should document your field type, so users will know what it "
"is. In addition to providing a docstring for it, which is useful for "
"developers, you can also allow users of the admin app to see a short "
"description of the field type via the :doc:`django.contrib.admindocs </ref/"
"contrib/admin/admindocs>` application. To do this provide descriptive text "
"in a :attr:`~Field.description` class attribute of your custom field. In the "
"above example, the description displayed by the ``admindocs`` application "
"for a ``HandField`` will be 'A hand of cards (bridge style)'."
msgstr ""
"Mar is gnách, ba cheart duit do chineál réimse a dhoiciméadú, ionas go "
"mbeidh a fhios ag úsáideoirí cad é. Chomh maith le docstring a sholáthar dó, "
"atá úsáideach d'fhorbróirí, is féidir leat ligean d'úsáideoirí an aip "
"riaracháin cur síos gairid ar an gcineál réimse a fheiceáil tríd an "
"bhfeidhmchlár: doc: `django.contrib.admin</ref/contrib/admin/admindocs> "
"docs`. Chun seo a dhéanamh soláthraíonn téacs tuairisciúil in a:attr: "
"`~field.description` tréith aicme do réimse saincheaptha. Sa sampla thuas, "
"is é 'Lámh cártaí (stíl droichead) 'an cur síos a thaispeánann an t-iarratas "
"``admindocs` ar ``lámha láimhse``."

msgid ""
"In the :mod:`django.contrib.admindocs` display, the field description is "
"interpolated with ``field.__dict__`` which allows the description to "
"incorporate arguments of the field. For example, the description "
"for :class:`~django.db.models.CharField` is::"
msgstr ""
"Sa taispeán:mod: `django.contrib.admindocs`, tá cur síos ar an réimse "
"idirphóilte le ``réimse. __dict__`` a ligeann don tuairisc argóintí an "
"réimse a ionchorprú. Mar shampla, is é an cur síos dag:class: "
"`~django.db.models.charfield`:"

msgid "Useful methods"
msgstr "Modhanna úsáideacha"

msgid ""
"Once you've created your :class:`~django.db.models.Field` subclass, you "
"might consider overriding a few standard methods, depending on your field's "
"behavior. The list of methods below is in approximately decreasing order of "
"importance, so start from the top."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh do fho-aicme: Class: `~Django.db.Models.Field` cruthaithe "
"agat, b'fhéidir go smaoinfidh tú ar chúpla modh caighdeánach a shárú, ag "
"brath ar iompar do réimse. Tá an liosta modhanna thíos in ord tábhachtachta "
"thart ar laghdú, mar sin tosaigh ón mbarr."

msgid "Custom database types"
msgstr "Cineálacha sonraí saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"Say you've created a PostgreSQL custom type called ``mytype``. You can "
"subclass ``Field`` and implement the :meth:`~Field.db_type` method, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Abair gur chruthaigh tú cineál saincheaptha PostgreSQL ar a dtugtar "
"``mytype``. Is féidir leat fo-aicme ``Field`` agus an modh:meth: "
"`~field.db_type` a chur i bhfeidhm, mar sin:"

msgid ""
"Once you have ``MytypeField``, you can use it in any model, just like any "
"other ``Field`` type::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh `MyTypeField` agat, is féidir leat é a úsáid in aon mhúnla, "
"díreach cosúil le haon chineál ``Field` eile:"

msgid ""
"If you aim to build a database-agnostic application, you should account for "
"differences in database column types. For example, the date/time column type "
"in PostgreSQL is called ``timestamp``, while the same column in MySQL is "
"called ``datetime``. You can handle this in a :meth:`~Field.db_type` method "
"by checking the ``connection.vendor`` attribute. Current built-in vendor "
"names are: ``sqlite``, ``postgresql``, ``mysql``, and ``oracle``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé mar aidhm agat feidhmchlár agnasach bunachar sonraí a thógáil, ba "
"cheart duit cuntas a thabhairt ar dhifríochtaí i gcineálacha colún bunachar "
"sonraí. Mar shampla, tugtar `timestamp ``ar an gcineál colún dáta/ama i "
"PostgreSQL, agus tugtar `datetime`` ar an gcolún céanna i MySQL. Is féidir "
"leat é seo a láimhseáil i modh a:meth: `~field.db_type` tríd an tréith "
"``connection.vendor`` a sheiceáil. Is iad na hainmneacha díoltóra ionsuite "
"atá ann faoi láthair ná: `sqlite``, `postgresql``, ``mysql``, agus "
"``oracle``."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~Field.db_type` and :meth:`~Field.rel_db_type` methods are called "
"by Django when the framework constructs the ``CREATE TABLE`` statements for "
"your application -- that is, when you first create your tables. The methods "
"are also called when constructing a ``WHERE`` clause that includes the model "
"field -- that is, when you retrieve data using QuerySet methods like "
"``get()``, ``filter()``, and ``exclude()`` and have the model field as an "
"argument."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn Django ar na modhanna: Meth: `~Field.DB_TYPE` agus:meth: "
"`~Field.rel_DB_TYPE` nuair a thógann an creat na ráitis ``CREATE TABLE`` "
"d'iarratas - is é sin, nuair a chruthaíonn tú do tháblaí den chéad uair. "
"Tugtar ar na modhanna freisin agus clásal ``WHERE`` á thógáil lena n-"
"áirítear an réimse samhail - is é sin, nuair a aisghabhann tú sonraí ag "
"baint úsáide as modhanna QuerySet mar ``get () ``, ``filter ()``, agus "
"```eisiamh () ``agus bíonn an réimse samhail mar argóint."

msgid ""
"Some database column types accept parameters, such as ``CHAR(25)``, where "
"the parameter ``25`` represents the maximum column length. In cases like "
"these, it's more flexible if the parameter is specified in the model rather "
"than being hard-coded in the ``db_type()`` method. For example, it wouldn't "
"make much sense to have a ``CharMaxlength25Field``, shown here::"
msgstr ""
"Glacann roinnt cineálacha colún bunachar sonraí le paraiméadair, mar shampla "
"``CHAR (25) ``, áit a léiríonn an paraiméadar ```25`` fad uasta an cholúin. "
"I gcásanna mar seo, tá sé níos solúbtha má shonraítear an paraiméadar sa "
"tsamhail seachas a bheith crua-chódaithe sa mhodh `db_type () `. Mar "
"shampla, ní bheadh sé mórán ciall go mbeadh ``CharmaxLength25field` a bheith "
"agat, a thaispeántar anseo:"

msgid ""
"The better way of doing this would be to make the parameter specifiable at "
"run time -- i.e., when the class is instantiated. To do that, implement "
"``Field.__init__()``, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach níos fearr chun é seo a dhéanamh ná an paraiméadar a "
"dhéanamh inshonraithe ag am reatha - ie, nuair a bhíonn an rang ag teacht "
"isteach. Chun sin a dhéanamh, cuir `Réimse i bhfeidhm. __init__ () ``, mar "
"sin:"

msgid ""
"Finally, if your column requires truly complex SQL setup, return ``None`` "
"from :meth:`.db_type`. This will cause Django's SQL creation code to skip "
"over this field. You are then responsible for creating the column in the "
"right table in some other way, but this gives you a way to tell Django to "
"get out of the way."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, má éilíonn do cholún socrú SQL fíor-chasta, filleadh "
"``None`` ó: meth: `.db_type`. Cuirfidh sé seo faoi deara go scipeálfaidh cód "
"cruthaithe SQL Django thar an réimse seo. Tá tú freagrach ansin as an colún "
"a chruthú sa tábla ceart ar bhealach éigin eile, ach tugann sé seo bealach "
"duit chun a rá le Django dul amach as an mbealach."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~Field.rel_db_type` method is called by fields such as "
"``ForeignKey`` and ``OneToOneField`` that point to another field to "
"determine their database column data types. For example, if you have an "
"``UnsignedAutoField``, you also need the foreign keys that point to that "
"field to use the same data type::"
msgstr ""
"Glaonn an modh: Meth: `~Field.rel_DB_Type` trí réimsí mar ``ForeignKey`` "
"agus ``OneTooneField`` a thugann pointe chuig réimse eile chun a gcineálacha "
"sonraí colún bunachar sonraí a chinneadh. Mar shampla, má tá "
"``UnsignedaUtofield`` agat, teastaíonn na heochracha eachtracha uait a "
"chuireann in iúl chuig an réimse sin chun an cineál sonraí céanna a úsáid:"

msgid "Converting values to Python objects"
msgstr "Luachanna a thiontú go rudaí Python"

msgid ""
"If your custom :class:`~Field` class deals with data structures that are "
"more complex than strings, dates, integers, or floats, then you may need to "
"override :meth:`~Field.from_db_value` and :meth:`~Field.to_python`."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéileálann do rang saincheap:class: `~Field` le struchtúir sonraí atá "
"níos casta ná teaghráin, dátaí, sláimhreacha nó snámha, ansin b'fhéidir go "
"mbeidh ort athraithe:meth: `~field.from_db_value` agus:meth: "
"`~field.to_python`."

msgid ""
"If present for the field subclass, ``from_db_value()`` will be called in all "
"circumstances when the data is loaded from the database, including in "
"aggregates and :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.values` calls."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé i láthair don fho-aicme réimse, glaofar ``from_db_value () ``i "
"ngach imthosca nuair a luchtaítear na sonraí ón mbunachar sonraí, lena n-"
"áirítear i gcomhiomlánacha agus:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.values` glaonna."

msgid ""
"``to_python()`` is called by deserialization and during "
"the :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.clean` method used from forms."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ``to_python () ``trí dhísheirialú agus le linn an modh:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.clean` a úsáidtear ó fhoirmeacha."

msgid ""
"As a general rule, ``to_python()`` should deal gracefully with any of the "
"following arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Mar riail ghinearálta, ba cheart go ndéanfadh ``to_python () ``déileáil go "
"grásta le haon cheann de na hargóintí seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"An instance of the correct type (e.g., ``Hand`` in our ongoing example)."
msgstr "Sampla den chineál ceart (m.sh., `Lám`` inár sampla leanúnach)."

msgid "A string"
msgstr "A shreang"

msgid "``None`` (if the field allows ``null=True``)"
msgstr "``None`` (má cheadaíonn an réimse ``Null=True``)"

msgid ""
"In our ``HandField`` class, we're storing the data as a ``VARCHAR`` field in "
"the database, so we need to be able to process strings and ``None`` in the "
"``from_db_value()``. In ``to_python()``, we need to also handle ``Hand`` "
"instances::"
msgstr ""
"Inár rang ``Handfield``, táimid ag stóráil na sonraí mar réimse ``VARCHAR`` "
"sa bhunachar sonraí, mar sin ní mór dúinn a bheith in ann teaghráin agus "
"``None`` a phróiseáil sa ``from_db_value () ``. I ``to_python () ``, ní mór "
"dúinn cásanna ``Hand`` a láimhseáil freisin:"

msgid ""
"Notice that we always return a ``Hand`` instance from these methods. That's "
"the Python object type we want to store in the model's attribute."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcuirimid sampla ``Hand`` ar ais i gcónaí ó na "
"modhanna seo. Sin an cineál réada Python ba mhaith linn a stóráil i dtréith "
"an tsamhail."

msgid ""
"For ``to_python()``, if anything goes wrong during value conversion, you "
"should raise a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` exception."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le ``to_python () ``, má théann aon rud mícheart le linn tiontaithe "
"luacha, ba cheart duit eisceacht a:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.ValidationError` a ardú."

msgid "Converting Python objects to query values"
msgstr "Rudaí Python a thiontú go luachanna ceisteanna"

msgid ""
"Since using a database requires conversion in both ways, if you "
"override :meth:`~Field.from_db_value` you also have to "
"override :meth:`~Field.get_prep_value` to convert Python objects back to "
"query values."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go n-éilíonn tiontú ar bhonn sonraí a úsáid ar an dá bhealach, má "
"théann tú róth:meth: `~field.from_db_value` caithfidh tú ró-ride:meth: "
"`~field.get_prep_value` chun rudaí Python a thiontú ar ais go luachanna "
"fiosrúcháin."

msgid ""
"If your custom field uses the ``CHAR``, ``VARCHAR`` or ``TEXT`` types for "
"MySQL, you must make sure that :meth:`.get_prep_value` always returns a "
"string type. MySQL performs flexible and unexpected matching when a query is "
"performed on these types and the provided value is an integer, which can "
"cause queries to include unexpected objects in their results. This problem "
"cannot occur if you always return a string type from :meth:`.get_prep_value`."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann do réimse saincheaptha na cineálacha ``CHAR``, `VARCHAR`` nó "
"``TEXT`` do MySQL, ní mór duit a chinntiú go bhfillfidh: meth: "
"`.get_prep_value` cineál teaghrán i gcónaí. Déanann MySQL meaitseáil "
"sholúbtha agus gan choinne nuair a dhéantar fiosrúchán ar na cineálacha seo "
"agus is sláimhir é an luach a chuirtear ar fáil, rud a d'fhéadfadh a bheith "
"ina gcúis le ceisteanna rudaí gan choinne a Ní féidir leis an bhfadhb seo "
"tarlú má thugann tú cineál teaghrán ar ais i gcónaí ó:meth: "
"`.get_prep_value`."

msgid "Converting query values to database values"
msgstr "Luachanna ceist a thiontú go luachanna bunachar"

msgid ""
"Some data types (for example, dates) need to be in a specific format before "
"they can be used by a database backend. :meth:`~Field.get_db_prep_value` is "
"the method where those conversions should be made. The specific connection "
"that will be used for the query is passed as the ``connection`` parameter. "
"This allows you to use backend-specific conversion logic if it is required."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh roinnt cineálacha sonraí (mar shampla, dátaí) a bheith i bhformáid "
"shonrach sula bhféadfaidh cúltaca bunachar sonraí iad a úsáid. :meth: "
"`~Field.get_DB_Prep_Value` is é an modh inar chóir na tiontaithe sin a "
"dhéanamh. Cuirtear an nasc sonrach a úsáidfear don cheist ar aghaidh mar "
"pharaiméadar ``nasc``. Ligeann sé seo duit loighic chomhshó cúltaca a úsáid "
"má tá sé ag teastáil."

msgid ""
"For example, Django uses the following method for its :class:`BinaryField`::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, úsáideann Django an modh seo a leanas dá: aicme: `BinaryField`::"

msgid ""
"In case your custom field needs a special conversion when being saved that "
"is not the same as the conversion used for normal query parameters, you can "
"override :meth:`~Field.get_db_prep_save`."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás go dteastaíonn tiontú speisialta ag teastáil ó do réimse "
"saincheaptha agus é a shábháil nach bhfuil mar an gcéanna leis an gcomhshó a "
"úsáidtear le haghaidh gnáthpharaiméadair fiosrúcháin, is féidir leat "
"athraithe:meth: `~field.get_db_prep_save`."

msgid "Preprocessing values before saving"
msgstr "Luachanna réamhphróiseála sula sábháil"

msgid ""
"If you want to preprocess the value just before saving, you can "
"use :meth:`~Field.pre_save`. For example, "
"Django's :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` uses this method to set "
"the attribute correctly in the case "
"of :attr:`~django.db.models.DateField.auto_now` "
"or :attr:`~django.db.models.DateField.auto_now_add`."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an luach a réamhphróiseáil díreach sula sábhálann tú, is "
"féidir leat: meth: `~field.pre_save` a úsáid. Mar shampla, úsáideann "
"Django's:Class: `~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField` an modh seo chun an tréith "
"a shocrú i gceart sa chás de:attr: `~django.db.models.dateField.auto_now` "
"nó:attr: `~Django.db.Models.DateField.Auto_Now_Add`."

msgid ""
"If you do override this method, you must return the value of the attribute "
"at the end. You should also update the model's attribute if you make any "
"changes to the value so that code holding references to the model will "
"always see the correct value."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéanann tú an modh seo a shárú, ní mór duit luach na tréithe a thabhairt "
"ar ais ag an deireadh. Ba cheart duit tréith an tsamhail a nuashonrú freisin "
"má dhéanann tú aon athruithe ar an luach ionas go bhfeicfidh cód ina bhfuil "
"tagairtí don tsamhail an luach ceart i gcónaí."

msgid "Specifying the form field for a model field"
msgstr "An réimse foirme do réimse samhail a shonrú"

msgid ""
"To customize the form field used by :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm`, you "
"can override :meth:`~Field.formfield`."
msgstr ""
"Chun an réimse foirme a úsáideann:: class: `~django.forms.ModelForm` a "
"shaincheapadh, is féidir leat: meth: `~Field.FormField` a shárú."

msgid ""
"The form field class can be specified via the ``form_class`` and "
"``choices_form_class`` arguments; the latter is used if the field has "
"choices specified, the former otherwise. If these arguments are not "
"provided, :class:`~django.forms.CharField` "
"or :class:`~django.forms.TypedChoiceField` will be used."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an rang réimse foirme a shonrú trí na hargóintí ``form_class`` "
"agus ``roghnaí_form_class``; úsáidtear an dara ceann má tá roghanna "
"sonraithe sa réimse, an chéad cheann eile a shlí eile. Mura gcuirtear na "
"hargóintí seo ar fáil, úsáidfear :class: `~django.forms.charfield` nó:class: "
"`~django.forms.typedChoiceField`."

msgid ""
"All of the ``kwargs`` dictionary is passed directly to the form field's "
"``__init__()`` method. Normally, all you need to do is set up a good default "
"for the ``form_class`` (and maybe ``choices_form_class``) argument and then "
"delegate further handling to the parent class. This might require you to "
"write a custom form field (and even a form widget). See the :doc:`forms "
"documentation </topics/forms/index>` for information about this."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar an foclóir ``kwargs`` ar fad díreach chuig modh ``__init__()`` "
"réimse na foirme. De ghnáth, níl le déanamh ach réamhshocrú maith a shocrú "
"don argóint ``form_class`` (agus b'fhéidir ``choices_form_class``) agus "
"ansin láimhseáil bhreise a tharmligean chuig an rang tuismitheora. "
"D’fhéadfadh go n-éileodh sé seo leat réimse foirme saincheaptha (agus fiú "
"giuirléid foirme) a scríobh. Féach an :doc:`doiciméid foirmeacha </topics/"
"forms/index>` le haghaidh faisnéise faoi seo."

msgid ""
"If you wish to exclude the field from the :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm`, "
"you can override the :meth:`~Field.formfield` method to return ``None``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Continuing our ongoing example, we can write the :meth:`~Field.formfield` "
"method as::"
msgstr ""
"Ag leanúint lenár sampla leanúnach, is féidir linn an modh: meth: "
"`~field.formField` a scríobh mar:"

msgid ""
"This assumes we've imported a ``MyFormField`` field class (which has its own "
"default widget). This document doesn't cover the details of writing custom "
"form fields."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé seo leis go bhfuil aicme réimse ``MyFormField`` iompórtáilte "
"againn (a bhfuil a ghiuirléid réamhshocraithe féin aige). Ní chlúdaíonn an "
"doiciméad seo na sonraí maidir le réimsí foirme saincheaptha a scríobh."

msgid "Emulating built-in field types"
msgstr "Cineálacha réimse ionsuite a aithris"

msgid ""
"If you have created a :meth:`.db_type` method, you don't need to worry "
"about :meth:`.get_internal_type` -- it won't be used much. Sometimes, "
"though, your database storage is similar in type to some other field, so you "
"can use that other field's logic to create the right column."
msgstr ""
"Má chruthaigh tú modh a:meth: `.db_type`, ní gá duit a bheith buartha "
"fao:meth: `.get_internal_type` - ní úsáidfear mórán é. Uaireanta, áfach, "
"bíonn do stóráil bunachar sonraí cosúil le cineál réimse éigin eile, ionas "
"gur féidir leat loighic réimse eile sin a úsáid chun an colún ceart a "
"chruthú."

msgid ""
"No matter which database backend we are using, this will mean "
"that :djadmin:`migrate` and other SQL commands create the right column type "
"for storing a string."
msgstr ""
"Is cuma cén cúltaca bunachar sonraí atá á úsáid againn, ciallóidh sé seo go "
"gcruthaíonn: djadmin: `migrate` agus orduithe SQL eile an cineál colún ceart "
"chun sreang a stóráil."

msgid ""
"If :meth:`.get_internal_type` returns a string that is not known to Django "
"for the database backend you are using -- that is, it doesn't appear in "
"``django.db.backends.<db_name>.base.DatabaseWrapper.data_types`` -- the "
"string will still be used by the serializer, but the "
"default :meth:`~Field.db_type` method will return ``None``. See the "
"documentation of :meth:`~Field.db_type` for reasons why this might be "
"useful. Putting a descriptive string in as the type of the field for the "
"serializer is a useful idea if you're ever going to be using the serializer "
"output in some other place, outside of Django."
msgstr ""
"If: Meth: `.get_internal_type` filleann sreang nach bhfuil ar eolas ag "
"Django don chúltaca bunachar sonraí atá á úsáid agat - is é sin, níl sé le "
"feiceáil i ``django.db.backends. <db_name>.base.databaseWrapper.Data_Types`` "
"-- úsáidfidh an serializer an sreang fós, ach cuirfidh an modh "
"réamhshocraithe: meth: `~Field.db_type` ar ais ``None``. Féach an doiciméadú "
"de:meth: `~field.db_type` ar chúiseanna a d'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith "
"úsáideach. Is smaoineamh úsáideach é teaghrán tuairisciúil a chur isteach "
"mar chineál an réimse don serializer má tá tú riamh ag baint úsáide as an "
"aschur serializer in áit éigin eile, lasmuigh de Django."

msgid "Converting field data for serialization"
msgstr "Sonraí réimse a thiontú le haghaidh sraitheadh"

msgid ""
"To customize how the values are serialized by a serializer, you can "
"override :meth:`~Field.value_to_string`. "
"Using :meth:`~Field.value_from_object` is the best way to get the field's "
"value prior to serialization. For example, since ``HandField`` uses strings "
"for its data storage anyway, we can reuse some existing conversion code::"
msgstr ""
"Chun an chaoi a ndéantar na luachanna a shraitheadh ag serializer a "
"shaincheapadh, is féidir leat: meth: `~field.value_to_string` a shárú. "
"Úsáid:Meth: `~ Field.value_from_Object` is é an bealach is fearr chun luach "
"an réimse a fháil roimh shraitheadh. Mar shampla, ós rud é go n-úsáideann "
"`Handfield` teaghráin lena stóráil sonraí ar aon nós, is féidir linn roinnt "
"cód tiontaithe atá ann cheana a athúsáid::"

msgid "Some general advice"
msgstr "Roinnt comhairle ginearálta"

msgid ""
"Writing a custom field can be a tricky process, particularly if you're doing "
"complex conversions between your Python types and your database and "
"serialization formats. Here are a couple of tips to make things go more "
"smoothly:"
msgstr ""
"Is próiseas deacair is féidir le réimse saincheaptha a scríobh, go háirithe "
"má tá tiontaithe casta á dhéanamh agat idir do chineálacha Python agus do "
"bhunachar sonraí agus formáidí sraitheach. Seo cúpla leid chun rudaí a "
"dhéanamh níos réidh:"

msgid ""
"Look at the existing Django fields (in :source:`django/db/models/fields/"
"__init__.py`) for inspiration. Try to find a field that's similar to what "
"you want and extend it a little bit, instead of creating an entirely new "
"field from scratch."
msgstr ""
"Féach ar na réimsí Django atá ann cheana (in:source: `django/db/models/"
"fields/__init__.py`) le haghaidh inspioráide. Déan iarracht réimse a fháil "
"atá cosúil leis an méid atá uait agus é a leathnú beagán, in ionad réimse "
"iomlán nua a chruthú ón tús."

msgid ""
"Put a ``__str__()`` method on the class you're wrapping up as a field. There "
"are a lot of places where the default behavior of the field code is to call "
"``str()`` on the value. (In our examples in this document, ``value`` would "
"be a ``Hand`` instance, not a ``HandField``). So if your ``__str__()`` "
"method automatically converts to the string form of your Python object, you "
"can save yourself a lot of work."
msgstr ""
"Cuir modh ``__str__ () ``ar an rang atá tú ag timfhilleadh suas mar réimse. "
"Tá go leor áiteanna ann ina bhfuil iompar réamhshocraithe an chód réimse "
"glaoch ar ``str () ``ar an luach. (Sna samplaí atá againn sa doiciméad seo, "
"is sampla ``Láimh`` a bheadh `luach ``, `Láimhe``, ``Láimhe ``, "
"``Láimhse``). Mar sin má athraíonn do mhodh ``__str__ () ``go huathoibríoch "
"go foirm teaghrán do réad Python, is féidir leat a lán oibre a shábháil duit "
"féin."

msgid "Writing a ``FileField`` subclass"
msgstr "Ag scríobh fo-aicme ``Filefield``"

msgid ""
"In addition to the above methods, fields that deal with files have a few "
"other special requirements which must be taken into account. The majority of "
"the mechanics provided by ``FileField``, such as controlling database "
"storage and retrieval, can remain unchanged, leaving subclasses to deal with "
"the challenge of supporting a particular type of file."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na modhanna thuas, tá cúpla riachtanas speisialta eile ag "
"réimsí a dhéileálann le comhaid nach mór a chur san áireamh. Is féidir le "
"formhór na meicnic a sholáthraíonn “Filefield”, amhail stóráil agus "
"aisghabháil bunachar sonraí a rialú, fanacht gan athrú, ag fágáil fo-aicmí "
"chun déileáil leis an dúshlán tacú le cineál áirithe comhad."

msgid ""
"Django provides a ``File`` class, which is used as a proxy to the file's "
"contents and operations. This can be subclassed to customize how the file is "
"accessed, and what methods are available. It lives at "
"``django.db.models.fields.files``, and its default behavior is explained in "
"the :doc:`file documentation </ref/files/file>`."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django aicme ``Comhad ``, a úsáidtear mar sheachfhreastalaí "
"d'ábhar agus oibríochtaí an chomhaid. Is féidir é seo a fho-aicmiú chun an "
"chaoi a ndéantar rochtain ar an gcomhad a shaincheapadh, agus na modhanna "
"atá ar fáil. Tá sé ina chónaí ag `django.db.models.fields.fil</ref/files/"
"file> es``, agus mínítear a iompar réamhshocraithe in:doc: `doiciméadú "
"comhad`."

msgid ""
"Once a subclass of ``File`` is created, the new ``FileField`` subclass must "
"be told to use it. To do so, assign the new ``File`` subclass to the special "
"``attr_class`` attribute of the ``FileField`` subclass."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chruthaítear fo-aicme de `Comhad ``, ní mór a rá don fho-aicme nua "
"``FileField`` é a úsáid. Chun é sin a dhéanamh, sannadh an fo-aicme nua "
"``File`` don tréith speisialta ```attr_class`` den fho-aicme ``FileField``."

msgid "A few suggestions"
msgstr "Cúpla moladh"

msgid ""
"In addition to the above details, there are a few guidelines which can "
"greatly improve the efficiency and readability of the field's code."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na sonraí thuas, tá cúpla treoirlínte ann ar féidir leo "
"éifeachtúlacht agus inléiteacht chód an réimse a fheabhsú go mór."

msgid ""
"The source for Django's own ``ImageField`` (in :source:`django/db/models/"
"fields/files.py`) is a great example of how to subclass ``FileField`` to "
"support a particular type of file, as it incorporates all of the techniques "
"described above."
msgstr ""
"Is sampla iontach é an fhoinse do `ImageField`` féin Django (in:source: "
"`django/db/models/fields/files.py`) de conas fo-aicme ``Filefield`` chun "
"tacú le cineál áirithe comhad, mar go n-ionchorpraíonn sé na teicnící go "
"léir a thuairiscítear thuas."

msgid ""
"Cache file attributes wherever possible. Since files may be stored in remote "
"storage systems, retrieving them may cost extra time, or even money, that "
"isn't always necessary. Once a file is retrieved to obtain some data about "
"its content, cache as much of that data as possible to reduce the number of "
"times the file must be retrieved on subsequent calls for that information."
msgstr ""
"Tréithe comhaid taisce nuair is féidir. Ós rud é go bhféadfar comhaid a "
"stóráil i gcórais stórála iargúlta, d'fhéadfadh go gcosnóidh siad am breise, "
"nó fiú airgead, ní gá é sin i gcónaí. Nuair a aisghabtar comhad chun roinnt "
"sonraí faoina ábhar a fháil, taisce an oiread de na sonraí sin agus is "
"féidir chun an líon uaireanta caithfear an comhad a aisghabháil ar ghlaonna "
"ina dhiaidh sin ar an bhfaisnéis sin a laghdú."

msgid "How to customize the ``shell`` command"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Django :djadmin:`shell` is an interactive Python environment that "
"provides access to models and settings, making it useful for testing code, "
"experimenting with queries, and interacting with application data."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Customizing the :djadmin:`shell` command allows adding extra functionality "
"or pre-loading specific modules. To do this, create a new management command "
"that subclasses ``django.core.management.commands.shell.Command`` and "
"overrides the existing ``shell`` management command. For more details, refer "
"to the guide on :ref:`overriding commands <overriding-commands>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Customize automatic imports"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To customize the automatic import behavior of the :djadmin:`shell` "
"management command, override the ``get_auto_imports()`` method. This method "
"should return a sequence of import paths for objects or modules available in "
"the application. For example:"
