"your function::"
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacann mórchuid na scagairí argóintí. Sa chás seo, fág an argóint as do "
"fheidhm:"

msgid "Registering custom filters"
msgstr "Clárú scagairí saincheap"

msgid ""
"Once you've written your filter definition, you need to register it with "
"your ``Library`` instance, to make it available to Django's template "
"language::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh do shainmhíniú scagaire scagaire scagaire scríofa agat, ní "
"mór duit é a chlárú le do shampla ``Leabharla``, chun é a chur ar fáil do "
"theanga teimpléad Django:"

msgid "The ``Library.filter()`` method takes two arguments:"
msgstr "Tógann an modh ``Library.filter () ``dhá argóint:"

msgid "The name of the filter -- a string."
msgstr "Ainm an scagaire - sreang."

msgid ""
"The compilation function -- a Python function (not the name of the function "
"as a string)."
msgstr ""
"An fheidhm tiomsaithe - feidhm Python (ní ainm na feidhme mar shreang)."

msgid "You can use ``register.filter()`` as a decorator instead::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``register.filter () ``a úsáid mar mhaisitheoir ina ionad sin:"

msgid ""
"If you leave off the ``name`` argument, as in the second example above, "
"Django will use the function's name as the filter name."
msgstr ""
"Má fhágann tú an argóint ``ainm ``amach, mar atá sa dara sampla thuas, "
"úsáidfidh Django ainm na feidhme mar ainm an scagaire."

msgid ""
"Finally, ``register.filter()`` also accepts three keyword arguments, "
"``is_safe``, ``needs_autoescape``, and ``expects_localtime``. These "
"arguments are described in :ref:`filters and auto-escaping <filters-auto-"
