"A naive implementation of ``CycleNode`` might look something like this::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cuma mar seo ar chur i bhfeidhm naif ar ``Cyclenode``:"

msgid ""
"But, suppose we have two templates rendering the template snippet from above "
"at the same time:"
msgstr ""
"Ach, cuir i gcás go bhfuil dhá theimpléad againn a dhéanann an snippet "
"teimpléad ó thuas ag an am céanna:"

msgid ""
"Thread 1 performs its first loop iteration, ``CycleNode.render()`` returns "
"'row1'"
msgstr ""
"Déanann Snáithe 1 a chéad athrú lúb, ``Cyclenode.render () ``filleann 'row1'"

msgid ""
"Thread 2 performs its first loop iteration, ``CycleNode.render()`` returns "
"'row2'"
msgstr ""
"Déanann Snáithe 2 a chéad athrú lúb, ``Cyclenode.render () ``filleann 'row2'"

msgid ""
"Thread 1 performs its second loop iteration, ``CycleNode.render()`` returns "
"'row1'"
msgstr ""
"Déanann Snáithe 1 a dara athrú lúb, ``Cyclenode.render () ``filleann 'row1'"

msgid ""
"Thread 2 performs its second loop iteration, ``CycleNode.render()`` returns "
"'row2'"
msgstr ""
"Déanann Snáithe 2 a dara athrú lúb, ``Cyclenode.render () ``filleann 'row2'"

msgid ""
"The CycleNode is iterating, but it's iterating globally. As far as Thread 1 "
"and Thread 2 are concerned, it's always returning the same value. This is "
"not what we want!"
msgstr ""
"Tá an CycleNode ag athrú, ach tá sé ag athrú ar fud an domhain. Chomh fada "
"agus a bhaineann le Snáithe 1 agus Snáithe 2, bíonn an luach céanna ar ais i "
"gcónaí. Ní hé seo an rud a theastaíonn uainn!"

msgid ""
"To address this problem, Django provides a ``render_context`` that's "
"associated with the ``context`` of the template that is currently being "
"rendered. The ``render_context`` behaves like a Python dictionary, and "
"should be used to store ``Node`` state between invocations of the ``render`` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Chun aghaidh a thabhairt ar an bhfadhb seo, soláthraíonn Django "
"``render_context`` a bhaineann le ``context`` an teimpléid atá á rinneadh "
"faoi láthair. Iompraíonn an ``render_context`` cosúil le foclóir Python, "
"agus ba chóir é a úsáid chun stát ``Node`` a stóráil idir inghairmithe an "
"modh ``render``."

msgid ""
"Let's refactor our ``CycleNode`` implementation to use the "
"``render_context``::"
msgstr ""
"Déanaimis ár bhfeidhmiú ``Cyclenode`` a athfhachtú chun an "
"``render_context`` a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"Note that it's perfectly safe to store global information that will not "
"change throughout the life of the ``Node`` as an attribute. In the case of "
"``CycleNode``, the ``cyclevars`` argument doesn't change after the ``Node`` "
"is instantiated, so we don't need to put it in the ``render_context``. But "
"state information that is specific to the template that is currently being "
"rendered, like the current iteration of the ``CycleNode``, should be stored "
"in the ``render_context``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil sé sábháilte faisnéis dhomhanda a stóráil nach "
"n-athróidh ar feadh saol an ``Node`` mar thréith. I gcás ``Cyclenode``, ní "
"athraíonn an argóint ``ciclevars`` tar éis an ``Node`` a bhunú, mar sin ní "
"gá dúinn é a chur sa `render_context``. Ach ba chóir faisnéis stáit atá "
"sonrach don teimpléad atá á rinneadh faoi láthair, cosúil le hathrú reatha "
"an ``Cyclenode``, a stóráil sa ``render_context``."

msgid ""
"Notice how we used ``self`` to scope the ``CycleNode`` specific information "
"within the ``render_context``. There may be multiple ``CycleNodes`` in a "
"given template, so we need to be careful not to clobber another node's state "
"information. The easiest way to do this is to always use ``self`` as the key "
"into ``render_context``. If you're keeping track of several state variables, "
"make ``render_context[self]`` a dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara conas a d'úsáid muid ``féin ``chun an fhaisnéis shonrach "
"``Cyclenode`` a scóip laistigh den ``render_context``. D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh "
"iolracha ``Cyclenodes`` i dteimpléad ar leith, mar sin ní mór dúinn a bheith "
"cúramach gan faisnéis stáit nód eile a chlacadh. Is é an bealach is éasca "
"chun é seo a dhéanamh ná ``self`` a úsáid i gcónaí mar an eochair isteach "
"``render_context``. Má tá súil á choinneáil agat ar roinnt athróg stáit, "
"déan foclóir ``render_context [self] ``."

msgid "Registering the tag"
msgstr "An chlib a chlárú"

msgid ""
"Finally, register the tag with your module's ``Library`` instance, as "
"explained in :ref:`writing custom template tags<howto-writing-custom-"
"template-tags>` above. Example::"
msgstr ""
"<howto-writing-custom-template-tags>Mar fhocal scoir, cláraigh an chlib le "
"sampla ``Leabharlanna`` do mhodúil, mar a mhínítear in:ref: `clibeanna "
"teimpléad saincheaptha a scríobh `thuas. Sampla::"

msgid "The ``tag()`` method takes two arguments:"
msgstr "Tógann an modh ``tag () ``dhá argóint:"

msgid ""
"The name of the template tag -- a string. If this is left out, the name of "
"the compilation function will be used."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an chlib teimpléad - sreang. Má fhágtar é seo amach, úsáidfear ainm na "
"feidhme tiomsaithe."

msgid ""
"As with filter registration, it is also possible to use this as a decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Mar is amhlaidh le clárú scagaire, is féidir é seo a úsáid mar mhaisitheoir "
"freisin:"

msgid ""
"If you leave off the ``name`` argument, as in the second example above, "
"Django will use the function's name as the tag name."
msgstr ""
"Má fhágann tú an argóint ``ainm ``amach, mar atá sa dara sampla thuas, "
"úsáidfidh Django ainm na feidhme mar ainm an chlib."

msgid "Passing template variables to the tag"
msgstr "Athróga teimpléad a chur chuig an gclib"

msgid ""
"Although you can pass any number of arguments to a template tag using "
"``token.split_contents()``, the arguments are all unpacked as string "
"literals. A little more work is required in order to pass dynamic content (a "
"template variable) to a template tag as an argument."
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir leat líon ar bith argóintí a chur chuig clib teimpléad ag "
"baint úsáide as ``token.split_contents () ``, déantar na hargóintí go léir "
"díphacáil mar litríochtaí teaghrán. Teastaíonn beagán níos mó oibre d'fhonn "
"ábhar dinimiciúil (athróg teimpléad) a chur chuig clib teimpléad mar argóint."

msgid ""
"While the previous examples have formatted the current time into a string "
"and returned the string, suppose you wanted to pass in "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` from an object and have the "
"template tag format that date-time:"
msgstr ""
"Cé gur fhormáidigh na samplaí roimhe seo an t-am reatha i sreang agus chuir "
"an sreang ar ais, cuir i gcás gur theastaigh uait pas a: class: "
"`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` ó réad agus go mbeadh an formáid clib "
"teimpléad agat an dáta-am sin:"

msgid "Initially, ``token.split_contents()`` will return three values:"
msgstr "Ar dtús, tabharfaidh `token.split_contents () ``trí luach ar ais:"

msgid "The tag name ``format_time``."
msgstr "Ainm an chlib ``format_time``."

msgid ""
"The string ``'blog_entry.date_updated'`` (without the surrounding quotes)."
msgstr "An teaghrán ```blog_entry.date_updated'` (gan na luachana máguaird)."

msgid ""
"The formatting string ``'\"%Y-%m-%d %I:%M %p\"'``. The return value from "
"``split_contents()`` will include the leading and trailing quotes for string "
"literals like this."
msgstr ""
"An teaghrán formáidithe ``'\"%Y-%M-%D %I: %M %p\"'``. Cuimsíonn an luach "
"tuairisceáin ó `split_contents () ``na luachana tosaigh agus na luachana "
"leantacha le haghaidh litríochtaí sreangacha mar seo."

msgid "Now your tag should begin to look like this::"
msgstr "Anois ba chóir go dtosóidh cuma seo ar do chlib::"

msgid ""
"You also have to change the renderer to retrieve the actual contents of the "
"``date_updated`` property of the ``blog_entry`` object.  This can be "
"accomplished by using the ``Variable()`` class in ``django.template``."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh tú an renderer a athrú freisin chun ábhar iarbhír na maoine "
"``date_updated`` den réad ``blog_entry`` a aisghabháil. Is féidir é seo a "
"chur i gcrích trí úsáid a bhaint as an aicme ``Athraitheach () ``i "
"`django.template``."

msgid ""
"To use the ``Variable`` class, instantiate it with the name of the variable "
"to be resolved, and then call ``variable.resolve(context)``. So, for "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Chun an aicme ``Variable`` a úsáid, cuir ainm an athróg atá le réiteach é, "
"agus ansin glaoigh ar ``variable.solve (context) ``. Mar sin, mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Variable resolution will throw a ``VariableDoesNotExist`` exception if it "
"cannot resolve the string passed to it in the current context of the page."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh réiteach athraitheach eisceacht ``VariableDoesNotExist`` mura "
"féidir leis an sreang a chuirtear chuige a réiteach i gcomhthéacs reatha an "
"leathanaigh."

msgid "Setting a variable in the context"
msgstr "Athróg a shocrú sa chomhthéacs"

msgid ""
"The above examples output a value. Generally, it's more flexible if your "
"template tags set template variables instead of outputting values. That way, "
"template authors can reuse the values that your template tags create."
msgstr ""
"Aschuir na samplaí thuas luach. Go ginearálta, bíonn sé níos solúbtha má "
"shocraíonn do chlibeanna teimpléid athróga teimpléid in ionad luachanna a "
"aschuir. Ar an mbealach sin, is féidir le húdair teimpléid na luachanna a "
"chruthaíonn do chlibeanna teimpléid a athúsáid."

msgid ""
"To set a variable in the context, use dictionary assignment on the context "
"object in the ``render()`` method. Here's an updated version of "
"``CurrentTimeNode`` that sets a template variable ``current_time`` instead "
"of outputting it::"
msgstr ""
"Chun athróg a shocrú sa chomhthéacs, bain úsáid as sannadh foclóra ar an "
"réad comhthéacs sa mhodh `render () ``. Seo leagan nuashonraithe de "
"``CurrentTimeNode`` a leagann athróg teimpléad ``current_time`` in ionad é a "
"chur amach:"

msgid ""
"Note that ``render()`` returns the empty string. ``render()`` should always "
"return string output. If all the template tag does is set a variable, "
"``render()`` should return the empty string."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfilleann ``render () ``an teaghrán folamh. Ba chóir "
"go gcuirfeadh ``render () ``aschur sreinge ar ais i gcónaí. Más athróg a "
"shocraíonn an chlib teimpléad go léir, ba chóir go gcuirfeadh ``render () "
"``an teaghrán folamh ar ais."

msgid "Here's how you'd use this new version of the tag:"
msgstr "Seo conas a úsáideann tú an leagan nua seo den chlib:"

msgid "Variable scope in context"
msgstr "Raon feidhme athraitheach i gcomh"

msgid ""
"Any variable set in the context will only be available in the same ``block`` "
"of the template in which it was assigned. This behavior is intentional; it "
"provides a scope for variables so that they don't conflict with context in "
"other blocks."
msgstr ""
"Ní bheidh aon athróg atá leagtha amach sa chomhthéacs ar fáil ach sa "
"``bloc`` céanna den teimpléad ina sannadh é. Tá an t-iompar seo d'aon ghnó; "
"soláthraíonn sé scóip d'athróga ionas nach mbeidh siad ag coinbhleacht le "
"comhthéacs i mbloic eile."

msgid ""
"But, there's a problem with ``CurrentTimeNode2``: The variable name "
"``current_time`` is hard-coded. This means you'll need to make sure your "
"template doesn't use ``{{ current_time }}`` anywhere else, because the ``{% "
"current_time %}`` will blindly overwrite that variable's value. A cleaner "
"solution is to make the template tag specify the name of the output "
"variable, like so:"
msgstr ""
"Ach, tá fadhb ann le ``CurrentTimeNode2``: Tá an t-ainm athróg "
"``current_time`` crua-chódaithe. Ciallaíonn sé seo go gcaithfidh tú a "
"chinntiú nach n-úsáideann do theimpléad ``{{current_time}}`` áit ar bith "
"eile, toisc go ndéanfaidh an ``{% current_time%}`` luach an athróg sin a "
"fhorscríobh go dall. Réiteach níos glaine is ea an chlib teimpléid a shonrú "
"ainm an athróg aschuir, mar sin:"

msgid ""
"To do that, you'll need to refactor both the compilation function and "
"``Node`` class, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Chun é sin a dhéanamh, beidh ort an fheidhm thiomsaithe agus an rang ``Node "
"``a athfhachtú, mar sin:"

msgid ""
"The difference here is that ``do_current_time()`` grabs the format string "
"and the variable name, passing both to ``CurrentTimeNode3``."
msgstr ""
"Is é an difríocht anseo ná go nglacann ``do_current_time () ``an teaghrán "
"formáide agus an t-ainm athraitheach, ag dul araon chuig "
"``CurrentTimeNode3``."

msgid ""
"Finally, if you only need to have a simple syntax for your custom context-"
"updating template tag, consider using "
"the :meth:`~django.template.Library.simple_tag` shortcut, which supports "
"assigning the tag results to a template variable."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, mura gá duit ach comhréir simplí a bheith agat le haghaidh "
"do chlib teimpléad saincheaptha a nuashonrú comhthéacs, smaoinigh ar "
"aiceara:meth: `~django.template.library.simple_tag` a úsáid, a thacaíonn le "
"torthaí an chlib a shannadh d'athróg teimpléad."

msgid "Parsing until another block tag"
msgstr "Parsáil go dtí chlib bloc eile"

msgid ""
"Template tags can work in tandem. For instance, the standard :ttag:`{% "
"comment %}<comment>` tag hides everything until ``{% endcomment %}``. To "
"create a template tag such as this, use ``parser.parse()`` in your "
"compilation function."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le clibeanna teimpléad oibriú in éineacht Mar shampla, folaíonn an "
"tag caighdeán:ttag: `{% comment%}<comment>` gach rud go dtí ``{% endcomment%}"
"``. Chun clib teimpléad mar seo a chruthú, bain úsáid as ``parser.parse () "
"``i do fheidhm tiomsaithe."

msgid "Here's how a simplified ``{% comment %}`` tag might be implemented::"
msgstr "Seo mar a d'fhéadfaí clib ``{% comment%} `simplithe a chur i bhfeidhm:"

msgid ""
"The actual implementation of :ttag:`{% comment %}<comment>` is slightly "
"different in that it allows broken template tags to appear between ``{% "
"comment %}`` and ``{% endcomment %}``. It does so by calling "
"``parser.skip_past('endcomment')`` instead of "
"``parser.parse(('endcomment',))`` followed by "
"``parser.delete_first_token()``, thus avoiding the generation of a node list."
msgstr ""
"Tá cur i bhfeidhm iarbhír de:ttag: `{% comment%}<comment>` beagán difriúil "
"sa mhéid go gceadaíonn sé clibeanna teimpléad briste le feiceáil idir ``{% "
"comment%} `agus`` {% endcomment%}`. Déanann sé amhlaidh trí ghlaoch ar "
"`parser.skip_past ('endcomment') ``in ionad ``parser.parse "
"('endcomment',))`` ina dhiaidh sin `parser.delete_first_token () ``, agus ar "
"an gcaoi sin giniúint liosta nód a sheachaint."

msgid ""
"``parser.parse()`` takes a tuple of names of block tags ''to parse until''. "
"It returns an instance of ``django.template.NodeList``, which is a list of "
"all ``Node`` objects that the parser encountered ''before'' it encountered "
"any of the tags named in the tuple."
msgstr ""
"Tógann ``parser.parse () ``cúpla ainmneacha de chlibeanna bloc “le parsáil "
"go dtí”. Tugann sé sampla de ``Django.Template.NodeList`` ar liosta é de na "
"rudaí ``Node`` go léir a bhuail an parser “roimh” bhuail sé aon cheann de na "
"clibeanna a ainmníodh sa tuple."

msgid ""
"In ``\"nodelist = parser.parse(('endcomment',))\"`` in the above example, "
"``nodelist`` is a list of all nodes between the ``{% comment %}`` and ``{% "
"endcomment %}``, not counting ``{% comment %}`` and ``{% endcomment %}`` "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
"I ``\"nodelist = parser.parse ('endcomment',)) \"``sa sampla thuas, is "
"liosta de na nóid go léir idir`` {% comment%} ``agus`` {% endcomment%} ``, "
"gan comhaireamh`` {% comment%} ``agus`` {% endcomment%} ``féin."

msgid ""
"After ``parser.parse()`` is called, the parser hasn't yet \"consumed\" the "
"``{% endcomment %}`` tag, so the code needs to explicitly call "
"``parser.delete_first_token()``."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis ``parser.parse () ``a ghlaoch, níor “ith” an parser an chlib`` {% "
"endcomment%} ``fós, mar sin ní mór don chód glaoch go sainráite ar "
"``parser.delete_first_token ()``."

msgid ""
"``CommentNode.render()`` returns an empty string. Anything between ``{% "
"comment %}`` and ``{% endcomment %}`` is ignored."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``CommentNode.render () ``teaghrán folamh ar ais. Déantar neamhaird "
"ar aon rud idir ``{% comment%}`` agus ``{% endcomment%}``."

msgid "Parsing until another block tag, and saving contents"
msgstr "Parsáil go dtí chlib bloc eile, agus ábhar a shábháil"

msgid ""
"In the previous example, ``do_comment()`` discarded everything between ``{% "
"comment %}`` and ``{% endcomment %}``. Instead of doing that, it's possible "
"to do something with the code between block tags."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla roimhe seo, chaith ``do_comment () ``gach rud idir`` {% comment%} "
"``agus`` {% endcomment%} ``. In ionad sin a dhéanamh, is féidir rud éigin a "
"dhéanamh leis an gcód idir clibeanna bloc."

msgid ""
"For example, here's a custom template tag, ``{% upper %}``, that capitalizes "
"everything between itself and ``{% endupper %}``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, seo clib teimpléad saincheaptha, ``{% upper%}``, a chaipitlíonn "
"gach rud eatarthu féin agus ``{% endupper%}``."

msgid "Usage:"
msgstr "Úsáid:"

msgid ""
"As in the previous example, we'll use ``parser.parse()``. But this time, we "
"pass the resulting ``nodelist`` to the ``Node``::"
msgstr ""
"Mar atá sa sampla roimhe seo, úsáidfimid ``parser.parse () ``. Ach an uair "
"seo, cuirimid an `nodelist`` mar thoradh air sin chuig an ``Node``:"

msgid ""
"The only new concept here is the ``self.nodelist.render(context)`` in "
"``UpperNode.render()``."
msgstr ""
"Is é an t-aon choincheap nua anseo an ``self.nodelist.render (comhthéacs) "
"``i `UpperNode.render ()``."

msgid ""
"For more examples of complex rendering, see the source code of :ttag:`{% for "
"%}<for>` in :source:`django/template/defaulttags.py` and :ttag:`{% if %}"
"<if>` in :source:`django/template/smartif.py`."
msgstr ""
"<if>Le haghaidh tuilleadh samplaí de rindreáil casta, féach an cód foinse "
"de:ttag: `{% for%}` in:source: <for>`django/template/defaulttags.py` "
"agus:ttag: `{% if%}` in:source: `django/template/smartif.py`."

msgid "How to delete a Django application"
msgstr "Conas feidhmchlár Django a scriosadh"

msgid ""
"Django provides the ability to group sets of features into Python packages "
"called :doc:`applications</ref/applications/>`. When requirements change, "
"apps may become obsolete or unnecessary. The following steps will help you "
"delete an application safely."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django an cumas tacair gnéithe a ghrúpáil isteach i bpacáistí "
"Python ar a dtugtar : doc: `iarratais</ref/applications/>`. Nuair a "
"athraíonn riachtanais, seans go n-éireoidh aipeanna as feidhm nó nach bhfuil "
"gá leo. Cabhróidh na céimeanna seo a leanas leat feidhmchlár a scriosadh go "
"sábháilte."

msgid "Remove all references to the app (imports, foreign keys etc.)."
msgstr "Bain gach tagairt don aip (allmhairí, eochracha eachtracha srl.)."

msgid "Remove all models from the corresponding ``models.py`` file."
msgstr "Bain gach samhail ón gcomhad comhfhreagrach ``models.py`."

msgid ""
"Create relevant migrations by running :djadmin:`makemigrations`. This step "
"generates a migration that deletes tables for the removed models, and any "
"other required migration for updating relationships connected to those "
"models."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh imirce ábhartha trí rith: djadmin: `makemigrations`. Gineann an "
"chéim seo imirce a scriosann táblaí do na samhlacha bainte, agus aon imirce "
"riachtanach eile chun caidrimh a bhaineann leis na samhlacha sin a nuashonrú."

msgid ""
":ref:`Squash <migration-squashing>` out references to the app in other apps' "
"migrations."
msgstr ""
":ref: `Squash <migration-squashing>`tagairtí don aip in imirce aipeanna eile."

msgid ""
"Apply migrations locally, runs tests, and verify the correctness of your "
"project."
msgstr ""
"Cuir ascnaimh i bhfeidhm go háitiúil, reáchtálann tú tástálacha, agus "
"dearbhaigh cruinneas do thionscadail."

msgid "Deploy/release your updated Django project."
msgstr "Imscar / scaoileadh do thionscadal Django nuashonraithe."

msgid "Remove the app from :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr "Bain an aip ó:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid "Finally, remove the app's directory."
msgstr "Faoi dheireadh, bain eolaire an aip."

msgid "How to use Django with Daphne"
msgstr "Conas Django a úsáid le Daphne"

msgid ""
":pypi:`Daphne <daphne>` is a pure-Python ASGI server for UNIX, maintained by "
"members of the Django project. It acts as the reference server for ASGI."
msgstr ""
":pypi: Is freastalaí <daphne>Pure-python ASGI é `Daphne `do UNIX, arna "
"chothabháil ag baill den tionscadal Django. Feidhmíonn sé mar an fhreastalaí "
"tagartha do ASGI."

msgid "Installing Daphne"
msgstr "Suiteáil Daphne"

msgid "You can install Daphne with ``pip``:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat Daphne a shuiteáil le ``pip``:"

msgid "Running Django in Daphne"
msgstr "Rith Django i Daphne"

msgid ""
"When Daphne is installed, a ``daphne`` command is available which starts the "
"Daphne server process. At its simplest, Daphne needs to be called with the "
"location of a module containing an ASGI application object, followed by what "
"the application is called (separated by a colon)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn Daphne suiteáilte, tá ordú ``daphne`` ar fáil a thosaíonn "
"próiseas freastalaí Daphne. Ag an rud is simplí, ní mór Daphne a ghlaoch le "
"suíomh modúl ina bhfuil réad feidhmchláir ASGI, agus mar a thugtar ar an "
"bhfeidhmchlár ina dhiaidh sin (scartha le colon)."

msgid "For a typical Django project, invoking Daphne would look like:"
msgstr "Maidir le tionscadal tipiciúil Django, bheadh cuma Daphne ag glaoch:"

msgid ""
"This will start one process listening on ``127.0.0.1:8000``. It requires "
"that your project be on the Python path; to ensure that run this command "
"from the same directory as your ``manage.py`` file."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh sé seo tús le próiseas amháin ag éisteacht ar ``127.0.0. 1:8000 ``. "
"Éilíonn sé go mbeidh do thionscadal ar chonair Python; chun a chinntiú go "
"rith an t-ordú seo ón eolaire céanna le do chomhad `manage.py`."

msgid "Integration with ``runserver``"
msgstr "Comhtháthú le ``runserver``"

msgid ""
"Daphne provides a :djadmin:`runserver` command to serve your site under ASGI "
"during development."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Daphne ordú a:djadmin: `runserver` chun freastal ar do shuíomh "
"faoi ASGI le linn na forbartha."

msgid ""
"This can be enabled by adding ``daphne`` to the start of "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` and adding an ``ASGI_APPLICATION`` setting "
"pointing to your ASGI application object::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir é seo a chumasú trí ``daphne`` a chur le tús do :setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS` agus socrú ``ASGI_APPLICATION`` a chur leis ag díriú ar do "
"réad feidhmchláir ASGI::"

msgid "How to use Django with Hypercorn"
msgstr "Conas Django a úsáid le Hypercorn"

msgid ""
"Hypercorn_ is an ASGI server that supports HTTP/1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3 with "
"an emphasis on protocol support."
msgstr ""
"Is freastalaí ASGI é Hypercorn_ a thacaíonn le HTTP/1, HTTP/2, agus HTTP/3 "
"le béim ar thacaíocht prótacal."

msgid "Installing Hypercorn"
msgstr "Suiteáil Hypercorn"

msgid "You can install Hypercorn with ``pip``:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat Hypercorn a shuiteáil le ``pip``:"

msgid "Running Django in Hypercorn"
msgstr "Rith Django i Hypercorn"

msgid ""
"When :pypi:`Hypercorn` is installed, a ``hypercorn`` command is available "
"which runs ASGI applications. Hypercorn needs to be called with the location "
"of a module containing an ASGI application object, followed by what the "
"application is called (separated by a colon)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn: PYPI: `Hypercorn` suiteáilte, tá ordú ``hypercorn`` ar fáil "
"a ritheann feidhmchláir ASGI. Caithfear hypercorn a ghlaoch le suíomh modúl "
"ina bhfuil réad feidhmchláir ASGI, agus mar a thugtar ar an bhfeidhmchlár "
"ina dhiaidh sin (scartha le colon)."

msgid "For a typical Django project, invoking Hypercorn would look like:"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le tionscadal tipiciúil Django, bheadh cuma Hypercorn a ghairm air "
"mar:"

msgid ""
"For more advanced usage, please read the `Hypercorn documentation "
"<Hypercorn_>`_."
msgstr ""
"<Hypercorn_>Le haghaidh úsáide níos airde, léigh an doiciméadú `Hypercorn `_ "
"le do thoil."

msgid "How to deploy with ASGI"
msgstr "Conas a imscaradh le ASGI"

msgid ""
"As well as WSGI, Django also supports deploying on ASGI_, the emerging "
"Python standard for asynchronous web servers and applications."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le WSGI, tacaíonn Django le húsáid ar ASGI_, an caighdeán Python "
"atá ag teacht chun cinn le haghaidh freastalaithe gréasáin agus feidhmchláir "
"asincrónacha."

msgid ""
"Django's :djadmin:`startproject` management command sets up a default ASGI "
"configuration for you, which you can tweak as needed for your project, and "
"direct any ASGI-compliant application server to use."
msgstr ""
"Leagann ordú bainistíochta Django's :djadmin:`startproject` cumraíocht "
"réamhshocraithe ASGI ar bun duit, ar féidir leat a athrú de réir mar is gá "
"do do thionscadal, agus d'fhonn aon fhreastalaí feidhmchláir a chomhlíonann "
"ASGI a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Django includes getting-started documentation for the following ASGI servers:"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django cáipéisíocht tosaithe do na freastalaithe ASGI seo a leanas:"

msgid "The ``application`` object"
msgstr "An réad ```iarrat``"

msgid ""
"Like WSGI, ASGI has you supply an ``application`` callable which the "
"application server uses to communicate with your code. It's commonly "
"provided as an object named ``application`` in a Python module accessible to "
"the server."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le WSGI, soláthraíonn ASGI duit ``feidhmchláir` inghlaoithe a "
"úsáideann an freastalaí feidhmchláir chun cumarsáid a dhéanamh le do chód. "
"Cuirtear é ar fáil go coitianta mar réad darb ainm ``feidhmchlár`` i modúl "
"Python atá inrochtana don fhreastalaí."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`startproject` command creates a file :file:`<project_name>/"
"asgi.py` that contains such an ``application`` callable."
msgstr ""
"<project_name>Cruthaíonn an t-ordú: DjaDmin: `startproject` comhad: `/"
"asgi.py` ina bhfuil `feidhmchlár ```` `` `` `` `` `` `` `ghlaoch."

msgid ""
"It's not used by the development server (``runserver``), but can be used by "
"any ASGI server either in development or in production."
msgstr ""
"Ní úsáideann an freastalaí forbartha é (`runserver ``), ach is féidir le "
"haon freastalaí ASGI é a úsáid i bhforbairt nó i dtáirgeadh."

msgid ""
"ASGI servers usually take the path to the application callable as a string; "
"for most Django projects, this will look like ``myproject.asgi:application``."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth glacann freastalaithe ASGI an cosán chuig an bhfeidhmchlár is "
"féidir glaoch mar shreang; i gcás formhór na dtionscadail Django, beidh cuma "
"“myproject.asgi:application”."

msgid ""
"While Django's default ASGI handler will run all your code in a synchronous "
"thread, if you choose to run your own async handler you must be aware of "
"async-safety."
msgstr ""
"Cé go reáchtálfaidh láimhseálaí réamhshocraithe ASGI Django do chód go léir "
"i snáithe sioncrónach, má roghnaíonn tú do láimhseálaí async féin a "
"reáchtáil caithfidh tú a bheith ar an eolas faoi shábháilteacht async."

msgid ""
"Do not call blocking synchronous functions or libraries in any async code. "
"Django prevents you from doing this with the parts of Django that are not "
"async-safe, but the same may not be true of third-party apps or Python "
"libraries."
msgstr ""
"Ná glaoigh ar bhlocáil feidhmeanna nó leabharlanna sioncrónacha in aon chód "
"async. Cuireann Django cosc ort é seo a dhéanamh leis na codanna de Django "
"nach bhfuil sábháilte go sinc-shábháilte, ach b'fhéidir nach bhfuil an rud "
"céanna fíor maidir le feidhmchláir tríú páirtí nó leabharlanna Python."

msgid "Configuring the settings module"
msgstr "An modúl socruithe a chumrú"

msgid ""
"When the ASGI server loads your application, Django needs to import the "
"settings module — that's where your entire application is defined."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a luchtaíonn freastalaí ASGI d'fheidhmchlár, ní mór do Django an modúl "
"socruithe a iompórtáil - sin an áit a sainmhínítear d'fheidhmchlár iomlán."

msgid ""
"Django uses the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment variable to "
"locate the appropriate settings module. It must contain the dotted path to "
"the settings module. You can use a different value for development and "
"production; it all depends on how you organize your settings."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django athróg timpeallachta: envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` chun "
"an modúl socruithe cuí a aimsiú. Caithfidh an cosán poncanach chuig an modúl "
"socruithe a bheith ann. Is féidir leat luach difriúil a úsáid le haghaidh "
"forbartha agus táirgeachta; braitheann sé ar fad ar an gcaoi a n-eagraíonn "
"tú do shocruithe."

msgid ""
"If this variable isn't set, the default :file:`asgi.py` sets it to "
"``mysite.settings``, where ``mysite`` is the name of your project."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an t-athróg seo socraithe, socraíonn an réamhshocraithe:file: "
"`asgi.py` é go `mysite.settings``, áit a bhfuil `mysite`` ainm do "
"thionscadail."

msgid "Applying ASGI middleware"
msgstr "Middleware ASGI a chur i bhfeidhm"

msgid ""
"To apply ASGI middleware, or to embed Django in another ASGI application, "
"you can wrap Django's ``application`` object in the ``asgi.py`` file. For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Chun middleware ASGI a chur i bhfeidhm, nó chun Django a leabú i "
"bhfeidhmchlár ASGI eile, is féidir leat réad ``feidhmchlár`` Django a "
"fhilleadh sa chomhad ``asgi.py`. Mar shampla::"

msgid "How to use Django with Uvicorn"
msgstr "Conas Django a úsáid le Uvicorn"

msgid ""
"Uvicorn_ is an ASGI server based on ``uvloop`` and ``httptools``, with an "
"emphasis on speed."
msgstr ""
"Is freastalaí ASGI é Uvicorn_ bunaithe ar `uvloop ``agus `httptools``, le "
"béim ar luas."

msgid "Installing Uvicorn"
msgstr "Suiteáil Uvicorn"

msgid "You can install Uvicorn with ``pip``:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat Uvicorn a shuiteáil le ``pip``:"

msgid "Running Django in Uvicorn"
msgstr "Rith Django in Uvicorn"

msgid ""
"When Uvicorn is installed, a ``uvicorn`` command is available which runs "
"ASGI applications. Uvicorn needs to be called with the location of a module "
"containing an ASGI application object, followed by what the application is "
"called (separated by a colon)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shuiteáiltear Uvicorn, tá ordú ``uvicorn ``ar fáil a ritheann "
"feidhmchláir ASGI. Ní mór glaoch ar Uvicorn le suíomh modúl ina bhfuil réad "
"iarratais ASGI, agus mar a thugtar ar an bhfeidhmchlár ina dhiaidh sin "
"(scartha le colon)."

msgid "For a typical Django project, invoking Uvicorn would look like:"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le tionscadal tipiciúil Django, bheadh cuma Uvicorn a thabhairt ar "
"aghaidh:"

msgid ""
"In development mode, you can add ``--reload`` to cause the server to reload "
"any time a file is changed on disk."
msgstr ""
"I mód forbartha, is féidir leat ``--reload ``a chur leis chun go gcuirfidh "
"an freastalaí athluchtú aon uair a athraítear comhad ar an diosca."

msgid ""
"For more advanced usage, please read the `Uvicorn documentation <Uvicorn_>`_."
msgstr ""
"<Uvicorn_>Le haghaidh úsáide níos airde, léigh an doiciméadú `Uvicorn `_ le "
"do thoil."

msgid "Deploying Django using Uvicorn and Gunicorn"
msgstr "Django a imscaradh ag baint úsáide as Uvicorn agus Gunicorn"

msgid ""
"Gunicorn_ is a robust web server that implements process monitoring and "
"automatic restarts. This can be useful when running Uvicorn in a production "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"Is freastalaí láidir gréasáin é Gunicorn_ a chuireann monatóireacht próisis "
"agus atosú uathoibríoch i bhfeidhm. Is féidir leis seo a bheith úsáideach "
"agus Uvicorn á reáchtáil i dtimpeallacht táirgeachta."

msgid "To install Uvicorn and Gunicorn, use the following:"
msgstr ""
"Chun Uvicorn agus Gunicorn a shuiteáil, bain úsáid as na rudaí seo a leanas:"

msgid "Then start Gunicorn using the Uvicorn worker class like this:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin cuir tús le Gunicorn ag baint úsáide as rang oibrithe Uvicorn mar seo:"

msgid "Deployment checklist"
msgstr "Seicliosta imscartha"

msgid ""
"The internet is a hostile environment. Before deploying your Django project, "
"you should take some time to review your settings, with security, "
"performance, and operations in mind."
msgstr ""
"Is timpeallacht naimhde é an t-idirlíon. Sula n-úsáidtear do thionscadal "
"Django, ba cheart duit roinnt ama a thógáil chun do shocruithe a "
"athbhreithniú, agus slándáil, feidhmíocht agus oibríochtaí san áireamh."

msgid ""
"Django includes many :doc:`security features </topics/security>`. Some are "
"built-in and always enabled. Others are optional because they aren't always "
"appropriate, or because they're inconvenient for development. For example, "
"forcing HTTPS may not be suitable for all websites, and it's impractical for "
"local development."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django go leor: doc: `gnéithe slándála' </topics/security>. Tá "
"cuid acu ionsuite agus cumasaithe i gcónaí. Tá daoine eile roghnach toisc "
"nach bhfuil siad oiriúnach i gcónaí, nó toisc go bhfuil siad deacair "
"d'fhorbairt. Mar shampla, b'fhéidir nach mbeidh HTTPS a chur i bhfeidhm "
"oiriúnach do gach suíomh Gréasáin, agus tá sé neamhphraiticiúil d'fhorbairt "
"áitiúil."

msgid ""
"Performance optimizations are another category of trade-offs with "
"convenience. For instance, caching is useful in production, less so for "
"local development. Error reporting needs are also widely different."
msgstr ""
"Is catagóir eile de thrádálacha le háisiúlacht iad barrfheabhsú "
"feidhmíochta. Mar shampla, tá caching úsáideach i dtáirgeadh, níos lú mar "
"sin d'fhorbairt áitiúil. Tá riachtanais tuairiscithe earráidí an-difriúil "
"freisin."

msgid "The following checklist includes settings that:"
msgstr "Cuimsíonn an seicliosta seo a leanas socruithe:"

msgid ""
"must be set properly for Django to provide the expected level of security;"
msgstr ""
"caithfear a shocrú i gceart chun Django an leibhéal slándála a bhfuil súil "
"leis a sholáthar;"

msgid "are expected to be different in each environment;"
msgstr "táthar ag súil go mbeidh difriúil i ngach timpeallacht;"

msgid "enable optional security features;"
msgstr "gnéithe slándála roghnacha a chumasú;"

msgid "enable performance optimizations;"
msgstr "optamú feidhmíochta a chumasú;"

msgid "provide error reporting."
msgstr "tuairisciú earráide ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Many of these settings are sensitive and should be treated as confidential. "
"If you're releasing the source code for your project, a common practice is "
"to publish suitable settings for development, and to use a private settings "
"module for production."
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor de na suíomhanna seo íogair agus ba chóir go ndéileálfaí leo faoi "
"rún. Má tá an cód foinse do do thionscadal á eisiúint agat, is "
"gnáthchleachtas é socruithe oiriúnacha a fhoilsiú le haghaidh forbartha, "
"agus modúl socruithe príobháideacha a úsáid le haghaidh táirgeadh."

msgid "Run ``manage.py check --deploy``"
msgstr "Rith seiceáil ``manage.py --deploy``"

msgid ""
"Some of the checks described below can be automated using the :option:`check "
"--deploy` option. Be sure to run it against your production settings file as "
"described in the option's documentation."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir cuid de na seiceálacha a thuairiscítear thíos a uathoibriú ag "
"baint úsáide as an rogha: rogha: `check --deploy`. Bí cinnte é a rith i "
"gcoinne do chomhad socruithe táirgeachta mar a thuairiscítear i ndoiciméadú "
"an rogha."

msgid "Switch away from ``manage.py runserver``"
msgstr "Athraigh ar shiúl ó ``manage.py runserver``"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`runserver` command is not designed for a production setting. "
"Be sure to switch to a production-ready WSGI or ASGI server. For a few "
"common options, see :doc:`WSGI servers </howto/deployment/wsgi/index>` "
"or :doc:`ASGI servers </howto/deployment/asgi/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Níl an t-ordú :djadmin:`runserver` deartha le haghaidh socrú táirgeachta. Bí "
"cinnte aistriú chuig freastalaí WSGI nó ASGI atá réidh le táirgeadh. Le "
"haghaidh roinnt roghanna coitianta, féach :doc:`freastalaithe WSGI </howto/"
"deployment/wsgi/index>` nó :doc:`freastalaithe ASGI </howto/deployment/asgi/"
"index>`."

msgid "Critical settings"
msgstr "Socruithe criticiúla"

msgid ":setting:`SECRET_KEY`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `SECRET_KEY`"

msgid ""
"**The secret key must be a large random value and it must be kept secret.**"
msgstr ""
"** Caithfidh luach randamach mór a bheith ag an eochair rúnda agus caithfear "
"é a choinneáil faoi rún. **"

msgid ""
"Make sure that the key used in production isn't used anywhere else and avoid "
"committing it to source control. This reduces the number of vectors from "
"which an attacker may acquire the key."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte nach n-úsáidtear an eochair a úsáidtear i dtáirgeadh áit ar bith "
"eile agus seachain é a thiomantas do rialú foinse. Laghdaíonn sé seo líon na "
"veicteoirí óna bhféadfadh ionsaitheoir an eochair a fháil."

msgid ""
"Instead of hardcoding the secret key in your settings module, consider "
"loading it from an environment variable::"
msgstr ""
"In ionad an eochair rúnda i do mhodúl socruithe a chódú, smaoinigh ar é a "
"luchtú ó athróg comhshaoil:"

msgid "or from a file::"
msgstr "nó ó chomhad::"

msgid "If rotating secret keys, you may use :setting:`SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá eochracha rúnda ag rothlú, is féidir leat úsáid a bhaint as:: setting: "
"`SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`::"

msgid ""
"Ensure that old secret keys are removed from ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`` in a "
"timely manner."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go mbaintear sean-eochracha rúnda ó ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`` go "
"tráthúil."

msgid ":setting:`DEBUG`"
msgstr ":socrú: `DEBUG`"

msgid "**You must never enable debug in production.**"
msgstr "** Ní mór duit dífhabhtú a chumasú riamh i dtáirgeadh. **"

msgid ""
"You're certainly developing your project with :setting:`DEBUG = True "
"<DEBUG>`, since this enables handy features like full tracebacks in your "
"browser."
msgstr ""
"Is cinnte go bhfuil do thionscadal á fhorbairt agat le :setting:`DEBUG = "
"Fíor <DEBUG>`, ós rud é go gcumasaíonn sé seo gnéithe úsáideacha ar nós "
"aisrianta iomlána i do bhrabhsálaí."

msgid ""
"For a production environment, though, this is a really bad idea, because it "
"leaks lots of information about your project: excerpts of your source code, "
"local variables, settings, libraries used, etc."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le timpeallacht táirgeachta, áfach, is droch-smaoineamh é seo, toisc "
"go scaiteann sé go leor faisnéise faoi do thionscadal: sleachta de do chód "
"foinse, athróga áitiúla, socruithe, leabharlanna a úsáidtear, srl."

msgid "Environment-specific settings"
msgstr "Socruithe comhshaolshonracha"

msgid ":setting:`ALLOWED_HOSTS`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `ALLOWED_HOSTS`"

msgid ""
"When :setting:`DEBUG = False <DEBUG>`, Django doesn't work at all without a "
"suitable value for :setting:`ALLOWED_HOSTS`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: Socrú: `DEBUG = False <DEBUG>`, ní oibríonn Django ar chor ar bith "
"gan luach oiriúnach do: setting: `ALLOWED_HOSTS`."

msgid ""
"This setting is required to protect your site against some CSRF attacks. If "
"you use a wildcard, you must perform your own validation of the ``Host`` "
"HTTP header, or otherwise ensure that you aren't vulnerable to this category "
"of attacks."
msgstr ""
"Tá an socrú seo ag teastáil chun do shuíomh a chosaint i gcoinne roinnt "
"ionsaithe CSRF. Má úsáideann tú cárta fiáin, ní mór duit do bhailíochtú féin "
"a dhéanamh ar an gceannteideal HTTP ``Host`, nó a chinntiú ar shlí eile nach "
"bhfuil tú leochaileach don chatagóir ionsaithe seo."

msgid ""
"You should also configure the web server that sits in front of Django to "
"validate the host. It should respond with a static error page or ignore "
"requests for incorrect hosts instead of forwarding the request to Django. "
"This way you'll avoid spurious errors in your Django logs (or emails if you "
"have error reporting configured that way). For example, on nginx you might "
"set up a default server to return \"444 No Response\" on an unrecognized "
"host:"
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart duit an freastalaí gréasáin atá suite os comhair Django a chumrú "
"chun an t-óstach a bhailíochtú. Ba chóir dó freagra a thabhairt le "
"leathanach earráide statach nó neamhaird a dhéanamh d'iarratais ar óstaigh "
"míchearta in ionad an iarratas a chur ar aghaidh chuig Ar an mbealach seo "
"seachnóidh tú earráidí bréige i do logaí Django (nó ríomhphoist má tá "
"tuairisciú earráide cumraithe agat ar an mbealach sin). Mar shampla, ar "
"nginx d'fhéadfá freastalaí réamhshocraithe a chur ar bun chun “444 Gan "
"Freagra” a thabhairt ar ais ar óstach neamh-aitheanta:"

msgid ":setting:`CACHES`"
msgstr ": socrú: `CACHES`"

msgid ""
"If you're using a cache, connection parameters may be different in "
"development and in production. Django defaults to per-process :ref:`local-"
"memory caching <local-memory-caching>` which may not be desirable."
msgstr ""
"Má tá taisce á úsáid agat, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh paraiméadair nasc difriúil "
"i bhforbairt agus i dtáirgeadh. <local-memory-caching>Réamhshocraíonn Django "
"ar aghaidh an phróisis: ref: `taiscáil cuimhne áitiúil `nach bhféadfadh a "
"bheith inmhianaithe."

msgid ""
"Cache servers often have weak authentication. Make sure they only accept "
"connections from your application servers."
msgstr ""
"Is minic a bhíonn fíordheimhniú lag ag freastalaithe taisce. Cinntigh nach "
"nglacann siad ach le naisc ó d’fhreastalaithe feidhmchláir."

msgid ":setting:`DATABASES`"
msgstr ":setting: `SONRAÍ SONRAÍ`"

msgid ""
"Database connection parameters are probably different in development and in "
"production."
msgstr ""
"Is dócha go bhfuil paraiméadair nasc bunachar sonraí difriúil i bhforbairt "
"agus i dtáirgeadh."

msgid ""
"Database passwords are very sensitive. You should protect them exactly "
"like :setting:`SECRET_KEY`."
msgstr ""
"Tá pasfhocail bhunachar sonraí an-íogair. Ba chóir duit iad a chosaint go "
"díreach cosúil:setting: `SECRET_KEY`."

msgid ""
"For maximum security, make sure database servers only accept connections "
"from your application servers."
msgstr ""
"Ar mhaithe le slándáil uasta, cinntigh nach nglacann freastalaithe bunachair "
"shonraí ach le naisc ó d’fhreastalaithe feidhmchláir."

msgid "If you haven't set up backups for your database, do it right now!"
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil cúltacaí curtha ar bun agat do do bhunachar sonraí, déan é anois!"

msgid ":setting:`EMAIL_BACKEND` and related settings"
msgstr ":setting: `EMAIL_BACKEND` agus socruithe gaolmhara"

msgid "If your site sends emails, these values need to be set correctly."
msgstr ""
"Má sheolann do shuíomh ríomhphoist, caithfear na luachanna seo a shocrú i "
"gceart."

msgid ""
"By default, Django sends email from webmaster@localhost and root@localhost. "
"However, some mail providers reject email from these addresses. To use "
"different sender addresses, modify the :setting:`DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` "
"and :setting:`SERVER_EMAIL` settings."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, seolann Django ríomhphost ó stiúrthóir gréasáin "
"@localhost agus fréamh @localhost. Mar sin féin, diúltaíonn roinnt "
"soláthraithe ríomhphoist ó na seoltaí seo. Chun seoltaí seoltóra éagsúla a "
"úsáid, modhnaigh socruithe:: `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` agus:setting: "
"`SERVER_EMAIL`."

msgid ":setting:`STATIC_ROOT` and :setting:`STATIC_URL`"
msgstr ":socrú: `STATIC_ROOT` agus:socrú: `STATIC_URL`"

msgid ""
"Static files are automatically served by the development server. In "
"production, you must define a :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` directory "
"where :djadmin:`collectstatic` will copy them."
msgstr ""
"Freastalaíonn an freastalaí forbartha comhaid statacha go huathoibríoch Sa "
"táirgeadh, ní mór duit a: setting: `STATIC_ROOT` eolaire a shainiú ina "
"ndéanfaidh: djadmin: `collectstatic` iad a chóipeáil."

msgid "See :doc:`/howto/static-files/index` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `/howto/static-files/index `le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ":setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` and :setting:`MEDIA_URL`"
msgstr ":socrú: `MEDIA_ROOT` agus:socrú: `MEDIA_URL`"

msgid ""
"Media files are uploaded by your users. They're untrusted! Make sure your "
"web server never attempts to interpret them. For instance, if a user uploads "
"a ``.php`` file, the web server shouldn't execute it."
msgstr ""
"Déanann do úsáideoirí comhaid meán a uaslódáil. Níl iontaofa orthu! Déan "
"cinnte nach ndéanann do fhreastalaí gréasáin iarracht riamh iad a lé Mar "
"shampla, má uaslódálann úsáideoir comhad ``.php``, níor chóir don "
"fhreastalaí gréasáin é a fhorghníomhú."

msgid "Now is a good time to check your backup strategy for these files."
msgstr ""
"Anois is am maith é chun do straitéis chúltaca do na comhaid seo a sheiceáil."

msgid "HTTPS"
msgstr "HTTPS"

msgid ""
"Any website which allows users to log in should enforce site-wide HTTPS to "
"avoid transmitting access tokens in clear. In Django, access tokens include "
"the login/password, the session cookie, and password reset tokens. (You "
"can't do much to protect password reset tokens if you're sending them by "
"email.)"
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart d'aon láithreán gréasáin a ligeann úsáideoirí logáil isteach HTTPS "
"ar fud an láithreáin a fhorfheidhmiú chun comharthaí rochtana a sheachaint I "
"Django, tá comharthaí rochtana an logáil isteach /pasfhocal, an fianán "
"seisiúin, agus comharthaí athshocraithe pasfhocal. (Ní féidir leat mórán a "
"dhéanamh chun comharthaí athshocraithe pasfhocal a chosaint má tá tú ag "
"seoladh trí ríomhphost iad.)"

msgid ""
"Protecting sensitive areas such as the user account or the admin isn't "
"sufficient, because the same session cookie is used for HTTP and HTTPS. Your "
"web server must redirect all HTTP traffic to HTTPS, and only transmit HTTPS "
"requests to Django."
msgstr ""
"Ní leor réimsí íogair ar nós an cuntas úsáideora nó an riarachán a chosaint, "
"toisc go n-úsáidtear an fianán seisiúin céanna le haghaidh HTTP agus HTTPS. "
"Ní mór do fhreastalaí gréasáin gach trácht HTTP a atreorú chuig HTTPS, agus "
"ní mór ach iarratais HTTPS a tharchur chuig Django."

msgid "Once you've set up HTTPS, enable the following settings."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh HTTPS curtha ar bun agat, cumasaigh na socruithe seo a leanas."

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE`"

msgid ""
"Set this to ``True`` to avoid transmitting the CSRF cookie over HTTP "
"accidentally."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh é seo go ``True`` chun an fianán CSRF a tharchur thar HTTP de "
"thaisme a sheachaint."

msgid ":setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE`"
msgstr ":setting: `SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE`"

msgid ""
"Set this to ``True`` to avoid transmitting the session cookie over HTTP "
"accidentally."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh é seo go ``True`` chun an fianán seisiúin a tharchur thar HTTP de "
"thaisme a sheachaint."

msgid "Performance optimizations"
msgstr "Optamú feidhmíochta"

msgid ""
"Setting :setting:`DEBUG = False <DEBUG>` disables several features that are "
"only useful in development. In addition, you can tune the following settings."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe:Socrú: `DEBUG = False <DEBUG>`díchumasaíonn roinnt gnéithe nach "
"bhfuil ach úsáideach i bhforbairt. Ina theannta sin, is féidir leat na "
"socruithe seo a leanas a thiúnadh."

msgid "Sessions"
msgstr "Seisiúin"

msgid ""
"Consider using :ref:`cached sessions <cached-sessions-backend>` to improve "
"performance."
msgstr ""
"<cached-sessions-backend>Smaoinigh ar úsáid: ref: `seisiúin chosaithe `chun "
"feidhmíocht a fheabhsú."

msgid ""
"If using database-backed sessions, regularly :ref:`clear old sessions "
"<clearing-the-session-store>` to avoid storing unnecessary data."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú seisiúin tacaíochta le bunachar sonraí, go rialáil:ref: "
"`seansheisiúin a ghlanadh <clearing-the-session-store>`chun sonraí gan ghá a "
"stóráil."

msgid ":setting:`CONN_MAX_AGE`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `CONN_MAX_AGE`"

msgid ""
"Enabling :ref:`persistent database connections <persistent-database-"
"connections>` can result in a nice speed-up when connecting to the database "
"accounts for a significant part of the request processing time."
msgstr ""
"Cumasach:ref: Is <persistent-database-connections>féidir le `naisc "
"leanúnacha bunachar sonraí `luasú deas a bheith mar thoradh air agus tú ag "
"nascadh leis an mbunachar sonraí mar chuid shuntasach den am próiseála "
"iarratais."

msgid "This helps a lot on virtualized hosts with limited network performance."
msgstr ""
"Cuidíonn sé seo go mór le hóstaigh fíorúlaithe a bhfuil feidhmíocht teoranta "
"líonra acu."

msgid ":setting:`TEMPLATES`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `TEMPLATES`"

msgid ""
"Enabling the cached template loader often improves performance drastically, "
"as it avoids compiling each template every time it needs to be rendered. "
"When :setting:`DEBUG = False <DEBUG>`, the cached template loader is enabled "
"automatically. See :class:`django.template.loaders.cached.Loader` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Is minic a fheabhsaíonn cumasú an lódóir teimpléad taiscéadaithe feidhmíocht "
"go suntasach, mar seachnaíonn sé gach teimpléad a thiomsú gach uair a "
"chaithfear é Nuair: Socrú: `DEBUG = False <DEBUG>`, cumasaítear an lódóir "
"teimpléad taisceáilte go huathoibríoch. Féach: Class: "
"`Django.Template.Loaders.Cached.Loader` le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "Error reporting"
msgstr "Tuairisciú earrá"

msgid ""
"By the time you push your code to production, it's hopefully robust, but you "
"can't rule out unexpected errors. Thankfully, Django can capture errors and "
"notify you accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Faoin am a bhrú tú do chód chuig táirgeadh, tá súil agam go bhfuil sé "
"láidir, ach ní féidir leat earráidí gan choinne a chur in iúl. Ar ámharaí an "
"tsaoil, is féidir le Django earráidí a ghabháil agus fógra duit dá réir."

msgid ":setting:`LOGGING`"
msgstr ": socrú: `LOGGING`"

msgid ""
"Review your logging configuration before putting your website in production, "
"and check that it works as expected as soon as you have received some "
"traffic."
msgstr ""
"Déan athbhreithniú ar do chumraíocht logála sula gcuirfidh tú do shuíomh "
"Gréasáin i dtáirgeadh, agus seiceáil go n-oibríonn sé mar a bhíothas ag súil "
"leis a luaithe a bheidh roinnt tráchta faighte agat."

msgid "See :doc:`/topics/logging` for details on logging."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/topics/loging` le haghaidh sonraí maidir le logáil."

msgid ":setting:`ADMINS` and :setting:`MANAGERS`"
msgstr ": socrú: `ADMINS` agus:socrú: `BAINISTEOIRÍ `"

msgid ":setting:`ADMINS` will be notified of 500 errors by email."
msgstr ":setting: Cuirfear in iúl do `ADMINS` faoi 500 earráid trí ríomhphost."

msgid ""
":setting:`MANAGERS` will be notified of 404 "
"errors. :setting:`IGNORABLE_404_URLS` can help filter out spurious reports."
msgstr ""
":setting: Tabharfar in iúl do `BAINISTEOIR` faoi 404 earráid. :setting: Is "
"féidir le `IGNORABLE_404_URLS` cabhrú le tuarascálacha bréige a scagadh "
"amach."

msgid ""
"See :doc:`/howto/error-reporting` for details on error reporting by email."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `/howto/earror-riarascálach` le haghaidh sonraí maidir le "
"tuairisciú earráide trí ríomhphost."

msgid "Error reporting by email doesn't scale very well"
msgstr "Ní chuireann tuairisciú earráide trí ríomhphost scála an-mhaith"

msgid ""
"Consider using an error monitoring system such as Sentry_ before your inbox "
"is flooded by reports. Sentry can also aggregate logs."
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh ar chóras monatóireachta earráide mar Sentry_ a úsáid sula "
"gcuirtear tuarascálacha faoi thuarascálacha do bhosca isteach. Is féidir le "
"Sentry logaí a chomhiomlánú freisin."

msgid "Customize the default error views"
msgstr "Saincheap na tuairimí earráide réamhshoc"

msgid ""
"Django includes default views and templates for several HTTP error codes. "
"You may want to override the default templates by creating the following "
"templates in your root template directory: ``404.html``, ``500.html``, "
"``403.html``, and ``400.html``. The :ref:`default error views <error-views>` "
"that use these templates should suffice for 99% of web applications, but you "
"can :ref:`customize them <customizing-error-views>` as well."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django radhairc réamhshocraithe agus teimpléid do roinnt cóid "
"earráide HTTP B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat na teimpléid réamhshocraithe a shárú "
"trí na teimpléid seo a leanas a chruthú i d'eolaire teimpléad fréimhe: "
"``404.html``, ``500.html``, ``403.html``, agus ``400.html``. <customizing-"
"error-views>Ba chóir go leor: Ref: `tuairimí earráide réamhshocraithe <error-"
"views>`a úsáideann na teimpléid seo do 99% d'fheidhmchláir gréasáin, ach is "
"féidir leat: ref: `iad a shaincheapadh` freisin."

msgid "How to deploy Django"
msgstr "Conas Django a imscaradh"

msgid ""
"Django is full of shortcuts to make web developers' lives easier, but all "
"those tools are of no use if you can't easily deploy your sites. Since "
"Django's inception, ease of deployment has been a major goal."
msgstr ""
"Tá Django lán le aicearraí chun saol forbróirí gréasáin a dhéanamh níos "
"éasca, ach níl aon úsáid as na huirlisí sin go léir mura féidir leat do "
"shuíomhanna a úsáid go héasca. Ó bunaíodh Django, ba phríomhsprioc é "
"éascaíocht a imscaradh."

msgid ""
"There are many options for deploying your Django application, based on your "
"architecture or your particular business needs, but that discussion is "
"outside the scope of what Django can give you as guidance."
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor roghanna ann chun d'fheidhmchlár Django a imscaradh, bunaithe ar "
"d'ailtireacht nó ar do riachtanais ghnó ar leith, ach tá an plé sin lasmuigh "
"de raon feidhme an méid is féidir le Django a thabhairt duit mar threoir."

msgid ""
"Django, being a web framework, needs a web server in order to operate. And "
"since most web servers don't natively speak Python, we need an interface to "
"make that communication happen. The :djadmin:`runserver` command starts a "
"lightweight development server, which is not suitable for production."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn freastalaí gréasáin ó Django, mar chreat gréasáin, chun oibriú. "
"Agus ós rud é nach labhraíonn mórchuid na bhfreastalaithe gréasáin Python go "
"dúchasach, teastaíonn comhéadan uainn chun an cumarsáid sin a dhéanamh. "
"Cuireann an t-ordú: DJADmin: `runserver` tús le freastalaí forbartha éadrom, "
"nach bhfuil oiriúnach le táirgeadh."

msgid "Django currently supports two interfaces: WSGI and ASGI."
msgstr "Tacaíonn Django le dhá chomhéadan faoi láthair: WSGI agus ASGI."

msgid ""
"`WSGI`_ is the main Python standard for communicating between web servers "
"and applications, but it only supports synchronous code."
msgstr ""
"Is é `WSGI`_ an príomhchaighdeán Python chun cumarsáid a dhéanamh idir "
"freastalaithe gréasáin agus feidhmchláir, ach ní thacaíonn sé ach le cód "
"sioncrónach."

msgid ""
"`ASGI`_ is the new, asynchronous-friendly standard that will allow your "
"Django site to use asynchronous Python features, and asynchronous Django "
"features as they are developed."
msgstr ""
"Is é `ASGI`_ an caighdeán nua, eascrónach atá neamhdhíobhálach a ligfidh do "
"shuíomh Django gnéithe asincrónacha Python, agus gnéithe asincrónacha Django "
"a úsáid de réir mar a fhorbraítear iad."

msgid ""
"You should also consider how you will handle :doc:`static files </howto/"
"static-files/deployment>` for your application, and how to "
"handle :doc:`error reporting</howto/error-reporting>`."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit smaoineamh freisin ar an gcaoi a láimhseálóidh t:doc: `comhaid "
"stataithe' le haghaidh d'iarratais, agus conas a láimhseáil: doc: "
"`tuairisciú earráid` </howto/static-files/deployment></howto/error-"
"reporting>."

msgid ""
"Finally, before you deploy your application to production, you should run "
"through our :doc:`deployment checklist<checklist>` to ensure that your "
"configurations are suitable."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, sula n-imscarann tú d'iarratas ar tháirgeadh, ba cheart duit "
"rith trínár seicliosta imscartha: doc: `chun a chinntiú go <checklist>bhfuil "
"do chumraíochtaí oiriúnach."

msgid "How to authenticate against Django's user database from Apache"
msgstr ""
"Conas fíordheimhniú i gcoinne bunachar sonraí úsáideoirí Django ó Apache"

msgid ""
"Since keeping multiple authentication databases in sync is a common problem "
"when dealing with Apache, you can configure Apache to authenticate against "
"Django's :doc:`authentication system </topics/auth/index>` directly. This "
"requires Apache version >= 2.2 and mod_wsgi >= 2.0. For example, you could:"
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é gur fadhb choitianta í bunachair sonraí fíordheimhnithe iolracha a "
"choinneáil i gcomhréir agus tú ag déileáil le Apache, is féidir leat Apache "
"a chumrú chun fíordheimhniú i gcoinne Django: doc: `córas "
"fíordheimhniúcháin` </topics/auth/index> Éilíonn sé seo leagan Apache > = "
"2.2 agus mod_wsgi > = 2.0. Mar shampla, d'fhéadfá:"

msgid ""
"Serve static/media files directly from Apache only to authenticated users."
msgstr ""
"Freastal ar chomhaid statacha/meán go díreach ó Apache d'úsáideoirí "
"fíordheimhnithe amháin."

msgid ""
"Authenticate access to a Subversion_ repository against Django users with a "
"certain permission."
msgstr ""
"Fíordheimhnigh rochtain ar stór Subversion_ i gcoinne úsáideoirí Django le "
"cead áirithe."

msgid "Allow certain users to connect to a WebDAV share created with mod_dav_."
msgstr ""
"Lig d'úsáideoirí áirithe ceangal le scair WebDAV a cruthaíodh le mod_dav_."

msgid ""
"If you have installed a :ref:`custom user model <auth-custom-user>` and want "
"to use this default auth handler, it must support an ``is_active`` "
"attribute. If you want to use group based authorization, your custom user "
"must have a relation named 'groups', referring to a related object that has "
"a 'name' field. You can also specify your own custom mod_wsgi auth handler "
"if your custom cannot conform to these requirements."
msgstr ""
"Má tá a:ref: `samhail úsáideora saincheaptha <auth-custom-user>`suiteáilte "
"agat agus má theastaíonn uait an láimhseálaí auth réamhshocraithe seo a "
"úsáid, caithfidh sé tacú le tréith ``is_active``. Más mian leat údarú "
"grúpbhunaithe a úsáid, caithfidh caidreamh ainmnithe 'grúpaí' a bheith ag "
"d'úsáideoir saincheaptha, ag tagairt do réad gaolmhar a bhfuil réimse 'ainm' "
"aige. Is féidir leat do láimhseálaí auth mod_wsgi saincheaptha féin a shonrú "
"mura féidir le do saincheaptha cloí leis na riachtanais seo."

msgid "Authentication with ``mod_wsgi``"
msgstr "Fíordheimhniú le ``mod_wsgi``"

msgid ""
"The use of ``WSGIApplicationGroup %{GLOBAL}`` in the configurations below "
"presumes that your Apache instance is running only one Django application. "
"If you are running more than one Django application, please refer to the "
"`Defining Application Groups`_ section of the mod_wsgi docs for more "
"information about this setting."
msgstr ""
"Le húsáid ``WSGIApplicationGroup %{GLOBAL}`` sna cumraíochtaí thíos, glacann "
"sé leis nach bhfuil ach feidhmchlár Django amháin á rith ag do shampla "
"Apache. Má tá níos mó ná feidhmchlár Django amháin á rith agat, féach le do "
"thoil don rannán `Grúpaí Feidhmchláir a Shainmhíniú`_ sna doiciméid mod_wsgi "
"chun tuilleadh eolais a fháil faoin socrú seo."

msgid ""
"Make sure that mod_wsgi is installed and activated and that you have "
"followed the steps to set up :doc:`Apache with mod_wsgi </howto/deployment/"
"wsgi/modwsgi>`."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go bhfuil mod_wsgi suiteáilte agus gníomhachtaithe agus gur lean "
"tú na céimeanna chun bunú:doc: `Apache le mod_</howto/deployment/wsgi/"
"modwsgi> wsgi`."

msgid ""
"Next, edit your Apache configuration to add a location that you want only "
"authenticated users to be able to view:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cuir do chumraíocht Apache in eagar chun suíomh a chur leis nach "
"dteastaíonn uait nach mbeidh ach úsáideoirí fíordheimhnithe in ann a "
"fheiceáil:"

msgid ""
"The ``WSGIAuthUserScript`` directive tells mod_wsgi to execute the "
"``check_password`` function in specified wsgi script, passing the user name "
"and password that it receives from the prompt. In this example, the "
"``WSGIAuthUserScript`` is the same as the ``WSGIScriptAlias`` that defines "
"your application :doc:`that is created by django-admin startproject </howto/"
"deployment/wsgi/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn an treoir ``wsgiauthuserscript`` do mod_wsgi an fheidhm "
"``check_password`` a fhorghníomhú i script wsgi sonraithe, ag dul ar aghaidh "
"an ainm úsáideora agus an pasfhocal a fhaigheann sé ón pras. Sa sampla seo, "
"tá an `WSGIAuthUserScript`` mar an gcéanna leis an ``WSGIScriptalias`` a "
"shainmhíníonn d'iarratas:doc: `atá cru</howto/deployment/wsgi/index> thaithe "
"ag django-admin startproject`."

msgid "Using Apache 2.2 with authentication"
msgstr "Apache 2.2 a úsáid le fíordheimhniú"

msgid "Make sure that ``mod_auth_basic`` and ``mod_authz_user`` are loaded."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go bhfuil `mod_auth_basic`` agus ``mod_authz_user`` luchtaithe."

msgid ""
"These might be compiled statically into Apache, or you might need to use "
"LoadModule to load them dynamically in your ``httpd.conf``:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfaí iad seo a thiomsú go statach i Apache, nó b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort "
"LoadModule a úsáid chun iad a luchtú go dinimiciúil i do `httpd.conf``:"

msgid ""
"Finally, edit your WSGI script ``mysite.wsgi`` to tie Apache's "
"authentication to your site's authentication mechanisms by importing the "
"``check_password`` function::"
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, cuir do script WSGI ``mysite.wsgi`` in eagar chun "
"fíordheimhniú Apache a cheangal le meicníochtaí fíordheimhnithe do shuíomh "
"tríd an fheidhm ``check_password`` a allmhairiú:"

msgid ""
"Requests beginning with ``/secret/`` will now require a user to authenticate."
msgstr ""
"Beidh iarratais a thosaíonn le ``/rúdaí/`` éilíonn úsáideoir a "
"fhíordheimhniú anois."

msgid ""
"The mod_wsgi `access control mechanisms documentation`_ provides additional "
"details and information about alternative methods of authentication."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn mod_wsgi `doiciméadú meicníochtaí rialaithe rochtaine`_ sonraí "
"agus faisnéis bhreise faoi mhodhanna malartacha fíordheimhnithe."

msgid "Authorization with ``mod_wsgi`` and Django groups"
msgstr "Údarú le grúpaí `mod_wsgi`` agus Django"

msgid ""
"mod_wsgi also provides functionality to restrict a particular location to "
"members of a group."
msgstr ""
"cuireann mod_wsgi feidhmiúlacht ar fáil freisin chun suíomh ar leith a "
"theorannú do bhaill ghrúpa."

msgid "In this case, the Apache configuration should look like this:"
msgstr "Sa chás seo, ba chóir go mbeadh cuma seo ar chumraíocht Apache:"

msgid ""
"To support the ``WSGIAuthGroupScript`` directive, the same WSGI script "
"``mysite.wsgi`` must also import the ``groups_for_user`` function which "
"returns a list groups the given user belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Chun tacú leis an treoir ``WSGIAuthGroupScript``, ní mór don script WSGI "
"céanna ``mysite.wsgi`` an fheidhm ``groups_for_user`` a iompórtáil freisin a "
"thugann liosta grúpaí leis an úsáideoir ar leith."

msgid ""
"Requests for ``/secret/`` will now also require user to be a member of the "
"\"secret-agents\" group."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn iarratais ar ``/rúna/`` anois an t-úsáideoir a bheith ina bhall den "
"ghrúpa “gníomhairí rúnaimh”."

msgid "How to use Django with Gunicorn"
msgstr "Conas Django a úsáid le Gunicorn"

msgid ""
"Gunicorn_ ('Green Unicorn') is a pure-Python WSGI server for UNIX. It has no "
"dependencies and can be installed using ``pip``."
msgstr ""
"Is freastalaí WSGI Pure-python do UNIX é Gunicorn_ ('Green Unicorn'). Níl "
"aon spleáchais aige agus is féidir é a shuiteáil ag baint úsáide as ``pip``."

msgid "Installing Gunicorn"
msgstr "Gunicorn a shuiteáil"

msgid ""
"Install gunicorn by running ``python -m pip install gunicorn``. For more "
"details, see the `gunicorn documentation`_."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil gunicorn trí ``python -m pip install gunicorn ``a reáchtáil. Le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadú “gunicorn” _."

msgid "Running Django in Gunicorn as a generic WSGI application"
msgstr "Rith Django i Gunicorn mar fheidhmchlár cineálach WSGI"

msgid ""
"When Gunicorn is installed, a ``gunicorn`` command is available which starts "
"the Gunicorn server process. The simplest invocation of gunicorn is to pass "
"the location of a module containing a WSGI application object named "
"``application``, which for a typical Django project would look like:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shuiteáiltear Gunicorn, tá ordú ``gunicorn`` ar fáil a thosaíonn "
"próiseas freastalaí Gunicorn. Is é an t-ainmniú is simplí ar gunicorn ná "
"suíomh modúl ina bhfuil réad feidhmchláir WSGI darb ainm ``feidhmchlár`` a "
"bheadh chuma air le haghaidh tipiciúil thionscadal Django:"

msgid ""
"This will start one process running one thread listening on "
"``127.0.0.1:8000``. It requires that your project be on the Python path; the "
"simplest way to ensure that is to run this command from the same directory "
"as your ``manage.py`` file."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh sé seo tús le próiseas amháin ag rith éisteacht snáithe amháin ar "
"``127.0.0. 1:8000 ``. Éilíonn sé go mbeadh do thionscadal ar chonair Python; "
"is é an bealach is simplí chun é sin a chinntiú ná an t-ordú seo a reáchtáil "
"ón eolaire céanna le do chomhad `manage.py`."

msgid "See Gunicorn's `deployment documentation`_ for additional tips."
msgstr "Féach “doiciméadú imscartha” _ Gunicorn le haghaidh leideanna breise."

msgid "How to deploy with WSGI"
msgstr "Conas a imscaradh le WSGI"

msgid ""
"Django's primary deployment platform is WSGI_, the Python standard for web "
"servers and applications."
msgstr ""
"Is é príomh-ardán imscartha Django ná WSGI_, caighdeán Python le haghaidh "
"freastalaithe gréasáin agus feidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"Django's :djadmin:`startproject` management command sets up a minimal "
"default WSGI configuration for you, which you can tweak as needed for your "
"project, and direct any WSGI-compliant application server to use."
msgstr ""
"Leagann ordú bainistíochta Django's :djadmin:`startproject` cumraíocht "
"réamhshocraithe WSGI ar bun duit, ar féidir leat a athrú de réir mar is gá "
"do do thionscadal, agus aon fhreastalaí feidhmchláir a chomhlíonann WSGI a "
"threorú chun é a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Django includes getting-started documentation for the following WSGI servers:"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django cáipéisíocht tosaithe do na freastalaithe WSGI seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The key concept of deploying with WSGI is the ``application`` callable which "
"the application server uses to communicate with your code. It's commonly "
"provided as an object named ``application`` in a Python module accessible to "
"the server."
msgstr ""
"Is é an príomhchoincheap a bhaineann le húsáid le WSGI an ``feidhmchláir "
"``is féidir a ghlaoch a úsáideann an freastalaí feidhmchláir chun cumarsáid "
"a dhéanamh le do chód. Cuirtear é ar fáil go coitianta mar réad darb ainm "
"``feidhmchlár`` i modúl Python atá inrochtana don fhreastalaí."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`startproject` command creates a file :file:`<project_name>/"
"wsgi.py` that contains such an ``application`` callable."
msgstr ""
"<project_name>Cruthaíonn an t-ordú: DjaDmin: `startproject` comhad: `/"
"wsgi.py` ina bhfuil `feidhmchlár ```` `` `` `` `` `` `` `ghlaoch."

msgid ""
"It's used both by Django's development server and in production WSGI "
"deployments."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann freastalaí forbartha Django é agus in imscaradh WSGI táirgeachta."

msgid ""
"WSGI servers obtain the path to the ``application`` callable from their "
"configuration. Django's built-in server, namely the :djadmin:`runserver` "
"command, reads it from the :setting:`WSGI_APPLICATION` setting. By default, "
"it's set to ``<project_name>.wsgi.application``, which points to the "
"``application`` callable in :file:`<project_name>/wsgi.py`."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann freastalaithe WSGI an cosán chuig an ``feidhmchlár ``is féidir a "
"ghlaoch óna gcumraíocht. Léann freastalaí ionsuite Django, eadhon an t-"
"ordú:djadmin: `runserver`, é ón socrú: setting: `WSGI_APPLICATION`. "
"<project_name>De réir réamhshocraithe, tá sé socraithe go "
"``<project_name>.wsgi.application``, a thugann in iúl don ``feidhmchlár`` is "
"féidir glaoch in:file: `/wsgi.py`."

msgid ""
"When the WSGI server loads your application, Django needs to import the "
"settings module — that's where your entire application is defined."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a luchtaíonn freastalaí WSGI d'iarratas, ní mór do Django an modúl "
"socruithe a iompórtáil - sin an áit a sainmhínítear d'fheidhmchlár iomlán."

msgid ""
"If this variable isn't set, the default :file:`wsgi.py` sets it to "
"``mysite.settings``, where ``mysite`` is the name of your project. That's "
"how :djadmin:`runserver` discovers the default settings file by default."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an t-athróg seo socraithe, socraíonn an réamhshocraithe:file: "
"`wsgi.py` é go `mysite.settings``, áit a bhfuil `mysite`` ainm do "
"thionscadail. Sin mar a aimsíonn: djadmin: `runserver` an comhad socruithe "
"réamhshocraithe de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Since environment variables are process-wide, this doesn't work when you run "
"multiple Django sites in the same process. This happens with mod_wsgi."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhfuil athróga comhshaoil ar fud an phróisis, ní oibríonn sé seo "
"nuair a reáchtáil tú suíomhanna iolracha Django sa phróiseas cé Tarlaíonn sé "
"seo le mod_wsgi."

msgid ""
"To avoid this problem, use mod_wsgi's daemon mode with each site in its own "
"daemon process, or override the value from the environment by enforcing "
"``os.environ[\"DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE\"] = \"mysite.settings\"`` in "
"your :file:`wsgi.py`."
msgstr ""
"Chun an fhadhb seo a sheachaint, bain úsáid as mod_wsgi mod_wsgi le gach "
"suíomh ina phróiseas daemon féin, nó athsháraigh an luach ón timpeallacht "
"trí ``os.environ [\"DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE\"] = “mysite.settings\"` i "
"d:file: `wsgi.py` a chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid "Applying WSGI middleware"
msgstr "Middleware WSGI a chur i bhfeidhm"

msgid ""
"To apply :pep:`WSGI middleware <3333#middleware-components-that-play-both-"
"sides>` you can wrap the application object. For instance you could add "
"these lines at the bottom of :file:`wsgi.py`::"
msgstr ""
"<3333 #middleware -components-that-play-both-sides>Chun iarratas a dhéanamh: "
"pep: `Middleware WSGI` is féidir leat an réad feidhmchláir a fhilleadh. Mar "
"shampla d'fhéadfá na línte seo a chur leis ag bun de:file: `wsgi.py`::"

msgid ""
"You could also replace the Django WSGI application with a custom WSGI "
"application that later delegates to the Django WSGI application, if you want "
"to combine a Django application with a WSGI application of another framework."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfá feidhmchlár saincheaptha WSGI a chur in ionad feidhmchlár Django "
"WSGI a thosclaíonn chuig feidhmchlár Django WSGI níos déanaí, más mian leat "
"feidhmchlár Django a chomhcheangal le feidhmchlár WSGI de chreat eile."

msgid "How to use Django with Apache and ``mod_wsgi``"
msgstr "Conas Django a úsáid le Apache agus ``mod_wsgi``"

msgid ""
"Deploying Django with Apache_ and `mod_wsgi`_ is a tried and tested way to "
"get Django into production."
msgstr ""
"Is bealach trialaithe é Django a imscaradh le Apache_ agus `mod_wsgi`_ chun "
"Django a chur i dtáirgeadh."

msgid ""
"mod_wsgi is an Apache module which can host any Python WSGI_ application, "
"including Django. Django will work with any version of Apache which supports "
"mod_wsgi."
msgstr ""
"mod_wsgi is modúl Apache é is féidir a óstáil ar aon iarratas Python WSGI_, "
"lena n-áirítear Django. Oibreoidh Django le haon leagan de Apache a "
"thacaíonn mod_wsgi."

msgid ""
"The `official mod_wsgi documentation`_ is your source for all the details "
"about how to use mod_wsgi. You'll probably want to start with the "
"`installation and configuration documentation`_."
msgstr ""
"Is é an `doiciméadú oifigiúil mod_wsgi`_ do fhoinse le haghaidh na sonraí go "
"léir faoi conas mod_wsgi a úsáid. Is dócha go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh tús a "
"chur leis an “doiciméadú suiteála agus cumraíochta” _."

msgid "Basic configuration"
msgstr "Cumraíocht bunúsach"

msgid ""
"Once you've got mod_wsgi installed and activated, edit your Apache server's "
"`httpd.conf`_ file and add the following."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh mod_wsgi suiteáilte agus gníomhachtaithe agat, cuir in eagar "
"comhad `httpd.conf`_ do fhreastalaí Apache agus cuir an méid seo a leanas "
"leis."

msgid ""
"The first bit in the ``WSGIScriptAlias`` line is the base URL path you want "
"to serve your application at (``/`` indicates the root url), and the second "
"is the location of a \"WSGI file\" -- see below -- on your system, usually "
"inside of your project package (``mysite`` in this example). This tells "
"Apache to serve any request below the given URL using the WSGI application "
"defined in that file."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad ghiotán sa líne `WSGIScriptalias`` an bunchosán URL ar mhaith "
"leat freastal ar d'iarratas (``/`` léiríonn an url fréimhe), agus is é an "
"dara ceann suíomh “comhad WSGI” - féach thíos - ar do chóras, de ghnáth "
"taobh istigh de do phacáiste tionscadail (``mysite`` sa sampla seo). Insíonn "
"sé seo le Apache aon iarratas faoi bhun an URL tugtha ag baint úsáide as an "
"bhfeidhmchlár WSGI atá sainmhínithe sa chomhad sin."

msgid ""
"If you install your project's Python dependencies inside a :mod:`virtual "
"environment <venv>`, add the path using ``WSGIPythonHome``. See the "
"`mod_wsgi virtual environment guide`_ for more details."
msgstr ""
"Má shuiteálann tú spleáchas Python do thionscadail taobh istigh de a:mod: "
"`timpeallacht fhíorúil`, cuir an cosán leis ag b <venv>aint úsáide as "
"``wsgipythonhome``. Féach an treoir timpeallachta fíorúil `mod_wsgi`_ le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The ``WSGIPythonPath`` line ensures that your project package is available "
"for import on the Python path; in other words, that ``import mysite`` works."
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn an líne `WSgipythonPath`` go bhfuil do phacáiste tionscadail ar "
"fáil le hallmhairiú ar an gcosán Python; i bhfocail eile, go n-oibríonn "
"``allmhairiú mysite``."

msgid ""
"The ``<Directory>`` piece ensures that Apache can access "
"your :file:`wsgi.py` file."
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn an píosa <Directory>```gur féidir le Apache rochtain a fháil ar do "
"chomhad:file: `wsgi.py`."

msgid ""
"Next we'll need to ensure this :file:`wsgi.py` with a WSGI application "
"object exists. As of Django version 1.4, :djadmin:`startproject` will have "
"created one for you; otherwise, you'll need to create it. See the :doc:`WSGI "
"overview documentation</howto/deployment/wsgi/index>` for the default "
"contents you should put in this file, and what else you can add to it."
msgstr ""
"Ansin beidh orainn a chinntiú go bhfuil sé seo: file: `wsgi.py` le réad "
"feidhmchláir WSGI ann. Maidir le leagan Django 1.4, beidh ceann cruthaithe "
"ag: djadmin: `startproject` duit; ar shlí eile, beidh ort é a chruthú. Féach "
"na:doc: `Doiciméadú forbhreathnaithe WSGI` maidir</howto/deployment/wsgi/"
"index> leis an ábhar réamhshocraithe ba chóir duit a chur sa chomhad seo, "
"agus cad eile is féidir leat a chur leis."

msgid ""
"If multiple Django sites are run in a single mod_wsgi process, all of them "
"will use the settings of whichever one happens to run first. This can be "
"solved by changing::"
msgstr ""
"Má reáchtáiltear suíomhanna iolracha Django i bpróiseas mod_wsgi amháin, "
"úsáidfidh gach ceann acu socruithe cibé acu a tharlaíonn a rith ar dtús. Is "
"féidir é seo a réiteach trí athrú:"

msgid "in ``wsgi.py``, to::"
msgstr "i `wsgi.py``, chuig:"

msgid ""
"or by :ref:`using mod_wsgi daemon mode<daemon-mode>` and ensuring that each "
"site runs in its own daemon process."
msgstr ""
"or by:ref: `ag baint úsáide as mod_wsgi daemon mod_wsgi <daemon-mode>`agus a "
"chinntiú go ritheann gach suíomh ina phróiseas daemon féin."

msgid "Fixing ``UnicodeEncodeError`` for file uploads"
msgstr "Socrú ``UnicodeEncodeError`` le haghaidh uaslódála comhad"

msgid ""
"If you get a ``UnicodeEncodeError`` when uploading or writing files with "
"file names or content that contains non-ASCII characters, make sure Apache "
"is configured to support UTF-8 encoding:"
msgstr ""
"Má fhaigheann tú ``UnicodeEncodeError`` agus comhaid á uaslódáil nó ag "
"scríobh le hainmneacha comhaid nó ábhar ina bhfuil carachtair neamh-ASCII, "
"déan cinnte go bhfuil Apache cumraithe chun tacú le hionchódú UTF-8:"

msgid ""
"A common location to put this configuration is ``/etc/apache2/envvars``."
msgstr ""
"Suíomh coitianta chun an chumraíocht seo a chur ná ``/etc/apache2/envvars``."

msgid ""
"Alternatively, if you are :ref:`using mod_wsgi daemon mode<daemon-mode>` you "
"can add ``lang`` and ``locale`` options to the ``WSGIDaemonProcess`` "
"directive:"
msgstr ""
"De rogha air sin, más t:ref: `ag baint úsáide as mod_wsgi daemon mod_wsgi "
"`is <daemon-mode>féidir leat roghanna ``lang`` agus ``locale`` a chur leis "
"an treoir ``WsgiDaemonProcess ``:"

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`unicode-files` section of the Unicode reference guide for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Féach an ranna:ref: `unicode-files` den treoir tagartha Unicode le haghaidh "
"sonraí."

msgid "Using ``mod_wsgi`` daemon mode"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as modh daemon ``mod_wsgi``"

msgid ""
"\"Daemon mode\" is the recommended mode for running mod_wsgi (on non-Windows "
"platforms). To create the required daemon process group and delegate the "
"Django instance to run in it, you will need to add appropriate "
"``WSGIDaemonProcess`` and ``WSGIProcessGroup`` directives. A further change "
