"use ``WSGIPythonPath``; instead you should use the ``python-path`` option to "
"``WSGIDaemonProcess``, for example:"
msgstr ""
"Is é “mód Daemon” an modh a mholtar chun mod_wsgi a reáchtáil (ar ardáin "
"neamh-Windows). Chun an grúpa próiseas daemon riachtanach a chruthú agus an "
"sampla Django a tharmligean chun rith ann, beidh ort treoracha "
"``WSGidaemonProcess ``agus `WSGIProcessGroup`` cuí a chur leis. Athrú eile "
"atá ag teastáil ar an gcumraíocht thuas má úsáideann tú modh daemon ná nach "
"féidir leat ``wsgipythonpath`` a úsáid; ina ionad sin ba chóir duit an rogha "
"``python-path`` a úsáid chun `WsgidaemonProcess ``, mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"If you want to serve your project in a subdirectory (``https://example.com/"
"mysite`` in this example), you can add ``WSGIScriptAlias`` to the "
"configuration above:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat freastal ar do thionscadal i bhfo-eolaire (``https://"
"example.com/mysite`` sa sampla seo), is féidir leat ``WSGiscriptalias`` a "
"chur leis an gcumraíocht thuas:"

msgid ""
"See the official mod_wsgi documentation for `details on setting up daemon "
"mode`_."
msgstr ""
"Féach an doiciméadú oifigiúil mod_wsgi le haghaidh `sonraí maidir le mód "
"daemon a bhunú `_."

msgid "Serving files"
msgstr "Comhad a sheirbheáil"

msgid ""
"Django doesn't serve files itself; it leaves that job to whichever web "
"server you choose."
msgstr ""
"Ní fhreastalaíonn Django ar chomhaid féin; fágann sé an post sin do cibé "
"freastalaí gréasáin a roghnaíonn tú."

msgid ""
"We recommend using a separate web server -- i.e., one that's not also "
"running Django -- for serving media. Here are some good choices:"
msgstr ""
"Molaimid freastalaí gréasáin ar leithligh a úsáid - ie, ceann nach bhfuil "
"Django á rith freisin - chun freastalaí ar na meáin a sheirbheáil. Seo "
"roinnt roghanna maithe:"

msgid "Nginx_"
msgstr "Nginx_"

msgid "A stripped-down version of Apache_"
msgstr "Leagan scriostha de Apache_"

msgid ""
"If, however, you have no option but to serve media files on the same Apache "
"``VirtualHost`` as Django, you can set up Apache to serve some URLs as "
"static media, and others using the mod_wsgi interface to Django."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil aon rogha agat, áfach, ach comhaid meán a sheirbheáil ar an "
"Apache ``VirtualHost`` céanna le Django, is féidir leat Apache a chur ar bun "
"chun roinnt URLanna a sheirbheáil mar mheáin statacha, agus cuid eile ag "
"baint úsáide as an comhéadan mod_wsgi chuig Django."

msgid ""
"This example sets up Django at the site root, but serves ``robots.txt``, "
"``favicon.ico``, and anything in the ``/static/`` and ``/media/`` URL space "
"as a static file. All other URLs will be served using mod_wsgi:"
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an sampla seo Django ag fréamh an láithreáin, ach freastalaíonn sé "
"ar `robots.txt``, `favicon.ico', agus aon rud sa spás URL ``/static/`` agus "
"``/media/`` mar chomhad statach. Freastalfar gach URL eile ag baint úsáide "
"as mod_wsgi:"

msgid "Serving the admin files"
msgstr "Freastal ar na comhaid riaracháin"

msgid ""
"When :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` is in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, the "
"Django development server automatically serves the static files of the admin "
"app (and any other installed apps). This is however not the case when you "
"use any other server arrangement. You're responsible for setting up Apache, "
"or whichever web server you're using, to serve the admin files."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn: MOD: `django.contrib.staticfiles` in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`, freastalaíonn freastalaí forbartha Django go huathoibríoch "
"ar chomhaid statacha an aip riaracháin (agus aon aipeanna suiteáilte eile). "
"Ní hé seo an cás áfach nuair a úsáideann tú aon socrú freastalaí eile. Tá tú "
"freagrach as Apache a bhunú, nó cibé freastalaí gréasáin atá á úsáid agat, "
"chun freastal ar na comhaid riaracháin."

msgid ""
"The admin files live in (:source:`django/contrib/admin/static/admin`) of the "
"Django distribution."
msgstr ""
"Tá na comhaid riaracháin ina gcónaí i (:source: `django/contrib/admin/static/"
"admin `) den dáileadh Django."

msgid ""
"We **strongly** recommend using :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` to handle "
"the admin files (along with a web server as outlined in the previous "
"section; this means using the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command to "
"collect the static files in :setting:`STATIC_ROOT`, and then configuring "
"your web server to serve :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` at :setting:`STATIC_URL`), "
"but here are three other approaches:"
msgstr ""
"Molaimid **láidre** úsáid: mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles` chun na comhaid "
"riaracháin a láimhseáil (in éineacht le freastalaí gréasáin mar a leagtar "
"amach sa chuid roimhe seo; ciallaíonn sé seo an t-ordú bainistíochta: "
"djadmin: `collectstatic` a úsáid chun na comhaid statacha a bhailiú "
"in:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`, agus ansin do fhreastalaí gréasáin a chumrú chun "
"socrú: `STATIC_ROOT`: `STATIC_URL`), ach seo trí chur chuige eile:"

msgid ""
"Create a symbolic link to the admin static files from within your document "
"root (this may require ``+FollowSymLinks`` in your Apache configuration)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh nasc siombalach leis na comhaid statacha riaracháin ó laistigh de "
"fhréamh do dhoiciméad (d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh `+FollowSymlinks`` ag teastáil "
"air seo i do chumraíocht Apache)."

msgid ""
"Use an ``Alias`` directive, as demonstrated above, to alias the appropriate "
"URL (probably :setting:`STATIC_URL` + ``admin/``) to the actual location of "
"the admin files."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid treoir ``Alias``, mar a léirítear thuas, chun an URL iomchuí "
"(b'fhéidir: socrú: `STATIC_URL` + ``admin/``) a aithris chuig suíomh iarbhír "
"na gcomhaid riaracháin."

msgid ""
"Copy the admin static files so that they live within your Apache document "
"root."
msgstr ""
"Cóipeáil na comhaid statacha riaracháin ionas go gcónaíonn siad laistigh de "
"fhréamh doiciméad Apache."

msgid "Authenticating against Django's user database from Apache"
msgstr "Fíordheimhniú i gcoinne bunachar sonraí úsáideoirí Django ó Apache"

msgid ""
"Django provides a handler to allow Apache to authenticate users directly "
"against Django's authentication backends. See the :doc:`mod_wsgi "
"authentication documentation </howto/deployment/wsgi/apache-auth>`."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django láimhseálaí chun ligean Apache úsáideoirí a "
"fhíordheimhniú go díreach i gcoinne cúltaca fíordheimhnithe Django. Féach "
"na:doc: `doiciméadú fíordheimhnithe mod_wsgi` </howto/deployment/wsgi/apache-"
"auth>."

msgid "How to use Django with uWSGI"
msgstr "Conas Django a úsáid le UWSgi"

msgid ""
"uWSGI_ is a fast, self-healing and developer/sysadmin-friendly application "
"container server coded in pure C."
msgstr ""
"uWSGI_ is freastalaí coimeádán feidhmchláir thapa, féin-leighis agus "
"cairdiúil don fhorbróir/sysadmin atá códaithe i C íon."

msgid ""
"The uWSGI docs offer a `tutorial`_ covering Django, nginx, and uWSGI (one "
"possible deployment setup of many). The docs below are focused on how to "
"integrate Django with uWSGI."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann doiciméid UwsGi `teagaisc `_ ar fáil a chlúdaíonn Django, nginx, "
"agus UWSgi (socrú imscartha féideartha amháin de go leor). Tá na doiciméid "
"thíos dírithe ar conas Django a chomhtháthú le UWSGI."

msgid "Prerequisite: uWSGI"
msgstr "Réamhriachtanas: UwsGi"

msgid ""
"The uWSGI wiki describes several `installation procedures`_. Using pip, the "
"Python package manager, you can install any uWSGI version with a single "
"command. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Déanann wiki UwsGi cur síos ar roinnt `nósanna imeachta suiteálaí`_. Ag "
"baint úsáide as pip, bainisteoir pacáiste Python, is féidir leat aon leagan "
"uwsGi a shuiteáil le hordú amháin. Mar shampla:"

msgid "uWSGI model"
msgstr "múnla uWSGI"

msgid ""
"uWSGI operates on a client-server model. Your web server (e.g., nginx, "
"Apache) communicates with a ``django-uwsgi`` \"worker\" process to serve "
"dynamic content."
msgstr ""
"feidhmíonn uWSGI ar mhúnla cliant-freastalaí. Déanann do fhreastalaí "
"gréasáin (m.sh., nginx, Apache) cumarsáid le próiseas `` django-uwsgi`` "
"\"oibrí\" chun freastal ar ábhar dinimiciúil."

msgid "Configuring and starting the uWSGI server for Django"
msgstr "An freastalaí UWSgi a chumrú agus a thosú do Django"

msgid ""
"uWSGI supports multiple ways to configure the process. See uWSGI's "
"`configuration documentation`_."
msgstr ""
"tacaíonn uWSGI le bealaí éagsúla chun an próiseas a chumrú. Féach ar "
"`dhoiciméadúchán cumraíochta`_ uWSGI."

msgid "Here's an example command to start a uWSGI server:"
msgstr "Seo ordú samplach chun freastalaí UWSgi a thosú:"

msgid ""
"This assumes you have a top-level project package named ``mysite``, and "
"within it a module :file:`mysite/wsgi.py` that contains a WSGI "
"``application`` object. This is the layout you'll have if you ran ``django-"
"admin startproject mysite`` (using your own project name in place of "
"``mysite``) with a recent version of Django. If this file doesn't exist, "
"you'll need to create it. See the :doc:`/howto/deployment/wsgi/index` "
"documentation for the default contents you should put in this file and what "
"else you can add to it."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé leis seo go bhfuil pacáiste tionscadail barrleibhéil agat darb "
"ainm ``mysite``, agus laistigh de modúl:file: `mysite/wsgi.py` ina bhfuil "
"réad WSGI ``application``. Seo an leagan amach a bheidh agat má rith tú "
"``django-admin startproject mysite`` (ag baint úsáide as d'ainm tionscadail "
"féin in ionad ``mysite``) le leagan le déanaí de Django. Mura bhfuil an "
"comhad seo ann, beidh ort é a chruthú. Féach an doiciméad:doc: `/howto/"
"deployment/wsgi/index` don ábhar réamhshocraithe ba chóir duit a chur sa "
"chomhad seo agus cad eile is féidir leat a chur leis."

msgid "The Django-specific options here are:"
msgstr "Is iad na roghanna sonracha Django anseo:"

msgid ""
"``chdir``: The path to the directory that needs to be on Python's import "
"path -- i.e., the directory containing the ``mysite`` package."
msgstr ""
"``chdir``: An cosán chuig an eolaire a chaithfidh a bheith ar chonair "
"allmhairithe Python - ie, an eolaire ina bhfuil an pacáiste ``mysite``."

msgid ""
"``module``: The WSGI module to use -- probably the ``mysite.wsgi`` module "
"that :djadmin:`startproject` creates."
msgstr ""
"``module``: An modúl WSGI le húsáid - is dócha an modúl ``mysite.wsgi`` a "
"chruthaíonn: djadmin: `startproject`."

msgid ""
"``env``: Should probably contain at least :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE`."
msgstr ""
"``env``: Ba chóir go mbeadh ar a laghad: envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` "
"ann."

msgid "``home``: Optional path to your project virtual environment."
msgstr ""
"``baile``: Conair roghnach chuig do thimpeallacht fhíorúil tionscadail."

msgid "Example ini configuration file:"
msgstr "Sampla an chomhad cumraíochta seo:"

msgid "Example ini configuration file usage:"
msgstr "Sampla úsáide comhad cumraíochta seo:"

msgid ""
"If you get a ``UnicodeEncodeError`` when uploading files with file names "
"that contain non-ASCII characters, make sure uWSGI is configured to accept "
"non-ASCII file names by adding this to your ``uwsgi.ini``:"
msgstr ""
"Má fhaigheann tú ``UnicodeEncodeError`` agus comhaid á uaslódáil le "
"hainmneacha comhaid ina bhfuil carachtair neamh-ASCII, déan cinnte go bhfuil "
"UWSGI cumraithe chun glacadh le hainmneacha comhaid neamh-ASCII trí é seo a "
"chur le do `uwsgi.ini``:"

msgid ""
"See the uWSGI docs on `managing the uWSGI process`_ for information on "
"starting, stopping and reloading the uWSGI workers."
msgstr ""
"Féach na doiciméid UwsGi maidir le `próiseas UwsGi a bhainistiú `_ le "
"haghaidh faisnéise maidir le tosú, stopadh agus athluchtú oibrithe UWSGI."

msgid "How to manage error reporting"
msgstr "Conas tuairisciú earráide a bhainisti"

msgid ""
"When you're running a public site you should always turn off "
"the :setting:`DEBUG` setting. That will make your server run much faster, "
"and will also prevent malicious users from seeing details of your "
"application that can be revealed by the error pages."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn suíomh poiblí á reáchtáil agat ba chóir duit an socrú: "
"setting: `DEBUG` a mhúchadh i gcónaí. Cuirfidh sé sin go rithfidh do "
"fhreastalaí i bhfad níos gasta, agus cuirfidh sé cosc ar úsáideoirí "
"mailíseacha sonraí d'iarratas a fheiceáil ar féidir leis na leathanaigh "
"earráide a nochtadh."

msgid ""
"However, running with :setting:`DEBUG` set to ``False`` means you'll never "
"see errors generated by your site -- everyone will instead see your public "
"error pages. You need to keep track of errors that occur in deployed sites, "
"so Django can be configured to create reports with details about those "
"errors."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, ciallaíonn rith le:setting: `DEBUG` socraithe go ``False`` ní "
"fheicfidh tú earráidí a ghineann do shuíomh riamh - feicfidh gach duine do "
"leathanaigh earráide poiblí ina ionad sin. Ní mór duit súil a choinneáil ar "
"earráidí a tharlaíonn i suíomhanna imscartha, ionas gur féidir Django a "
"chumrú chun tuarascálacha a chruthú le sonraí faoi na hearráidí sin."

msgid "Email reports"
msgstr "Tuarascálacha ríomh"

msgid "Server errors"
msgstr "Earráidí freastalaí"

msgid ""
"When :setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``, Django will email the users listed in "
"the :setting:`ADMINS` setting whenever your code raises an unhandled "
"exception and results in an internal server error (strictly speaking, for "
"any response with an HTTP status code of 500 or greater). This gives the "
"administrators immediate notification of any errors. The :setting:`ADMINS` "
"will get a description of the error, a complete Python traceback, and "
"details about the HTTP request that caused the error."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: Socrú: ``False`` ná `DEBUG`, ríomhphostálfaidh Django na húsáideoirí "
"atá liostaithe sa socrú: Setting: `ADMINS` aon uair a ardaíonn do chód "
"eisceacht neamh-láimhseáilte agus bíonn earráid inmheánach freastalaí mar "
"thoradh air (go docht, le haghaidh aon fhreagra le cód stádais HTTP 500 nó "
"níos mó). Tugann sé seo fógra láithreach do na riarthóirí faoi aon earráidí. "
"Gheobhaidh an: SETTING: `ADMINS` cur síos ar an earráid, rianú iomlán "
"Python, agus sonraí faoin iarratas HTTP a bhí ina chúis leis an earráid."

msgid ""
"In order to send email, Django requires a few settings telling it how to "
"connect to your mail server. At the very least, you'll need to "
"specify :setting:`EMAIL_HOST` and possibly :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_USER` "
"and :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD`, though other settings may be also "
"required depending on your mail server's configuration. Consult :doc:`the "
"Django settings documentation </ref/settings>` for a full list of email-"
"related settings."
msgstr ""
"Chun ríomhphost a sheoladh, éilíonn Django roinnt socruithe a insíonn dó "
"conas ceangal le do fhreastalaí ríomhphoist. Ar a laghad, beidh ort :socrú: "
"`EMAIL_HOST` a shonrú agus b'fhéidir : socrú: `EMAIL_HOST_USER` agus : "
"socrú: `EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD` a shonrú, cé go bhféadfadh socruithe eile a "
"bheith ag teastáil freisin ag brath ar chumraíocht do fhreastalaí "
"ríomhphoist. Téigh i gcomhairle le :doc:`doiciméadú socruithe Django </ref/"
"settings>` le haghaidh liosta iomlán de shocruithe a bhaineann le ríomhphost."

msgid ""
"By default, Django will send email from root@localhost. However, some mail "
"providers reject all email from this address. To use a different sender "
"address, modify the :setting:`SERVER_EMAIL` setting."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, seolfaidh Django ríomhphost ó root @localhost. Mar "
"sin féin, diúltaíonn roinnt soláthraithe ríomhphoist go léir ón seoladh seo. "
"Chun seoladh seoltóra difriúil a úsáid, modhnaigh an socrú:setting: "
"`SERVER_EMAIL`."

msgid ""
"To activate this behavior, put the email addresses of the recipients in "
"the :setting:`ADMINS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Chun an t-iompar seo a ghníomhachtú, cuir seoltaí ríomhphoist na "
"bhfaighteoirí sa socrú: socrú: `ADMINS`."

msgid ""
"Server error emails are sent using the logging framework, so you can "
"customize this behavior by :doc:`customizing your logging configuration </"
"topics/logging>`."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar ríomhphoist earráide freastalaí leis an gcreat logála, ionas gur "
"féidir leat an t-iompar seo a shaincheapadh trí :doc: `do chumraíocht logála "
"a shaincheapadh </topics/logáil>`."

msgid "404 errors"
msgstr "404 earráidí"

msgid ""
"Django can also be configured to email errors about broken links (404 \"page "
"not found\" errors). Django sends emails about 404 errors when:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir Django a chumrú freisin chun earráidí ríomhphoist faoi naisc "
"briste (404 earráidí “nár aimsíodh leathanach”). Seolann Django ríomhphoist "
"faoi earráidí 404 nuair:"

msgid ":setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``;"
msgstr ":setting: Is é `DEBUG` ``False``;"

msgid ""
"Your :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting "
"includes :class:`django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware`."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn do shuíomh: Socrú: `MIDDLEWARE`: aicme: "
"`django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkemailsMiddleware`."

msgid ""
"If those conditions are met, Django will email the users listed in "
"the :setting:`MANAGERS` setting whenever your code raises a 404 and the "
"request has a referer. It doesn't bother to email for 404s that don't have a "
"referer -- those are usually people typing in broken URLs or broken web "
"bots. It also ignores 404s when the referer is equal to the requested URL, "
"since this behavior is from broken web bots too."
msgstr ""
"Má chomhlíontar na coinníollacha sin, cuirfidh Django ríomhphost chuig na "
"húsáideoirí atá liostaithe sa socrú: SETTING: `MANAGERS` aon uair a ardaíonn "
"do chód 404 agus tá tagairtí ag an iarraidh. Ní chuireann sé isteach ar "
"ríomhphost a dhéanamh do 404s nach bhfuil tagairteoir acu - de ghnáth is "
"daoine iad sin ag clóscríobh URLanna briste nó róbótaí gréasáin briste. "
"Déanann sé neamhaird freisin ar 404s nuair a bhíonn an tagairteoir cothrom "
"leis an URL iarrtha, ós rud é go dtagann an t-iompar seo ó róbótaí gréasáin "
"briste freisin."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware` must appear "
"before other middleware that intercepts 404 errors, such "
"as :class:`~django.middleware.locale.LocaleMiddleware` "
"or :class:`~django.contrib.flatpages.middleware.FlatpageFallbackMiddleware`. "
"Put it toward the top of your :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkemailsMiddleware` caithfidh "
"feiceáil os comhair middleware eile a chuireann isteach ar 404 earráid, mar "
"shampla:class: `~django.middleware.locale.localeMiddleware` nó:class: "
"`~django.contrib.flatpages.middleware.flatpagefallbackleware`. Cuir é i "
"dtreo barr do shuíomh: socrú: `MIDDLEWARE`."

msgid ""
"You can tell Django to stop reporting particular 404s by tweaking "
"the :setting:`IGNORABLE_404_URLS` setting. It should be a list of compiled "
"regular expression objects. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat a rá le Django stop a chur le tuairisciú 404s áirithe tríd an "
"socrú: setting: `IGNORABLE_404_URLS` a mhodhnú. Ba chóir go mbeadh sé ina "
"liosta de rudaí léirithe rialta tiomsaithe. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"In this example, a 404 to any URL ending with ``.php`` or ``.cgi`` will "
"*not* be reported. Neither will any URL starting with ``/phpmyadmin/``."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, tuairiscífear 404 chuig aon URL a chríochnaíonn le ``.php`` "
"nó ``.cgi`` *ní*. Ní bheidh aon URL ag tosú le ``/phpmyadmin/``."

msgid ""
"The following example shows how to exclude some conventional URLs that "
"browsers and crawlers often request::"
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an sampla seo a leanas conas roinnt URLanna traidisiúnta a "
"iarrann brabhsálaithe agus crawlers go minic a eisiamh:"

msgid ""
"(Note that these are regular expressions, so we put a backslash in front of "
"periods to escape them.)"
msgstr ""
"(Tabhair faoi deara gur abairtí rialta iad seo, mar sin cuirimid cúltaca os "
"comhair tréimhsí chun éalú orthu.)"

msgid ""
"If you'd like to customize the behavior "
"of :class:`django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware` further (for "
"example to ignore requests coming from web crawlers), you should subclass it "
"and override its methods."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat iompraíocht de:class: "
"`django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkemailsMiddleware` a shaincheapadh "
"tuilleadh (mar shampla chun neamhaird a dhéanamh d'iarratais a thagann ó "
"crawlers gréasáin), ba cheart duit é a fho-aicmiú agus a mhodhanna a shárú."

msgid ""
"404 errors are logged using the logging framework. By default, these log "
"records are ignored, but you can use them for error reporting by writing a "
"handler and :doc:`configuring logging </topics/logging>` appropriately."
msgstr ""
"Logáiltear earráidí 404 ag baint úsáide as an gcreat logála. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, déantar neamhaird ar na taifid logála seo, ach is féidir "
"leat iad a úsáid le haghaidh tuairisciú earráide trí láimhseálaí a scríobh "
"agus:doc: `log</topics/logging> áil a chumrú' go cuí."

msgid "Filtering error reports"
msgstr "Tuarascálacha earráide sc"

msgid ""
"Filtering sensitive data is a hard problem, and it's nearly impossible to "
"guarantee that sensitive data won't leak into an error report. Therefore, "
"error reports should only be available to trusted team members and you "
"should avoid transmitting error reports unencrypted over the internet (such "
"as through email)."
msgstr ""
"Is fadhb chrua é sonraí íogaire a scagadh, agus tá sé beagnach dodhéanta a "
"chinntiú nach ligfidh sonraí íogaire isteach i dtuairisc earráide. Mar sin, "
"níor cheart go mbeadh tuairiscí earráide ar fáil ach do bhaill foirne "
"iontaofa agus ba cheart duit tuarascálacha earráide gan chriptiú a tharchur "
"thar an idirlíon (mar shampla trí ríomhphost) a sheachaint."

msgid "Filtering sensitive information"
msgstr "Eolas íogair a scagadh"

msgid ""
"Error reports are really helpful for debugging errors, so it is generally "
"useful to record as much relevant information about those errors as "
"possible. For example, by default Django records the `full traceback`_ for "
"the exception raised, each `traceback frame`_’s local variables, and "
"the :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest`’s :ref:`attributes<httprequest-"
"attributes>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá tuarascálacha earráide an-chabhrach le haghaidh earráidí dífhabhtaithe, "
"mar sin de ghnáth bíonn sé úsáideach an oiread faisnéise ábhartha a "
"thaifeadadh faoi na hearrá <httprequest-attributes>Mar shampla, de réir "
"réamhshocraithe taifeadann Django an `taceback iomlán`_ don eisceacht a "
"ardaíodh, athróga áitiúla gach `fráma rianaithe`_, agus an:class: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest`'s:ref: `tréithe `."

msgid ""
"However, sometimes certain types of information may be too sensitive and "
"thus may not be appropriate to be kept track of, for example a user's "
"password or credit card number. So in addition to filtering out settings "
"that appear to be sensitive as described in the :setting:`DEBUG` "
"documentation, Django offers a set of function decorators to help you "
"control which information should be filtered out of error reports in a "
"production environment (that is, where :setting:`DEBUG` is set to "
"``False``): :func:`sensitive_variables` "
"and :func:`sensitive_post_parameters`."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, uaireanta d'fhéadfadh cineálacha áirithe faisnéise a bheith ró-"
"íogair agus mar sin b'fhéidir nach mbeadh sé oiriúnach súil a choinneáil "
"orthu, mar shampla pasfhocal úsáideora nó uimhir chárta creidmheasa. Mar "
"sin, chomh maith le socruithe atá le cosúil go bhfuil siad íogair a scagadh "
"mar a thuairiscítear sa dhoiciméadú: 'DEBUG', cuireann Django sraith "
"maisitheoirí feidhme ar fáil chun cabhrú leat a rialú cén fhaisnéis ba chóir "
"a scagadh as tuarascálacha earráide i dtimpeallacht táirgeachta (is é sin, "
"áit:setting: `False`) ::func: `sensitive_variables` agus:func: "
"`sensitive_paraiméadair post'."

msgid ""
"If a function (either a view or any regular callback) in your code uses "
"local variables susceptible to contain sensitive information, you may "
"prevent the values of those variables from being included in error reports "
"using the ``sensitive_variables`` decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann feidhm (amharc nó aon ghlaoch ar ais rialta) i do chód athróga "
"áitiúla a bhfuil faisnéis íogair ann, féadfaidh tú cosc a chur ar luachanna "
"na n-athróg sin a chur san áireamh i dtuarascálacha earráide ag baint úsáide "
"as an maisitheoir ``sensitive_variables`:"

msgid ""
"In the above example, the values for the ``user``, ``pw`` and ``cc`` "
"variables will be hidden and replaced with stars (``**********``) in the "
"error reports, whereas the value of the ``name`` variable will be disclosed."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, cuirfear na luachanna do na hathróga ``úsáideoir ``, `pw`` "
"agus `cc`` i bhfolach agus cuirfear réaltaí (`**********``) in ionad sna "
"tuarascálacha earráide, ach nochtfar luach an athróg ``ainm``."

msgid ""
"To systematically hide all local variables of a function from error logs, do "
"not provide any argument to the ``sensitive_variables`` decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Chun gach athróg áitiúil de fheidhm a cheilt go córasach ó logaí earráide, "
"ná tabhair aon argóint don maisitheoir ``sensitive_variables`:"

msgid "When using multiple decorators"
msgstr "Agus maisitheoirí iolracha á úsáid agat"

msgid ""
"If the variable you want to hide is also a function argument (e.g. "
"'``user``’ in the following example), and if the decorated function has "
"multiple decorators, then make sure to place ``@sensitive_variables`` at the "
"top of the decorator chain. This way it will also hide the function argument "
"as it gets passed through the other decorators::"
msgstr ""
"Más argóint feidhme é an t-athróg a theastaíonn uait a cheilt freisin (m.sh. "
"'``úsáideoir ``' sa sampla seo a leanas), agus má tá maisitheoirí iolracha "
"ag an bhfeidhm maisithe, déan cinnte go gcuirfidh tú`` @sensitive_variables "
"``ag barr an slabhra maisiúcháin. Ar an mbealach seo folóidh sé an argóint "
"feidhme freisin de réir mar a chuirtear tríd na maisitheoirí eile::"

msgid ""
"If one of your views receives an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object "
"with :attr:`POST parameters<django.http.HttpRequest.POST>` susceptible to "
"contain sensitive information, you may prevent the values of those "
"parameters from being included in the error reports using the "
"``sensitive_post_parameters`` decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Má fhaigheann duine de <django.http.HttpRequest.POST>do thuairimí "
"réad: :class: `~django.http.http.httpRequest` le: attr: `Paraiméadair POST "
"`atá so-ghabhálach go mbeidh faisnéis íogair ann, féadfaidh tú cosc a chur "
"ar luachanna na bparaiméadair sin a chur san áireamh sna tuarascálacha "
"earráide ag baint úsáide as an maisitheoir ``sensitive_post_parameters``:"

msgid ""
"In the above example, the values for the ``pass_word`` and "
"``credit_card_number`` POST parameters will be hidden and replaced with "
"stars (``**********``) in the request's representation inside the error "
"reports, whereas the value of the ``name`` parameter will be disclosed."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, cuirfear na luachanna do pharaiméadair POST ``pass_word`` "
"agus ``credit_card_number`` i bhfolach agus cuirfear réaltaí (`**********``) "
"in ionadaíocht an iarratais taobh istigh de na tuarascálacha earráide, ach "
"nochtfar luach an pharaiméadar ``ainm ``."

msgid ""
"To systematically hide all POST parameters of a request in error reports, do "
"not provide any argument to the ``sensitive_post_parameters`` decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Chun gach paraiméadar POST d'iarratas a cheilt go córasach i dtuarascálacha "
"earráide, ná cuir aon argóint ar fáil don maisitheoir "
"``sensitive_post_paraméters':"

msgid ""
"All POST parameters are systematically filtered out of error reports for "
"certain :mod:`django.contrib.auth.views` views (``login``, "
"``password_reset_confirm``, ``password_change``, and ``add_view`` and "
"``user_change_password`` in the ``auth`` admin) to prevent the leaking of "
"sensitive information such as user passwords."
msgstr ""
"Déantar gach paraiméadar POST a scagadh go córasach as tuarascálacha "
"earráide le go cinnte:mod: tuairimí `django.contrib.auth.views` (``login``, "
"`password_reset_confirm``, `password_change``, agus `add_view`` agus "
"`user_change_password`` admin `auth``) chun faisnéis íogair a chosc mar "
"shampla pasfhocail úsáideora."

msgid "Custom error reports"
msgstr "Tuarascálacha earráide sain"

msgid ""
"All :func:`sensitive_variables` and :func:`sensitive_post_parameters` do is, "
"respectively, annotate the decorated function with the names of sensitive "
"variables and annotate the ``HttpRequest`` object with the names of "
"sensitive POST parameters, so that this sensitive information can later be "
"filtered out of reports when an error occurs. The actual filtering is done "
"by Django's default error reporter "
"filter: :class:`django.views.debug.SafeExceptionReporterFilter`. This filter "
"uses the decorators' annotations to replace the corresponding values with "
"stars (``**********``) when the error reports are produced. If you wish to "
"override or customize this default behavior for your entire site, you need "
"to define your own filter class and tell Django to use it via "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER_FILTER` setting::"
msgstr ""
"All:Func: `sensitive_variables` agus:func: `sensitive_post_parameters` is ea "
"anótáil, faoi seach, an fheidhm maisithe le hainmneacha athróg íogair agus "
"an rud `HttpRequest ``a anótáil le hainmneacha paraiméadair íogair POST, "
"ionas gur féidir an fhaisnéis íogair seo a scagadh amach as tuarascálacha "
"nuair a tharlaíonn earráid. Déantar an scagadh iarbhír ag scagaire "
"tuairisceora earráide réamhshocraithe Django: :class: "
"`django.views.debug.safeExceptionReporterFilter`. Úsáideann an scagaire seo "
"anótaí na mhaisitheoirí chun réaltaí (`**********``) a chur in ionad na "
"luachanna comhfhreagracha nuair a tháirgtear na tuarascálacha earráide. Más "
"mian leat an t-iompar réamhshocraithe seo a shárú nó a shaincheapadh do do "
"shuíomh iomlán, ní mór duit do rang scagaire féin a shainiú agus a rá le "
"Django é a úsáid trí:setting: `DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER_FILTER`::"

msgid ""
"You may also control in a more granular way which filter to use within any "
"given view by setting the ``HttpRequest``’s ``exception_reporter_filter`` "
"attribute::"
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tú rialú ar bhealach níos gráinneach freisin cén scagaire atá le "
"húsáid laistigh d'aon radharc ar leith trí thréith "
"```exception_reporter_filter`` ``httpRequest`` a shocrú:"

msgid ""
"Your custom filter class needs to inherit "
"from :class:`django.views.debug.SafeExceptionReporterFilter` and may "
"override the following attributes and methods:"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh do rang scagaire saincheaptha oidhreacht ó:class: "
"`django.views.debug.safeExceptionReporterFilter` agus féadfaidh sé na "
"tréithe agus na modhanna seo a leanas a shárú:"

msgid ""
"The string value to replace sensitive value with. By default it replaces the "
"values of sensitive variables with stars (``**********``)."
msgstr ""
"An luach teaghrán le luach íogair a chur in ionad. De réir réamhshocraithe "
"cuireann sé réaltaí in ionad luachanna na n-athróg íogair (`**********``)."

msgid ""
"A compiled regular expression object used to match settings and "
"``request.META`` values considered as sensitive. By default equivalent to::"
msgstr ""
"Réad léirithe rialta tiomsaithe a úsáidtear chun socruithe agus luachanna "
"``request.meta`` a mheaitear mar íogair a mheaitseáil. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe atá comhionann le:"

msgid "The term ``AUTH`` was added."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` to activate the filtering in :meth:`get_post_parameters` "
"and :meth:`get_traceback_frame_variables`. By default the filter is active "
"if :setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``. Note that sensitive ``request.META`` "
"values are always filtered along with sensitive setting values, as described "
"in the :setting:`DEBUG` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``True`` chun an scagadh a ghníomhachtú in:meth: "
"`get_post_paraméters` agus:meth: `get_traceback_frame_variables`. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe tá an scagaire gníomhach má tá: socrú: `DEBUG` ``False``. "
"Tabhair faoi deara go ndéantar luachanna íogaire ``request.meta`` a scagadh "
"i gcónaí in éineacht le luachanna socraithe íogaire, mar a thuairiscítear sa "
"doiciméadúiséireacht: `DEBUG`."

msgid ""
"Returns the filtered dictionary of POST parameters. Sensitive values are "
"replaced with :attr:`cleansed_substitute`."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an foclóir scagtha de pharaiméadair POST. Cuirtear: attr: "
"`cleansed_substitute` in ionad luachanna íogair."

msgid ""
"Returns the filtered dictionary of local variables for the given traceback "
"frame. Sensitive values are replaced with :attr:`cleansed_substitute`."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an foclóir scagtha d'athróg áitiúla ar ais don fhráma rianaithe ar "
"leith. Cuirtear: attr: `cleansed_substitute` in ionad luachanna íogair."

msgid ""
"If you need to customize error reports beyond filtering you may specify a "
"custom error reporter class by defining "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER` setting::"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit tuarascálacha earráide a shaincheapadh níos faide ná scagadh "
"féadfaidh tú rang tuairisceoir earráide saincheaptha a shonrú trí:setting: "
"`DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER` a shainiú::"

msgid ""
"The exception reporter is responsible for compiling the exception report "
"data, and formatting it as text or HTML appropriately. (The exception "
"reporter uses :setting:`DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER_FILTER` when preparing "
"the exception report data.)"
msgstr ""
"Tá an tuairisceoir eisceachta freagrach as sonraí na tuarascála eisceachta a "
"thiomsú, agus iad a fhormáidiú mar théacs nó HTML go cuí. (Úsáideann an "
"tuairisceoir eisceachta: socrú: `DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER_FILTER` agus "
"sonraí na tuarascála eisceachta á ullmhú.)"

msgid ""
"Your custom reporter class needs to inherit "
"from :class:`django.views.debug.ExceptionReporter`."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh do rang tuairisceora saincheaptha oidhreacht ó:class: "
"`django.views.debug.exceptionReporter`."

msgid ""
"Property that returns a :class:`pathlib.Path` representing the absolute "
"filesystem path to a template for rendering the HTML representation of the "
"exception. Defaults to the Django provided template."
msgstr ""
"Maoin a thugann ar ais a:class: `PathLib.path` a léiríonn cosán iomlán an "
"chórais chomhaid chuig teimpléad chun léiriú HTML na heisceachta a léiriú. "
"Réamhshocraithe don teimpléad a chuirtear ar fáil Django."

msgid ""
"Property that returns a :class:`pathlib.Path` representing the absolute "
"filesystem path to a template for rendering the plain-text representation of "
"the exception. Defaults to the Django provided template."
msgstr ""
"Maoin a thugann ar ais a:class: `PathLib.path` a léiríonn cosán iomlán an "
"chórais chomhaid chuig teimpléad chun léiriú téacs simplí na heisceachta a "
"léiriú. Réamhshocraithe don teimpléad a chuirtear ar fáil Django."

msgid "Return a dictionary containing traceback information."
msgstr "Cuir ar ais foclóir ina bhfuil faisnéis rianaithe ar ais."

msgid ""
"This is the main extension point for customizing exception reports, for "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an príomhphointe síneadh chun tuarascálacha eisceachta a "
"shaincheapadh, mar shampla:"

msgid "Return HTML version of exception report."
msgstr "Tabhair ar ais leagan HTML den tuarascáil eisceachta."

msgid "Used for HTML version of debug 500 HTTP error page."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear le haghaidh leagan HTML de leathanach earráide HTTP debug 500."

msgid "Return plain text version of exception report."
msgstr "Tabhair ar ais leagan téacs simplí den tuarascáil eisceachta."

msgid ""
"Used for plain text version of debug 500 HTTP error page and email reports."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear le haghaidh leagan téacs simplí de leathanach earráide HTTP debug "
"500 agus tuarascálacha ríomhphoist."

msgid ""
"As with the filter class, you may control which exception reporter class to "
"use within any given view by setting the ``HttpRequest``’s "
"``exception_reporter_class`` attribute::"
msgstr ""
"Mar is amhlaidh leis an rang scagaire, féadfaidh tú rialú cén rang "
"tuairisceoir eisceachta atá le húsáid laistigh d'aon radharc ar leith trí "
"thréith ```exception_reporter_class`` ``httpRequest`` a shocrú:"

msgid ""
"You can also set up custom error reporting by writing a custom piece "
"of :ref:`exception middleware <exception-middleware>`. If you do write "
"custom error handling, it's a good idea to emulate Django's built-in error "
"handling and only report/log errors if :setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"<exception-middleware>Is féidir leat tuairisciú earráide saincheaptha a chur "
"ar bun freisin trí phíosa saincheaptha de: ref: `middleware eisceachta `a "
"scríobh. Má scríobhann tú láimhseáil earráide saincheaptha, is smaoineamh "
"maith é aithris a dhéanamh ar láimhseáil earráide ionsuite Django agus "
"earráidí a thuairisciú/logáil ach amháin má tá: socrú: ``False`` ná `DEBUG`."

msgid "How-to guides"
msgstr "Treoracha conas"

msgid "Practical guides covering common tasks and problems."
msgstr "Treoracha praiticiúla a chlúdaíonn tascanna agus fadhbanna coitianta."

msgid "Models, data and databases"
msgstr "Múnlaí, sonraí agus bunachair sonraí"

msgid "Templates and output"
msgstr "Teimpléid agus aschur"

msgid "Project configuration and management"
msgstr "Cumraíocht agus bainistíocht tionscadail"

msgid "Installing, deploying and upgrading"
msgstr "Suiteáil, imscaradh agus uasghrádú"

msgid "Other guides"
msgstr "Treoracha eile"

msgid ""
"The `Django community aggregator`_, where we aggregate content from the "
"global Django community. Many writers in the aggregator write this sort of "
"how-to material."
msgstr ""
"An `aggregatóir pobail Django `_, áit a dtugaimid ábhar ón bpobal domhanda "
"Django a chomhiomlánú. Scríobhann go leor scríbhneoirí sa chomhiomlántóir "
"ábhar conas seo."

msgid "How to provide initial data for models"
msgstr "Conas sonraí tosaigh a sholáthar do mhúnlaí"

msgid ""
"It's sometimes useful to prepopulate your database with hard-coded data when "
"you're first setting up an app. You can provide initial data with migrations "
"or fixtures."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta bíonn sé úsáideach do bhunachar sonraí a réamhdhíonrú le sonraí "
"crua-chódaithe nuair a bhíonn aip ar bun agat ar dtús. Is féidir leat sonraí "
"tosaigh a sholáthar le himirce nó daingneáin."

msgid "Provide initial data with migrations"
msgstr "Sonraí tosaigh a sholáthar le himirce"

msgid ""
"To automatically load initial data for an app, create a :ref:`data migration "
"<data-migrations>`. Migrations are run when setting up the test database, so "
"the data will be available there, subject to :ref:`some limitations <test-"
"case-serialized-rollback>`."
msgstr ""
"<data-migrations>Chun sonraí tosaigh do aip a luchtú go huathoibríoch, "
"cruthaigh a:ref: `imirce sonraí `. <test-case-serialized-"
"rollback>Reáchtáiltear imirce agus an bunachar sonraí tástála á bunú, mar "
"sin beidh na sonraí ar fáil ansin, faoi réir: ref: `roinnt teorainneacha `."

msgid "Provide data with fixtures"
msgstr "Sonraí a sholáthar le daingneáin"

msgid ""
"You can also provide data using :ref:`fixtures <fixtures-explanation>`, "
"however, this data isn't loaded automatically, except if you "
"use :attr:`.TransactionTestCase.fixtures`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat sonraí a sholáthar freisin ag baint úsáidea:ref: `daing "
"<fixtures-explanation>neáin `, áfach, ní luchtaítear na sonraí seo go "
"huathoibríoch, ach amháin má úsáideann tú: attr: "
"`.transactionTestCase.fixtures`."

msgid ""
"A fixture is a collection of data that Django knows how to import into a "
"database. The most straightforward way of creating a fixture if you've "
"already got some data is to use the :djadmin:`manage.py dumpdata <dumpdata>` "
"command. Or, you can write fixtures by hand; fixtures can be written as "
"JSON, XML or YAML (with PyYAML_ installed) documents. "
"The :doc:`serialization documentation </topics/serialization>` has more "
"details about each of these supported :ref:`serialization formats "
"<serialization-formats>`."
msgstr ""
"Is bailiúchán sonraí é daingneán a bhfuil a fhios ag Django conas a "
"iompórtáil isteach i mbunachar sonraí. <dumpdata>Is é an bealach is simplí "
"chun daingneán a chruthú má tá roinnt sonraí agat cheana féin ná an t-"
"ordú:djadmin: `manage.py dumpdata `a úsáid. Nó, is féidir leat daingneáin a "
"scríobh de láimh; is féidir daingneáin a scríobh mar dhoiciméid JSON, XML nó "
"YAML (le PyYAML_ suiteáilte). </topics/serialization> <serialization-"
"formats>Tá tuilleadh sonraí ag an doiciméadú: Doc: `sraitheoireach` faoi "
"gach ceann de na formáidí sraitheoireachta seo a tacaítear leis: ref: "
"`sraitheach`."

msgid ""
"As an example, though, here's what a fixture for a ``Person`` model might "
"look like in JSON:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, áfach, seo an chuma a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ar dhaingneán do "
"mhúnla ``Person` i JSON:"

msgid "And here's that same fixture as YAML:"
msgstr "Agus seo an daingneán céanna le YAML:"

msgid "You'll store this data in a ``fixtures`` directory inside your app."
msgstr ""
"Stórálfaidh tú na sonraí seo in eolaire ``fixtures` taobh istigh d'aip."

msgid ""
"You can load data by calling :djadmin:`manage.py loaddata <loaddata>` "
"``<fixturename>``, where ``<fixturename>`` is the name of the fixture file "
"you've created. Each time you run :djadmin:`loaddata`, the data will be read "
"from the fixture and reloaded into the database. Note this means that if you "
"change one of the rows created by a fixture and then run :djadmin:`loaddata` "
"again, you'll wipe out any changes you've made."
msgstr ""
"<fixturename>Is féidir leat sonraí a luchtú trí ghlaoch: djadmin: `manage.py "
"loaddata <loaddata>````<fixturename>, áit a bhfuil`` ``ainm an chomhaid "
"daingneáin a chruthaigh tú. Gach uair a rith tú: djadmin: `loaddata`, "
"léifear na sonraí ón daingneán agus a athluchtú isteach sa bhunachar sonraí. "
"Tabhair faoi deara ciallaíonn sé seo má athraíonn tú ceann de na sraitheanna "
"a chruthaigh daingneán agus ansin rith: djadmin: `loaddata` arís, "
"scriosfaidh tú aon athruithe a rinne tú amach."

msgid "Tell Django where to look for fixture files"
msgstr "Inis do Django cá háit le comhaid daingneáin a lorg"

msgid ""
"By default, Django looks for fixtures in the ``fixtures`` directory inside "
"each app, so the command ``loaddata sample`` will find the file ``my_app/"
"fixtures/sample.json``. This works with relative paths as well, so "
"``loaddata my_app/sample`` will find the file ``my_app/fixtures/my_app/"
"sample.json``."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, féachann Django daingneáin san eolaire ``fixtures`` "
"taobh istigh de gach aip, mar sin gheobhaidh an t-ordú ``loaddata sample`` "
"an comhad ``my_app/fixtures/sample.json``. Oibríonn sé seo le cosáin "
"choibhneasta freisin, mar sin gheobhaidh ``loaddata my_app/sample`` an "
"comhad ``my_app/fixtures/my_app/sample.json``."

msgid ""
"Django also looks for fixtures in the list of directories provided in "
"the :setting:`FIXTURE_DIRS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Féachann Django daingneáin freisin ar liosta na n-eolairí a chuirtear ar "
"fáil sa socrú: setting: `FIXTURE_DIRS`."

msgid ""
"To completely prevent default search from happening, use an absolute path to "
"specify the location of your fixture file, e.g. ``loaddata /path/to/sample``."
msgstr ""
"Chun cuardach réamhshocraithe a chosc go hiomlán ó tharla, bain úsáid as "
"cosán iomlán chun suíomh do chomhad daingneáin a shonrú, m.sh. `loaddata /"
"path/to/sample ``."

msgid "Namespace your fixture files"
msgstr "Spás ainmneacha do chomhaid daingneáin"

msgid ""
"Django will use the first fixture file it finds whose name matches, so if "
"you have fixture files with the same name in different applications, you "
"will be unable to distinguish between them in your ``loaddata`` commands. "
"The easiest way to avoid this problem is by *namespacing* your fixture "
"files. That is, by putting them inside a directory named for their "
"application, as in the relative path example above."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfidh Django an chéad chomhad daingneáin a aimsíonn sé a n-ainm a "
"mheaitseálann, mar sin má tá comhaid daingneáin agat leis an ainm céanna in "
"iarratais éagsúla, ní bheidh tú in ann idirdhealú a dhéanamh eatarthu i "
"d'orduithe ``loaddata`. Is é an bealach is éasca chun an fhadhb seo a "
"sheachaint ná trí* spás ainmnea* do chomhaid daingneáin. Is é sin, trí iad a "
"chur taobh istigh de eolaire ainmnithe dá bhfeidhmchlár, mar atá sa sampla "
"coibhneasta coibhneasta thuas."

msgid ""
"Fixtures are also used by the :ref:`testing framework <topics-testing-"
"fixtures>` to help set up a consistent test environment."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear daingneáin freisin ag an: ref: `creat tástála <topics-testing-"
"fixtures>`chun cabhrú le timpeallacht chomhsheasmhach tástála a bhunú."

msgid "How to integrate Django with a legacy database"
msgstr "Conas Django a chomhtháthú le bunachar sonraí oidhreachta"

msgid ""
"While Django is best suited for developing new applications, it's quite "
"possible to integrate it into legacy databases. Django includes a couple of "
"utilities to automate as much of this process as possible."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil Django is fearr oiriúnach chun feidhmchláir nua a fhorbairt, is "
"féidir é a chomhtháthú i mbunachair sonraí oidhreachta. Cuimsíonn Django "
"cúpla fóntais chun an oiread den phróiseas seo agus is féidir a uathoibriú."

msgid ""
"This document assumes you know the Django basics, as covered in "
"the :doc:`tutorial </intro/tutorial01>`."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an doiciméad seo leis go bhfuil na buneilimintí Django ar eolas "
"agat, mar atá clúdaithe in:doc: `teagorial` </intro/tutorial01>."

msgid ""
"Once you've got Django set up, you'll follow this general process to "
"integrate with an existing database."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh Django curtha ar bun agat, leanfaidh tú an próiseas "
"ginearálta seo chun comhtháthú le bunachar sonraí atá ann cheana."

msgid "Give Django your database parameters"
msgstr "Tabhair do pharaiméadair bunachar sonraí do Dj"

msgid ""
"You'll need to tell Django what your database connection parameters are, and "
"what the name of the database is. Do that by editing "
"the :setting:`DATABASES` setting and assigning values to the following keys "
"for the ``'default'`` connection:"
msgstr ""
"Beidh ort a insint do Django cad iad do pharaiméadair nasc bunachar sonraí, "
"agus cad é ainm an bhunachar sonraí. Déan é sin tríd an socrú:setting: "
"`DATABASES` a chur in eagar agus luachanna a shannadh do na heochracha seo a "
"leanas don nasc ``'default' ``:"

msgid ":setting:`NAME`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `AINM`"

msgid ":setting:`ENGINE <DATABASE-ENGINE>`"
msgstr "<DATABASE-ENGINE>: socrú: `INNEALL `"

msgid ":setting:`USER`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `ÚSÁIDEOIR`"

msgid ":setting:`PASSWORD`"
msgstr ":setting: `PASSWORD`"

msgid ":setting:`HOST`"
msgstr ":socrú: `HOST`"

msgid ":setting:`PORT`"
msgstr ":socrú: `PORT `"

msgid "Auto-generate the models"
msgstr "Giniúint na samhlacha go huath"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a utility called :djadmin:`inspectdb` that can create "
"models by introspecting an existing database. You can view the output by "
"running this command:"
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le fóntais ar a dtugtar: djadmin: `inspectdb` atá in ann "
"samhlacha a chruthú trí bhunachar sonraí atá ann cheana a iontráil. Is "
"féidir leat féachaint ar an aschur tríd an ordú seo a rith:"

msgid "Save this as a file by using standard Unix output redirection:"
msgstr ""
"Sábháil é seo mar chomhad trí athatreorú aschuir caighdeánach Unix a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"This feature is meant as a shortcut, not as definitive model generation. See "
"the :djadmin:`documentation of inspectdb <inspectdb>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Tá an ghné seo i gceist mar aicearra, ní mar ghiniúint samhail "
"chinntitheach. <inspectdb>Féach na:djadmin: `doiciméadú inspectdb `le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"Once you've cleaned up your models, name the file ``models.py`` and put it "
"in the Python package that holds your app. Then add the app to "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh do mhúnlaí glan agat, ainmnigh an comhad ``models.py`` agus "
"cuir é sa phacáiste Python a choinníonn d'aip. Ansin cuir an aip le do "
"shuíomh: setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"By default, :djadmin:`inspectdb` creates unmanaged models. That is, "
"``managed = False`` in the model's ``Meta`` class tells Django not to manage "
"each table's creation, modification, and deletion::"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, cruthaíonn: djadmin: `inspectdb` samhlacha neamh-"
"bhainistithe. Is é sin, deir ``bhainistithe = False`` i rang ``Meta`` an "
"tsamhail le Django gan cruthú, modhnú agus scriosadh gach tábla a bhainistiú:"

msgid ""
"If you do want to allow Django to manage the table's lifecycle, you'll need "
"to change the :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.managed` option above to "
"``True`` (or remove it because ``True`` is its default value)."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat ligean a thabhairt do Django saolré an tábla a bhainistiú, "
"beidh ort an rogha: attr: `~django.db.models.options.managed` thuas a athrú "
"go `True`` (nó é a bhaint toisc gurb é `True`` a luach réamhshocraithe)."

msgid "Install the core Django tables"
msgstr "Suiteáil na táblaí lárnacha Django"

msgid ""
"Next, run the :djadmin:`migrate` command to install any extra needed "
"database records such as admin permissions and content types:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, reáchtáil an t-ordú:djadmin: `migrate` chun aon taifid bhunachar "
"sonraí breise is gá a shuiteáil mar cheadanna riaracháin agus cineálacha "
"ábhair:"

msgid "Test and tweak"
msgstr "Tástáil agus tweak"

msgid ""
"Those are the basic steps -- from here you'll want to tweak the models "
"Django generated until they work the way you'd like. Try accessing your data "
"via the Django database API, and try editing objects via Django's admin "
"site, and edit the models file accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Sin iad na céimeanna bunúsacha - ó anseo beidh tú ag iarraidh a tweak na "
"samhlacha Django a ghintear go dtí go n-oibríonn siad ar an mbealach is mian "
"leat. Bain triail as rochtain a fháil ar do shonraí trí API bunachar sonraí "
"Django, agus déan iarracht rudaí a chur in eagar trí shuíomh riaracháin "
"Django, agus cuir comhad na samhlacha in eagar dá réir."

msgid "How to configure and use logging"
msgstr "Conas logáil a chumrú agus a úsáid"

msgid ":ref:`Django logging reference <logging-ref>`"
msgstr "<logging-ref>:ref: `Tagairt logála Django `"

msgid ":ref:`Django logging overview <logging-explanation>`"
msgstr "<logging-explanation>:ref: `Forbhreathnú logála Django `"

msgid ""
"Django provides a working :ref:`default logging configuration <default-"
"logging-configuration>` that is readily extended."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django oibrí:ref: `cumraíocht logála réamhshocraithe <default-"
"logging-configuration>`a leathnaítear go héasca."

msgid "Make a basic logging call"
msgstr "Déan glao logála bunúsach"

msgid ""
"To send a log message from within your code, you place a logging call into "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Chun teachtaireacht logála a sheoladh ó laistigh de do chód, cuireann tú "
"glao logála isteach ann."

msgid "Don't be tempted to use logging calls in ``settings.py``."
msgstr "Ná bíodh mealladh ort glaonna logála a úsáid i `settings.py``."

msgid ""
"The way that Django logging is configured as part of the ``setup()`` "
"function means that logging calls placed in ``settings.py`` may not work as "
"expected, because *logging will not be set up at that point*. To explore "
"logging, use a view function as suggested in the example below."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn an bealach a chuirtear logáil Django mar chuid den fheidhm "
"``setup () ``go bhféadfadh glaonna logála a chuirtear i `settings.py` "
"`oibreoidh mar a bhíothas ag súil leis, toisc nach mbunófar logáil ag an "
"bpointe sin *. Chun logáil a iniúchadh, bain úsáid as feidhm amharc mar a "
"mholtar sa sampla thíos."

msgid ""
"First, import the Python logging library, and then obtain a logger instance "
"with :py:func:`logging.getLogger`. Provide the ``getLogger()`` method with a "
"name to identify it and the records it emits. A good option is to use "
"``__name__`` (see :ref:`naming-loggers` below for more on this) which will "
"provide the name of the current Python module as a dotted path::"
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, iompórtáil leabharlann logála Python, agus ansin faigh sampla "
