"tarchur comhad mór CSV a láimhseáil go héifeachtúil::"

msgid "Using the template system"
msgstr "An córas teimpléad a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use the :doc:`Django template system </topics/"
"templates>` to generate CSV. This is lower-level than using the convenient "
"Python :mod:`csv` module, but the solution is presented here for "
"completeness."
msgstr ""
"De rogha air sin, is féidir leat an córas teimpléad: doc: `Django` a úsáid "
"chun CSV a ghiniúint. </topics/templates> Tá sé seo ar leibhéal níos ísle ná "
"an modúl áisiúil Python: MOD: `csv` a úsáid, ach cuirtear an réiteach i "
"láthair anseo le haghaidh iomláine."

msgid ""
"The idea here is to pass a list of items to your template, and have the "
"template output the commas in a :ttag:`for` loop."
msgstr ""
"Is é an smaoineamh anseo liosta míreanna a chur chuig do theimpléad, agus an "
"teimpléad a chur ar aschur na camóga in a:ttag: `for` lúb."

msgid "Here's an example, which generates the same CSV file as above::"
msgstr "Seo sampla, a ghineann an comhad CSV céanna mar thuas:"

msgid ""
"The only difference between this example and the previous example is that "
"this one uses template loading instead of the CSV module. The rest of the "
"code -- such as the ``content_type='text/csv'`` -- is the same."
msgstr ""
"Is é an t-aon difríocht idir an sampla seo agus an sampla roimhe seo ná go n-"
"úsáideann an ceann seo luchtú teimpléid in ionad an modúl CSV. Tá an chuid "
"eile den chód - mar shampla an ``content_type='text/csv'`` - mar an gcéanna."

msgid ""
"Then, create the template ``my_template_name.txt``, with this template code:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cruthaigh an teimpléad ``my_template_name.txt``, leis an gcód "
"teimpléad seo:"

msgid ""
"This short template iterates over the given data and displays a line of CSV "
"for each row. It uses the :tfilter:`addslashes` template filter to ensure "
"there aren't any problems with quotes."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn an teimpléad gearr seo thar na sonraí a thugtar agus taispeánann "
"sé líne CSV do gach sraith. Úsáideann sé an scagaire teimpléad:tfilter: "
"`addslashes` chun a chinntiú nach bhfuil aon fhadhbanna le luachana."

msgid "Other text-based formats"
msgstr "Formáidí téacs-bhunaithe eile"

msgid ""
"Notice that there isn't very much specific to CSV here -- just the specific "
"output format. You can use either of these techniques to output any text-"
"based format you can dream of. You can also use a similar technique to "
"generate arbitrary binary data; see :doc:`/howto/outputting-pdf` for an "
"example."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil an-shonrach ann maidir le CSV anseo - díreach "
"an fhormáid aschuir ar leith. Is féidir leat ceachtar de na teicnící seo a "
"úsáid chun aon fhormáid téacs-bhunaithe is féidir leat a aisling a aschur. "
"Is féidir leat teicníc den chineál céanna a úsáid freisin chun sonraí "
"dénártha treallach a ghiniúint; féach:doc: `/howto/outputting-pdf` mar "
"shampla."

msgid "How to create PDF files"
msgstr "Conas comhaid PDF a chruthú"

msgid ""
"This document explains how to output PDF files dynamically using Django "
"views. This is made possible by the excellent, open-source ReportLab_ Python "
"PDF library."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo conas comhaid PDF a aschur go dinimiciúil ag úsáid "
"radhairc Django Is féidir é seo a dhéanamh leis an leabharlann PDF "
"ReportLab_ Python foinse oscailte den scoth."

msgid ""
"The advantage of generating PDF files dynamically is that you can create "
"customized PDFs for different purposes -- say, for different users or "
"different pieces of content."
msgstr ""
"Is é an buntáiste a bhaineann le comhaid PDF a ghiniúint go dinimiciúil ná "
"gur féidir leat PDFanna saincheaptha a chruthú chun críocha éagsúla -- "
"abair, d'úsáideoirí éagsúla nó do phíosaí éagsúla ábhair."

msgid ""
"For example, Django was used at kusports.com_ to generate customized, "
"printer-friendly NCAA tournament brackets, as PDF files, for people "
"participating in a March Madness contest."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, úsáideadh Django ag kusports.com_ chun lúibíní comórtais NCAA "
"saincheaptha, atá cairdiúil don phriontáil a ghiniúint, mar chomhaid PDF, do "
"dhaoine a ghlac páirt i gcomórtas March Madness."

msgid "Install ReportLab"
msgstr "Suiteáil ReportLab"

msgid ""
"The ReportLab library is :pypi:`available on PyPI <reportlab>`. A `user "
"guide`_ (not coincidentally, a PDF file) is also available for download. You "
"can install ReportLab with ``pip``:"
msgstr ""
"<reportlab>Is é leabharlann ReportLab: pypi: `ar fáil ar PyPI `. Tá `treoir "
"úsáideora `_ (ní comhtharlach, comhad PDF) ar fáil le híoslódáil freisin. Is "
"féidir leat ReportLab a shuiteáil le ``pip``:"

msgid ""
"Test your installation by importing it in the Python interactive interpreter:"
msgstr ""
"Tástáil do shuiteáil trína iompórtáil san ateangaire idirghníomhach Python:"

msgid "If that command doesn't raise any errors, the installation worked."
msgstr "Mura n-ardaíonn an t-ordú sin aon earráidí, d'oibrigh an tsuiteáil."

msgid "Write your view"
msgstr "Scríobh do thuairim"

msgid ""
"The key to generating PDFs dynamically with Django is that the ReportLab API "
"acts on file-like objects, and Django's :class:`~django.http.FileResponse` "
"objects accept file-like objects."
msgstr ""
"Is é an eochair chun PDFanna a ghiniúint go dinimiciúil le Django ná go "
"ngníomhaíonn an API ReportLab ar rudaí cosúil le comhad, agus glacann rudaí "
"djangos:class: `~django.http.FileResponse` le rudaí cosúil le comhad."

msgid "Here's a \"Hello World\" example::"
msgstr "Seo sampla “Hello World”:"

msgid ""
"The response will automatically set the MIME type :mimetype:`application/"
"pdf` based on the filename extension. This tells browsers that the document "
"is a PDF file, rather than an HTML file or a generic :mimetype:`application/"
"octet-stream` binary content."
msgstr ""
"Socróidh an freagra an cineál MIME go huathoibríoch: mimetype: `application/"
"pdf` bunaithe ar an síneadh ainm comhaid. Insíonn sé seo do bhrabhsálaithe "
"gur comhad PDF é an doiciméad, seachas comhad HTML nó ábhar dénártha "
"ginearic:mimetype: `application/octet-stream`."

msgid ""
"When ``as_attachment=True`` is passed to ``FileResponse``, it sets the "
"appropriate ``Content-Disposition`` header and that tells web browsers to "
"pop-up a dialog box prompting/confirming how to handle the document even if "
"a default is set on the machine. If the ``as_attachment`` parameter is "
"omitted, browsers will handle the PDF using whatever program/plugin they've "
"been configured to use for PDFs."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuirtear ``as_attachment=True`` chuig `FileResponse``, socraíonn sé "
"an ceannteideal ``Content-Disposition`` cuí agus insíonn sé do "
"bhrabhsálaithe gréasáin bosca dialóige a chur in iúl agus ag dearbhú conas "
"an doiciméad a láimhseáil fiú má shocraítear réamhshocrú ar an meaisín. Má "
"fhágann an paraiméadar `as_attachment`, láimhseálfaidh brabhsálaithe an PDF "
"ag baint úsáide as cibé clár/breiseán atá cumraithe acu le húsáid le "
"haghaidh PDFanna."

msgid ""
"You can provide an arbitrary ``filename`` parameter. It'll be used by "
"browsers in the \"Save as...\" dialog."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat paraiméadar treallach ``file`` a sholáthar. Úsáidfidh "
"brabhsálaithe é sa dialóg “Sábháil mar...”."

msgid ""
"You can hook into the ReportLab API: The same buffer passed as the first "
"argument to ``canvas.Canvas`` can be fed to "
"the :class:`~django.http.FileResponse` class."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat dul isteach sa API ReportLab: Is féidir an maolán céanna a "
"rith mar an chéad argóint chuig `Canvas.canvas`` a chothú chuig an "
"aic:class: `~django.http.fileResponse`."

msgid ""
"Note that all subsequent PDF-generation methods are called on the PDF object "
"(in this case, ``p``) -- not on ``buffer``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go ndéantar gach modh giniúna PDF ina dhiaidh sin ar an "
"réad PDF (sa chás seo, `p``) -- ní ar `maolán ``."

msgid ""
"Finally, it's important to call ``showPage()`` and ``save()`` on the PDF "
"file."
msgstr ""
"Mar fhocal scoir, tá sé tábhachtach glaoch ar ``Showpage () ``agus ``save "
"()`` ar an gcomhad PDF."

msgid ""
"ReportLab is not thread-safe. Some of our users have reported odd issues "
"with building PDF-generating Django views that are accessed by many people "
"at the same time."
msgstr ""
"Níl ReportLab sábháilte le snáithe. Thuairiscigh cuid dár n-úsáideoirí "
"saincheisteanna aisteacha maidir le tuairimí Django a ghineann PDF a thógáil "
"ar rochtain ag go leor daoine ag an am céanna."

msgid "Other formats"
msgstr "Formáidí eile"

msgid ""
"Notice that there isn't a lot in these examples that's PDF-specific -- just "
"the bits using ``reportlab``. You can use a similar technique to generate "
"any arbitrary format that you can find a Python library for. Also see :doc:`/"
"howto/outputting-csv` for another example and some techniques you can use "
"when generated text-based formats."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil go leor sna samplaí seo atá sainiúil le PDF - "
"díreach na giotáin ag baint úsáide as `reportlab`. Is féidir leat teicníc "
"den chineál céanna a úsáid chun aon fhormáid treallach a ghiniúint ar féidir "
"leat leabharlann Python a fháil dó. Féach freisin: doc: `/howto/outputting-"
"csv` le haghaidh sampla eile agus roinnt teicnící is féidir leat a úsáid "
"nuair a ghintear formáidí téacs-bhunaithe."

msgid ""
"Django Packages provides a `comparison of packages <https://"
"djangopackages.org/grids/g/pdf/>`_ that help generate PDF files from Django."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Pacáistí Django `comparáid ar phacáistí `_ a chabhraíonn le "
"comhaid PDF a ghiniúint < https://djangopackages.org/grids/g/pdf/> ó Django."

msgid "How to override templates"
msgstr "Conas teimpléid a shárú"

msgid ""
"In your project, you might want to override a template in another Django "
"application, whether it be a third-party application or a contrib "
"application such as ``django.contrib.admin``. You can either put template "
"overrides in your project's templates directory or in an application's "
"templates directory."
msgstr ""
"I do thionscadal, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat teimpléad a shárú in iarratas "
"Django eile, cibé acu is feidhmchlár tríú páirtí é nó feidhmchlár contrib "
"mar ``django.contrib.admin ``. Is féidir leat athshlánú teimpléid a chur in "
"eolaire teimpléid do thionscadail nó in eolaire teimpléid feidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"If you have app and project templates directories that both contain "
"overrides, the default Django template loader will try to load the template "
"from the project-level directory first. In other words, :setting:`DIRS "
"<TEMPLATES-DIRS>` is searched before :setting:`APP_DIRS <TEMPLATES-"
"APP_DIRS>`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá eolairí teimpléid aipeanna agus tionscadail agat ina bhfuil "
"foriompaithe araon acu, déanfaidh an lódóir teimpléad réamhshocraithe Django "
"iarracht an teimpléad a luchtú ón eolaire leibhéal tionscadail <TEMPLATES-"
"APP_DIRS>Is é sin le rá, cuardaítear :setting: `DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>`roimhe "
"sean:setting: `APP_DIRS`."

msgid ""
"Read :ref:`overriding-built-in-widget-templates` if you're looking to do "
"that."
msgstr ""
"Léitheo:ref: `teimpléid overriding-built-in-giuirléid' má tá tú ag iarraidh "
"é sin a dhéanamh."

msgid "Overriding from the project's templates directory"
msgstr "Sárú ó eolaire teimpléid an tionscadail"

msgid ""
"First, we'll explore overriding templates by creating replacement templates "
"in your project's templates directory."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, déanfaimid iniúchadh ar theimpléid sháraitheacha trí theimpléid "
"athsholáthair a chruthú in eolaire teimpléad do thionscadail."

msgid ""
"Let's say you're trying to override the templates for a third-party "
"application called ``blog``, which provides the templates ``blog/post.html`` "
"and ``blog/list.html``. The relevant settings for your project would look "
"like::"
msgstr ""
"Ligean le rá go bhfuil tú ag iarraidh na teimpléid d'fheidhmchlár tríú "
"páirtí ar a dtugtar ``blog ``a sholáthraíonn na teimpléid ``blog/post.html`` "
"agus ``blog/list.html``, a sholáthraíonn na teimpléid ``blog/post.html``. "
"Bheadh cuma na socruithe ábhartha do thionscadal seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The :setting:`TEMPLATES` setting and ``BASE_DIR`` will already exist if you "
"created your project using the default project template. The setting that "
"needs to be modified is :setting:`DIRS<TEMPLATES-DIRS>`."
msgstr ""
"Beidh an socrú: SETTING: `TEMPLATES` agus ``BASE_DIR`` ann cheana féin má "
"chruthaigh tú do thionscadal ag baint úsáide as an teimpléad réamhshocraithe "
"tionscadail. <TEMPLATES-DIRS>Is é an socrú is gá a mhodhnú ná: socrú: `DIRS "
"`."

msgid ""
"These settings assume you have a ``templates`` directory in the root of your "
"project. To override the templates for the ``blog`` app, create a folder in "
"the ``templates`` directory, and add the template files to that folder:"
msgstr ""
"Glacann na socruithe seo leis go bhfuil eolaire ``teimpléad`` agat i "
"bhfréamh do thionscadail. Chun na teimpléid don aip `blog ``a shárú, "
"cruthaigh fillteán san eolaire ``teimpléid``, agus cuir na comhaid teimpléad "
"leis an bhfillteán sin:"

msgid ""
"The template loader first looks for templates in the ``DIRS`` directory. "
"When the views in the ``blog`` app ask for the ``blog/post.html`` and ``blog/"
"list.html`` templates, the loader will return the files you just created."
msgstr ""
"Féachann an lódóir teimpléid ar dtús teimpléid san eolaire ``DIRS`. Nuair a "
"iarrann na tuairimí san aip `blog ``na teimpléid `blog/post.html` agus "
"``blog/list.html`, cuirfidh an lódóir na comhaid a chruthaigh tú díreach ar "
"ais."

msgid "Overriding from an app's template directory"
msgstr "Sárú ó eolaire teimpléad aip"

msgid ""
"Since you're overriding templates located outside of one of your project's "
"apps, it's more common to use the first method and put template overrides in "
"a project's templates folder. If you prefer, however, it's also possible to "
"put the overrides in an app's template directory."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhfuil teimpléid thart agat atá suite taobh amuigh de cheann de "
"na feidhmchláir do thionscadail, tá sé níos coitianta an chéad mhodh a úsáid "
"agus forlíonta teimpléid a chur i bhfillteán teimpléid tionscadail. Más "
"fearr leat, áfach, is féidir na foriomláin a chur in eolaire teimpléad aip "
"freisin."

msgid ""
"First, make sure your template settings are checking inside app directories::"
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, déan cinnte go bhfuil do shocruithe teimpléid á seiceáil taobh "
"istigh de na heolairí aipeanna::"

msgid ""
"If you want to put the template overrides in an app called ``myapp`` and the "
"templates to override are named ``blog/list.html`` and ``blog/post.html``, "
"then your directory structure will look like:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat na teimpléid a shárú in aip ar a dtugtar `myapp`` agus tugtar "
"`blog/list.html`` agus ``blog/post.html`` ar na teimpléid atá le "
"frithsheasmhú, ansin beidh cuma ar do struchtúr eolaire:"

msgid ""
"With :setting:`APP_DIRS<TEMPLATES-APP_DIRS>` set to ``True``, the template "
"loader will look in the app's templates directory and find the templates."
msgstr ""
"Le: Socrú: `APP_DIRS <TEMPLATES-APP_DIRS>`socraithe go ``True``, féachfaidh "
"an lódóir teimpléid in eolaire teimpléid an aip agus gheobhaidh sé na "
"teimpléid."

msgid "Extending an overridden template"
msgstr "Teimpléad athsháraithe a leathnú"

msgid ""
"With your template loaders configured, you can extend a template using "
"the :ttag:`{% extends %}<extends>` template tag whilst at the same time "
"overriding it. This can allow you to make small customizations without "
"needing to reimplement the entire template."
msgstr ""
"Agus do luchtaitheoirí teimpléad cumraithe, is féidir leat teimpléad a "
"leathnú ag baint úsáide as an gclib te <extends>impléad:ttag: `{% extens%}` "
"agus é a shárú ag an am céanna. Féadann sé seo ligean duit saincheaptha "
"beaga a dhéanamh gan gá duit an teimpléad iomlán a athchur i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"For example, you can use this technique to add a custom logo to the ``admin/"
"base_site.html`` template:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, is féidir leat an teicníc seo a úsáid chun lógó saincheaptha a "
"chur leis an teimpléad ``admin/base_site.html``:"

msgid "``templates/admin/base_site.html``"
msgstr "``teimpléid/admin/base_site.html``"

msgid "Key points to note:"
msgstr "Príomhphointí le tabhairt faoi deara:"

msgid ""
"The example creates a file at ``templates/admin/base_site.html`` that uses "
"the configured project-level ``templates`` directory to override ``admin/"
"base_site.html``."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn an sampla comhad ag ``templates/admin/base_site.html`` a "
"úsáideann an eolaire ``teimpléid ``leibhéal tionscadail cumraithe chun "
"`admin/base_site.html`` a shárú."

msgid ""
"The new template extends ``admin/base_site.html``, which is the same "
"template as is being overridden."
msgstr ""
"Leathnaíonn an teimpléad nua ``admin/base_site.html``, arb é an teimpléad "
"céanna atá á athshealbhú."

msgid ""
"The template replaces just the ``branding`` block, adding a custom logo, and "
"using ``block.super`` to retain the prior content."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an teimpléad in ionad an bhloc `branding`, ag cur lógó saincheaptha "
"leis, agus `block.super`` á úsáid chun an t-ábhar roimhe seo a choinneáil."

msgid ""
"The rest of the template is inherited unchanged from ``admin/"
"base_site.html``."
msgstr "Tá an chuid eile den teimpléad gan athrú ó `admin/base_site.html``."

msgid ""
"This technique works because the template loader does not consider the "
"already loaded override template (at ``templates/admin/base_site.html``) "
"when resolving the ``extends`` tag. Combined with ``block.super`` it is a "
"powerful technique to make small customizations."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn an teicníc seo toisc nach ndéanann an lódóir teimpléad a mheas ar "
"an teimpléad athshlánaithe atá luchtaithe cheana féin (ag `templates/admin/"
"base_site.html``) agus an chlib ``extenses ``á réiteach. In éineacht le "
"`block.super`` is teicníc cumhachtach é chun saincheaptha beaga a dhéanamh."

msgid "How to deploy static files"
msgstr "Conas comhaid statacha a imscaradh"

msgid ""
"For an introduction to the use of :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles`, "
"see :doc:`/howto/static-files/index`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh réamhrá ar úsáid:mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles`, féach: doc: "
"`/howto/static-files/index`."

msgid "Serving static files in production"
msgstr "Freastal ar chomhaid statacha sa táirgeadh"

msgid ""
"The basic outline of putting static files into production consists of two "
"steps: run the :djadmin:`collectstatic` command when static files change, "
"then arrange for the collected static files directory "
"(:setting:`STATIC_ROOT`) to be moved to the static file server and served. "
"Depending on the ``staticfiles`` :setting:`STORAGES` alias, files may need "
"to be moved to a new location manually or the :func:`post_process "
"<django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage.post_process>` method "
"of the ``Storage`` class might take care of that."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá sa imlíne bhunúsach ar chomhaid statacha a chur i dtáirgeadh dhá "
"chéim: reáchtáil an t-ordú:djadmin: `collectstatic` nuair a athraíonn "
"comhaid statacha, ansin socraigh go ndéanfar eolaire comhaid statacha "
"bailithe (:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`) a aistriú chuig an bhfreastalaí comhad "
"statach agus a sheirbheáil. "
"<django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage.post_process>Ag brath "
"ar an ailias ``staticfiles```: setting: `STORAGES`, b'fhéidir go gcaithfear "
"comhaid a bhogadh go suíomh nua de láimh nó d'fhéadfadh an modh: func: "
"`post_process `den rang `Storage`` aire a thabhairt dó sin."

msgid ""
"As with all deployment tasks, the devil's in the details. Every production "
"setup will be a bit different, so you'll need to adapt the basic outline to "
"fit your needs. Below are a few common patterns that might help."
msgstr ""
"Mar is amhlaidh le gach tasc imscartha, tá an diabhal sna sonraí. Beidh gach "
"socrú táirgeachta beagán difriúil, mar sin beidh ort an imlíne bhunúsach a "
"oiriúnú chun freastal ar do riachtanais. Seo thíos cúpla patrún coitianta a "
"d'fhéadfadh cabhrú leo."

msgid "Serving the site and your static files from the same server"
msgstr "Freastal ar an suíomh agus do chomhaid statacha ón bhfreastalaí céanna"

msgid ""
"If you want to serve your static files from the same server that's already "
"serving your site, the process may look something like:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat do chuid comhad statacha a sheirbheáil ón bhfreastalaí céanna "
"atá ag freastalú ar do shuíomh cheana féin, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cuma rud "
"éigin ar an bpróiseas:"

msgid "Push your code up to the deployment server."
msgstr "Brúigh do chód suas go dtí an fhreastalaí imscartha."

msgid ""
"On the server, run :djadmin:`collectstatic` to copy all the static files "
"into :setting:`STATIC_ROOT`."
msgstr ""
"Ar an bhfreastalaí, rith: djadmin: `collectstatic` chun na comhaid statacha "
"go léir a chóipeáil ion:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`."

msgid ""
"Configure your web server to serve the files in :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` under "
"the URL :setting:`STATIC_URL`. For example, here's :ref:`how to do this with "
"Apache and mod_wsgi <serving-files>`."
msgstr ""
"Cumraigh do fhreastalaí gréasáin chun na comhaid a sheirbheáil in:setting: "
"`STATIC_ROOT` faoin URL:Setting: `STATIC_URL`. <serving-files>Mar shampla, "
"anseo 's:ref: `conas é seo a dhéanamh le Apache agus mod_wsgi `."

msgid ""
"You'll probably want to automate this process, especially if you've got "
"multiple web servers."
msgstr ""
"Is dócha gur mhaith leat an próiseas seo a uathoibriú, go háirithe má tá "
"freastalaithe gréasáin iolracha agat."

msgid "Serving static files from a dedicated server"
msgstr "Comhaid statacha a sheirbhísiú ó fhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"Most larger Django sites use a separate web server -- i.e., one that's not "
"also running Django -- for serving static files. This server often runs a "
"different type of web server -- faster but less full-featured. Some common "
"choices are:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an chuid is mó de shuíomhanna Django níos mó freastalaí gréasáin "
"ar leithligh - ie, ceann nach bhfuil Django á reáchtáil freisin - chun "
"comhaid statacha a sheirbheáil. Is minic a reáchtáil an freastalaí seo "
"cineál difriúil freastalaí gréasáin - níos gasta ach níos lú lánfheidhme. Is "
"iad roinnt roghanna coitianta:"

msgid ""
"Configuring these servers is out of scope of this document; check each "
"server's respective documentation for instructions."
msgstr ""
"Tá na freastalaithe seo a chumrú as raon feidhme an doiciméad seo; seiceáil "
"doiciméadú gach freastalaí faoi seach le haghaidh treoracha."

msgid ""
"Since your static file server won't be running Django, you'll need to modify "
"the deployment strategy to look something like:"
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é nach mbeidh do fhreastalaí comhad statach ag rith Django, beidh ort "
"an straitéis imscartha a mhodhnú chun cuma rud éigin mar:"

msgid "When your static files change, run :djadmin:`collectstatic` locally."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a athraíonn do chuid comhad statacha, rith: djadmin: `collectstatic` "
"go háitiúil."

msgid ""
"Push your local :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` up to the static file server into the "
"directory that's being served. `rsync <https://rsync.samba.org/>`_ is a "
"common choice for this step since it only needs to transfer the bits of "
"static files that have changed."
msgstr ""
"Brúigh do shuíomh áitiúil: `STATIC_ROOT` suas go dtí an fhreastalaí comhaid "
"statach isteach san eolaire atá á sheirbheáil. Is rogha coitianta é `rsync< "
"https://rsync.samba.org/> `_ don chéim seo ós rud é nach gá dó ach na "
"giotáin comhaid statacha a athraigh a aistriú."

msgid "Serving static files from a cloud service or CDN"
msgstr "Freastal ar chomhaid statacha ó sheirbhís scamall nó CDN"

msgid ""
"Another common tactic is to serve static files from a cloud storage provider "
"like Amazon's S3 and/or a CDN (content delivery network). This lets you "
"ignore the problems of serving static files and can often make for faster-"
"loading web pages (especially when using a CDN)."
msgstr ""
"Tactic coitianta eile is ea freastal ar chomhaid statacha ó sholáthraí "
"stórála néil mar S3 Amazon agus/nó CDN (líonra seachadta ábhair). Ligeann sé "
"seo duit neamhaird a dhéanamh de na fadhbanna a bhaineann le comhaid "
"statacha a sheirbheáil agus is minic a fhágann gur féidir leathanaigh "
"ghréasáin a luchtú níos tapúla (go háirithe agus CDN in úsáid)."

msgid ""
"When using these services, the basic workflow would look a bit like the "
"above, except that instead of using ``rsync`` to transfer your static files "
"to the server you'd need to transfer the static files to the storage "
"provider or CDN."
msgstr ""
"Agus na seirbhísí seo á úsáid agat, bheadh cuma beagáinín cosúil leis an "
"sreabhadh oibre bunúsach thuas, ach amháin in ionad ``rsync` a úsáid chun do "
"chuid comhad statacha a aistriú chuig an bhfreastalaí bheadh ort na comhaid "
"statacha a aistriú chuig an soláthraí stórála nó CDN."

msgid ""
"There's any number of ways you might do this, but if the provider has an "
"API, you can use a :doc:`custom file storage backend </howto/custom-file-"
"storage>` to integrate the CDN with your Django project. If you've written "
"or are using a 3rd party custom storage backend, you can "
"tell :djadmin:`collectstatic` to use it by setting ``staticfiles`` "
"in :setting:`STORAGES`."
msgstr ""
"Tá líon bealaí ar bith ann a d'fhéadfá é seo a dhéanamh, ach má tá API ag an "
"soláthraí, is féidir leat a:doc: `cúltaca stórála comhaid saincheapaithe' a "
"úsáid chun an CDN a chomhtháthú le </howto/custom-file-storage> do "
"thionscadal Django. Má scríobh tú nó má tá cúltaca stórála saincheaptha tríú "
"páirtí á úsáid agat, is féidir leat a rá: djadmin: `collectstatic` chun é a "
"úsáid trí `staticfiles`` a shocrú in:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"For example, if you've written an S3 storage backend in "
"``myproject.storage.S3Storage`` you could use it with::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá cúltaca stórála S3 scríofa agat i "
"``MyProject.Storage.s3Storage`` d'fhéadfá é a úsáid le:"

msgid ""
"Once that's done, all you have to do is run :djadmin:`collectstatic` and "
"your static files would be pushed through your storage package up to S3. If "
"you later needed to switch to a different storage provider, you may only "
"have to change ``staticfiles`` in the :setting:`STORAGES` setting."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh sé sin déanta, níl le déanamh agat ach rith: djadmin: "
"`collectstatic` agus brúfaí do chuid comhad statacha trí do phacáiste "
"stórála suas go dtí S3. Más gá duit aistriú chuig soláthraí stórála difriúil "
"níos déanaí, b'fhéidir nach mbeidh ort ach `staticfiles`` a athrú sa "
"socrúit:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"For details on how you'd write one of these backends, see :doc:`/howto/"
"custom-file-storage`. There are 3rd party apps available that provide "
"storage backends for many common file storage APIs. A good starting point is "
"the `overview at djangopackages.org <https://djangopackages.org/grids/g/"
"storage-backends/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sonraí faoi conas a scríobhfá ceann de na cúltaca seo, féach: "
"doc: `/howto/custom-file-storage`. Tá aipeanna tríú páirtí ar fáil a "
"sholáthraíonn cúltaca stórála do go leor APIs stórála comhaid coitianta. "
"Pointe tosaigh maith is ea an `forbhreathnú ag d< https://djangopackages.org/"
"grids/g/storage-backends/> jangopackages.org`_."

msgid "Learn more"
msgstr "Tuilleadh eolais"

msgid ""
"For complete details on all the settings, commands, template tags, and other "
"pieces included in :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles`, see :doc:`the "
"staticfiles reference </ref/contrib/staticfiles>`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sonraí iomlána ar na socruithe go léir, orduithe, clibeanna "
"teimpléad, agus píosaí eile atá san áireamh in:mod: "
"`django.contrib.staticfiles`, féach: doc: `the staticfiles tagair</ref/"
"contrib/staticfiles> '."

msgid "How to manage static files (e.g. images, JavaScript, CSS)"
msgstr "Conas comhaid statacha a bhainistiú (m.sh. íomhánna, JavaScript, CSS)"

msgid ""
"Websites generally need to serve additional files such as images, "
"JavaScript, or CSS. In Django, we refer to these files as \"static files\".  "
"Django provides :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` to help you manage them."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth ní mór do láithreáin ghréasáin comhaid bhreise a sheirbheáil mar "
"íomhánna, JavaScript, nó CSS. I Django, tagraímid do na comhaid seo mar "
"“comhaid statacha”. Soláthraíonn Django: mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles` "
"chun cabhrú leat iad a bhainistiú."

msgid "This page describes how you can serve these static files."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an leathanach seo cur síos ar conas is féidir leat na comhaid "
"statacha seo a sheirbheáil."

msgid "Configuring static files"
msgstr "Comhaid statacha a chumrú"

msgid ""
"Make sure that ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` is included in "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go bhfuil ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` san áireamh i do: "
"setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid "In your settings file, define :setting:`STATIC_URL`, for example::"
msgstr ""
"I do chomhad socruithe, sainmhínigh: setting: `STATIC_URL`, mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"In your templates, use the :ttag:`static` template tag to build the URL for "
"the given relative path using the configured "
"``staticfiles`` :setting:`STORAGES` alias."
msgstr ""
"I do theimpléid, bain úsáid as an clib teimpléad:ttag: `static` chun an URL "
"a thógáil don chonair choibhneasta tugtha ag baint úsáide as an ainm "
"cumraithe ``staticfiles``:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"Store your static files in a folder called ``static`` in your app. For "
"example ``my_app/static/my_app/example.jpg``."
msgstr ""
"Stóráil do chuid comhad statacha i bhfillteán ar a dtugtar ``static`` i "
"d'aip. Mar shampla ``my_app/static/my_app/example.jpg``."

msgid "Serving the files"
msgstr "Freastal ar na comhaid"

msgid ""
"In addition to these configuration steps, you'll also need to actually serve "
"the static files."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na céimeanna cumraíochta seo, beidh ort na comhaid statacha "
"a sheirbheáil i ndáiríre."

msgid ""
"During development, if you use :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles`, this will "
"be done automatically by :djadmin:`runserver` when :setting:`DEBUG` is set "
"to ``True`` (see :func:`django.contrib.staticfiles.views.serve`)."
msgstr ""
"Le linn na forbartha, má úsáideann tú: mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles`, "
"déanfaidh sé seo go huathoibríoch ar:djadmin: `runserver` nuair a "
"shocraítear: `DEBUG` go `True`` (féach:func: "
"`django.contrib.staticfiles.views.serve`)."

msgid ""
"This method is **grossly inefficient** and probably **insecure**, so it is "
"**unsuitable for production**."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh sean**an-neamhéifeachtúil** agus is dóchúil** neamhchinnteach**, "
"mar sin níl sé**mí-oiriúnach le haghaidh táirgeachta**."

msgid ""
"See :doc:`/howto/static-files/deployment` for proper strategies to serve "
"static files in production environments."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `/cona/comhad statacha/imscaradh `le haghaidh straitéisí cearta "
"chun comhaid statacha a sheirbheáil i dtimpeallachtaí táirgeachta."

msgid ""
"Your project will probably also have static assets that aren't tied to a "
"particular app. In addition to using a ``static/`` directory inside your "
"apps, you can define a list of directories (:setting:`STATICFILES_DIRS`) in "
"your settings file where Django will also look for static files. For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Is dócha go mbeidh sócmhainní statacha ag do thionscadal nach bhfuil "
"ceangailte le aip áirithe. Chomh maith le eolaire `static/`` a úsáid taobh "
"istigh de d'aipeanna, is féidir leat liosta eolairí a shainiú (:setting: "
"`STATICFILES_DIRS`) i do chomhad socruithe áit a lorgfaidh Django comhaid "
"statacha freisin. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"See the documentation for the :setting:`STATICFILES_FINDERS` setting for "
"details on how ``staticfiles`` finds your files."
msgstr ""
"Féach an doiciméadú le haghaidh socrú:setting: `STATICFILES_FINDERS` le "
"haghaidh sonraí faoin gcaoi a aimsíonn ``staticfiles`` do chuid comhad."

msgid "Static file namespacing"
msgstr "Spásáil ainmneacha comhad statach"

msgid ""
"Now we *might* be able to get away with putting our static files directly in "
"``my_app/static/`` (rather than creating another ``my_app`` subdirectory), "
"but it would actually be a bad idea. Django will use the first static file "
"it finds whose name matches, and if you had a static file with the same name "
"in a *different* application, Django would be unable to distinguish between "
"them. We need to be able to point Django at the right one, and the best way "
"to ensure this is by *namespacing* them. That is, by putting those static "
"files inside *another* directory named for the application itself."
msgstr ""
"Anois is féidir linn * a bheith in ann dul amach lenár gcomhaid statacha a "
"chur go díreach i ``my_app/static/`` (seachas fo-eolaire ``my_app ``eile a "
"chruthú), ach is droch-smaoineamh a bheadh ann i ndáiríre. Úsáidfidh Django "
"an chéad chomhad statach a aimsíonn sé a n-ainm a mheaitseálann, agus dá "
"mbeadh comhad statach agat leis an ainm céanna in iarratas* difriol*, ní "
"bheadh Django in ann idirdhealú a dhéanamh eatarthu. Ní mór dúinn a bheith "
"in ann Django a chur in iúl ar an gceann ceart, agus is é an bealach is "
"fearr chun é seo a chinntiú ná trí* spás ainmneacha iad. Is é sin, trí na "
"comhaid statacha sin a chur taobh istigh d'eolaire eil* eile a ainmnítear "
"don fheidhmchlár féin."

msgid ""
"You can namespace static assets in :setting:`STATICFILES_DIRS` by "
"specifying :ref:`prefixes <staticfiles-dirs-prefixes>`."
msgstr ""
"<staticfiles-dirs-prefixes>Is féidir leat spás ainmneacha sócmhainní "
"statacha in:setting: `STATICFILES_DIRS` trí:ref: `prefixes `a shonrú."

msgid "Serving static files during development"
msgstr "Ag freastal ar chomhaid statacha le linn"

msgid ""
"If you use :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` as explained "
"above, :djadmin:`runserver` will do this automatically when :setting:`DEBUG` "
"is set to ``True``. If you don't have ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, you can still manually serve static files "
"using the :func:`django.views.static.serve` view."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú: mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles` mar a mhínítear thuas, "
"déanfaidh: djadmin: `runserver` é seo go huathoibríoch nuair:setting: "
"`DEBUG` socraithe go ``True``. Mura bhfuil ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` "
"agat in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, is féidir leat comhaid statacha a "
"sheirbheáil de láimh fós ag baint úsáide as an amharc:func: "
"`django.views.static.serve`."

msgid ""
"This is not suitable for production use! For some common deployment "
"strategies, see :doc:`/howto/static-files/deployment`."
msgstr ""
"Níl sé seo oiriúnach le húsáid táirgeachta! Maidir le roinnt straitéisí "
"imscartha coitianta, féach:doc: `/howto/static-files/deployment`."

msgid ""
"For example, if your :setting:`STATIC_URL` is defined as ``static/``, you "
"can do this by adding the following snippet to your ``urls.py``::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má shainmhínítear duit:setting: `STATIC_URL` mar ``static/``, "
"is féidir leat é seo a dhéanamh tríd an snippet seo a leanas a chur le do "
"`urls.py``:"

msgid ""
"This helper function works only in debug mode and only if the given prefix "
"is local (e.g. ``static/``) and not a URL (e.g. ``http://static.example.com/"
"``)."
msgstr ""
"Ní oibríonn an fheidhm chúntóra seo ach i mód dífhabhtaithe agus ach amháin "
"má tá an réimír a thugtar áitiúil (m.sh. `static/``) agus ní URL (m.sh. "
"``http://static.example.com/``)."

msgid ""
"Also this helper function only serves the actual :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` "
"folder; it doesn't perform static files discovery "
"like :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles`."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin ní fhreastalaíonn an fheidhm chúntóra seo ach ar an "
"bhfillteán fíor:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`; ní dhéanann sé fionnachtain comhaid "
"statacha cosúil:mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles`."

msgid ""
"Finally, static files are served via a wrapper at the WSGI application "
"layer. As a consequence, static files requests do not pass through the "
"normal :doc:`middleware chain </topics/http/middleware>`."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, seirbheáltar comhaid statacha trí fhilleadh ag an gciseal "
"feidhmchláir WSGI. Mar thoradh air sin, ní théann iarratais ar chomhaid "
"statacha tríd an ngnáth:doc: `</topics/http/middleware> slabhra middleware`."

msgid "Serving files uploaded by a user during development"
msgstr "Freastal ar chomhaid a uaslódálann úsáideoir le linn na"

msgid ""
"During development, you can serve user-uploaded media files "
"from :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` using the :func:`django.views.static.serve` view."
msgstr ""
"Le linn na forbartha, is féidir leat comhaid meán a uaslódáladh ón úsáideoir "
"a sheirbheáil ó:setting: `MEDIA_ROOT` ag baint úsáide as an amharc: func: "
"`django.views.static.serve`."

msgid ""
"For example, if your :setting:`MEDIA_URL` is defined as ``media/``, you can "
"do this by adding the following snippet to your :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF`::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má shainmhínítear duit:setting: `MEDIA_URL` mar ``media/``, is "
"féidir leat é seo a dhéanamh tríd an snippet seo a leanas a chur le "
"duit:setting: `ROOT_URLCONF`:"

msgid ""
"This helper function works only in debug mode and only if the given prefix "
"is local (e.g. ``media/``) and not a URL (e.g. ``http://media.example.com/"
"``)."
msgstr ""
"Ní oibríonn an fheidhm chúntóra seo ach i mód dífhabhtaithe agus ach amháin "
"má tá an réimír a thugtar áitiúil (m.sh. ``media/``) agus ní URL (m.sh. "
"``http://media.example.com/``)."

msgid ""
"When running tests that use actual HTTP requests instead of the built-in "
"testing client (i.e. when using the built-in :class:`LiveServerTestCase "
"<django.test.LiveServerTestCase>`) the static assets need to be served along "
"the rest of the content so the test environment reproduces the real one as "
"faithfully as possible, but ``LiveServerTestCase`` has only very basic "
"static file-serving functionality: It doesn't know about the finders feature "
"of the ``staticfiles`` application and assumes the static content has "
"already been collected under :setting:`STATIC_ROOT`."
msgstr ""
"Agus tástálacha á <django.test.LiveServerTestCase>reáchtáil a úsáideann "
"iarratais HTTP iarbhír in ionad an cliant tástála ionsuite (ie agus an t-"
"ion:class: `LiveServerTestCase 'á úsáid) ní mór na sócmhainní statacha a "
"sheirbheáil feadh an chuid eile den ábhar ionas go atáirgeann an "
"timpeallacht tástála fíor chomh dílis agus is féidir, ach níl ach "
"feidhmiúlacht seirbhíse comhad statach an-bhunúsach aige: Níl a fhios aige "
"faoi ghné aimsitheoirí an `````feidhmchlár staticfiles ``agus glacann sé go "
"bhfuil an t-ábhar statach bailíodh cheana féin fao:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`."

msgid ""
"Because of this, ``staticfiles`` ships its "
"own :class:`django.contrib.staticfiles.testing.StaticLiveServerTestCase`, a "
"subclass of the built-in one that has the ability to transparently serve all "
"the assets during execution of these tests in a way very similar to what we "
"get at development time with ``DEBUG = True``, i.e. without having to "
"collect them using :djadmin:`collectstatic` first."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall air seo, seolann `staticfiles`` a chuid féin: class: "
"`django.contrib.staticFiles.Testing.staticLiveServerTestCase`, fo-aicme den "
"ceann ionsuite a bhfuil sé de chumas freastal ar na sócmhainní go "
"trédhearcach le linn na dtástálacha seo a fhorghníomhú ar bhealach an-"
"chosúil leis an méid a fhaighimid ag am forbartha le `DEBUG = True``, ie gan "
"gá a bhailiú iad ag baint úsáidea:djadmin: `collectstatic` ar dtús."

msgid "Deployment"
msgstr "Imscaradh"

msgid ""
":mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` provides a convenience management command "
"for gathering static files in a single directory so you can serve them "
"easily."
msgstr ""
":mod: Soláthraíonn `django.contrib.staticfiles` ordú bainistíochta "
"áisiúlachta chun comhaid statacha a bhailiú in eolaire amháin ionas gur "
"féidir leat freastal orthu go héasca."

msgid ""
"Set the :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` setting to the directory from which you'd "
"like to serve these files, for example::"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an socrú:setting: `STATIC_ROOT` chuig an eolaire uaidh ar mhaith "
"leat na comhaid seo a sheirbheáil, mar shampla:"

msgid "Run the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command:"
msgstr "Rith an t-ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic`:"

msgid ""
"This will copy all files from your static folders into "
"the :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` directory."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh sé seo gach comhad ó do fhillteáin statacha a chóipeáil isteach "
"san eolair:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`."

msgid ""
"Use a web server of your choice to serve the files. :doc:`/howto/static-"
"files/deployment` covers some common deployment strategies for static files."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid freastalaí gréasáin de do rogha chun na comhaid a sheirbheáil. :doc: `/"
"howto/static-files/deployment` clúdaíonn roinnt straitéisí imscartha "
"coitianta do chomhaid statacha."

msgid ""
"This document has covered the basics and some common usage patterns. For "
"complete details on all the settings, commands, template tags, and other "
"pieces included in :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles`, see :doc:`the "
"staticfiles reference </ref/contrib/staticfiles>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaigh an doiciméad seo na buneilimintí agus roinnt patrúin úsáide "
"coitianta Le haghaidh sonraí iomlána ar na socruithe go léir, orduithe, "
"clibeanna teimpléad, agus píosaí eile atá san áireamh in:mod: "
"`django.contrib.staticfiles`, féach: doc: `the staticfiles tagair</ref/"
"contrib/staticfiles> '."

msgid "How to upgrade Django to a newer version"
msgstr "Conas Django a uasghrádú go leagan níos nuaí"

msgid ""
"While it can be a complex process at times, upgrading to the latest Django "
"version has several benefits:"
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir leis a bheith ina phróiseas casta uaireanta, tá roinnt "
"buntáistí ag uasghrádú chuig an leagan is déanaí Django:"

msgid "New features and improvements are added."
msgstr "Cuirtear gnéithe agus feabhsuithe nua leis."

msgid "Bugs are fixed."
msgstr "Socraítear fabhtanna."

msgid ""
"Older version of Django will eventually no longer receive security updates. "
"(see :ref:`supported-versions-policy`)."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhfaighidh leagan níos sine de Django nuashonruithe slándála a "
"thuilleadh. (féach:ref: `beartas leaganacha tacaíochtaí`)."

msgid ""
"Upgrading as each new Django release is available makes future upgrades less "
"painful by keeping your code base up to date."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéantar uasghrádú de réir mar a bhíonn gach scaoileadh Django nua ar "
"fáil ní bheidh sé chomh pianmhar uasghráduithe sa todhchaí trí do bhunachar "
"cód a choinneáil cothrom le dáta."

msgid ""
"Here are some things to consider to help make your upgrade process as smooth "
"as possible."
msgstr ""
"Seo roinnt rudaí le breithniú chun cabhrú le do phróiseas uasghrádaithe a "
"dhéanamh chomh réidh agus is féidir."

msgid "Required Reading"
msgstr "Léamh Riachtanach"

msgid ""
"If it's your first time doing an upgrade, it is useful to read "
"the :doc:`guide on the different release processes </internals/release-"
"process>`."
msgstr ""
"Más é do chéad uair a dhéanann uasghrádú, tá sé úsáideach an: doc: `treoir "
"maidir leis na próisis scaoilte éagsúla' a léamh </internals/release-"
"process>."

msgid ""
"Afterward, you should familiarize yourself with the changes that were made "
"in the new Django version(s):"
msgstr ""
"Ina dhiaidh sin, ba cheart duit eolas a chur ar na hathruithe a rinneadh sna "
"leaganacha nua Django:"

msgid ""
"Read the :doc:`release notes </releases/index>` for each 'final' release "
"from the one after your current Django version, up to and including the "
"version to which you plan to upgrade."
msgstr ""
"Léigh na:doc: `nótaí scaoil` do gach scaoile</releases/index> adh 'deiridh' "
"ón gceann tar éis do leagan reatha Django, suas go dtí agus san áireamh an "
"leagan a bhfuil sé ar intinn agat uasghrádú air."

msgid ""
"Look at the :doc:`deprecation timeline</internals/deprecation>` for the "
"relevant versions."
msgstr ""
"Féach ar an :doc:`amlíne dímheasa</internals/dímheas>` le haghaidh na "
"leaganacha cuí."

msgid ""
"Pay particular attention to backwards incompatible changes to get a clear "
"idea of what will be needed for a successful upgrade."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair aird ar leith ar athruithe neamhchomhoiriúnacha ar ais chun tuairim "
"shoiléir a fháil ar cad a bheidh ag teastáil le haghaidh uasghrádú rathúil."

msgid ""
"If you're upgrading through more than one feature version (e.g. 2.0 to 2.2), "
"it's usually easier to upgrade through each feature release incrementally "
"(2.0 to 2.1 to 2.2) rather than to make all the changes for each feature "
"release at once. For each feature release, use the latest patch release "
"(e.g. for 2.1, use 2.1.15)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag uasghrádú trí níos mó ná leagan gné amháin (m.sh. 2.0 go 2.2), "
"is gnách go mbíonn sé níos éasca uasghrádú trí gach scaoileadh gné go "
"chéimiúil (2.0 go 2.1 go 2.2) seachas na hathruithe go léir a dhéanamh do "
"gach scaoileadh gné ag an am céanna. Maidir le gach scaoileadh gné, bain "
"úsáid as an scaoileadh paiste is déanaí (m.sh. le haghaidh 2.1, bain úsáid "
"as 2.1.15)."

msgid ""
"The same incremental upgrade approach is recommended when upgrading from one "
"LTS to the next."
msgstr ""
"Moltar an cur chuige uasghrádaithe incriminteach céanna agus tú ag uasghrádú "
"ó LTS amháin go dtí an chéad cheann eile."

msgid "Dependencies"
msgstr "Spleithiúlachtaí"

msgid ""
"In most cases it will be necessary to upgrade to the latest version of your "
"Django-related dependencies as well. If the Django version was recently "
"released or if some of your dependencies are not well-maintained, some of "
"your dependencies may not yet support the new Django version. In these cases "
"you may have to wait until new versions of your dependencies are released."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna beidh sé riachtanach uasghrádú a dhéanamh go dtí an "
"leagan is déanaí de do spleáchais a bhaineann le Django freisin. Má "
"scaoileadh an leagan Django le déanaí nó mura ndéantar cuid de do spleáchais "
"a chothabháil go maith, b'fhéidir nach dtacaíonn cuid de do spleáchais leis "
"an leagan nua Django fós. Sna cásanna seo b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort fanacht go "
"dtí go scaoilfear leaganacha nua de do spleáchais."

msgid "Resolving deprecation warnings"
msgstr "Rabhadh dífhabhtaithe a réiteach"

msgid ""
"Before upgrading, it's a good idea to resolve any deprecation warnings "
"raised by your project while using your current version of Django. Fixing "
"these warnings before upgrading ensures that you're informed about areas of "
"the code that need altering."
msgstr ""
"Sula ndéanfar uasghrádú, is smaoineamh maith é aon rabhaidh dímheasa a "
"d’ardaigh do thionscadal a réiteach agus do leagan reatha de Django á úsáid "
"agat. Cinntíonn sé sin go gcuirtear ar an eolas thú faoi réimsí den chód ar "
"gá iad a athrú má cheartaítear na rabhaidh seo roimh uasghrádú."

msgid ""
"In Python, deprecation warnings are silenced by default. You must turn them "
"on using the ``-Wa`` Python command line option or "
"the :envvar:`PYTHONWARNINGS` environment variable. For example, to show "
"warnings while running tests:"
msgstr ""
"I Python, cuirtear rabhaidh dímheasa ina dtost de réir réamhshocraithe. Ní "
"mór duit iad a chur ar siúl agus úsáid á baint as an rogha líne ordaithe "
"Python ``-Wa`` nó as an athróg timpeallachta :envvar:`PYTHONWARNINGS`. Mar "
"shampla, chun rabhaidh a thaispeáint agus tástálacha á rith:"

msgid ""
"If you're not using the Django test runner, you may need to also ensure that "
"any console output is not captured which would hide deprecation warnings. "
"For example, if you use `pytest <https://docs.pytest.org/>`__:"
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú ag baint úsáide as an rádala tástála Django, b'fhéidir go "
"mbeadh ort a chinntiú freisin nach bhfuil aon aschur consól a gabhadh a "
"cheilt rabhaidh dímheasa. Mar shampla, má úsáideann tú `pytest <https://"
"docs.pytest.org/>`__:"

msgid ""
"Resolve any deprecation warnings with your current version of Django before "
"continuing the upgrade process."
msgstr ""
"Réiteach aon rabhaidh dífhabhtaithe le do leagan reatha de Django sula "
"leanann tú leis an bpróiseas uasghrádaithe."

msgid ""
"Third party applications might use deprecated APIs in order to support "
"multiple versions of Django, so deprecation warnings in packages you've "
"installed don't necessarily indicate a problem. If a package doesn't support "
"the latest version of Django, consider raising an issue or sending a pull "
"request for it."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh feidhmchláir tríú páirtí APIs measartha a úsáid d'fhonn tacú le "
"leaganacha iolracha de Django, mar sin ní gá go léiríonn rabhaidh "
"díluasaithe i bpacáistí atá suiteáilte agat fadhb. Mura dtacaíonn pacáiste "
"leis an leagan is déanaí de Django, smaoinigh ar cheist a ardú nó iarratas "
"tarraingthe a sheoladh air."

msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Suiteáil"

msgid ""
"Once you're ready, it is time to :doc:`install the new Django version </"
"topics/install>`. If you are using a :mod:`virtual environment <venv>` and "
"it is a major upgrade, you might want to set up a new environment with all "
"the dependencies first."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh tú réidh, tá sé in am: doc: `an leagan nua Django a "
"shuiteáil</topics/install> `. Má tá a:mod: `timpeallacht fhíorúil á úsáid "
"agat agus <venv>is uasghrádú mór é, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat timpeallacht "
"nua a bhunú leis na spleáchais go léir ar dtús."

msgid ""
"If you installed Django with pip_, you can use the ``--upgrade`` or ``-U`` "
"flag:"
msgstr ""
"Má shuiteáil tú Django le pip_, is féidir leat an bratach ``--upgrade`` nó "
"``-U`` a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"When the new environment is set up, :doc:`run the full test suite </topics/"
"testing/overview>` for your application. Again, it's useful to turn on "
"deprecation warnings on so they're shown in the test output (you can also "
"use the flag if you test your app manually using ``manage.py runserver``):"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuirtear an timpeallacht nua ar bun, :doc: `reáchtáil an t-suite "
"tástála iomlán` do d'iarratas. </topics/testing/overview> Arís, tá sé "
"úsáideach rabhaidh díscrúdaithe a chasadh air ionas go dtaispeánfar iad san "
"aschur tástála (is féidir leat an bratach a úsáid freisin má thástáil tú "
"d'aip de láimh ag baint úsáide as `manage.py runserver ``):"

msgid ""
"After you have run the tests, fix any failures. While you have the release "
"notes fresh in your mind, it may also be a good time to take advantage of "
"new features in Django by refactoring your code to eliminate any deprecation "
"warnings."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis duit na tástálacha a reáchtáil, socraigh aon teipeanna. Cé go bhfuil "
"na nótaí scaoilte úr i d'intinn agat, b'fhéidir gur am maith é freisin leas "
"a bhaint as gnéithe nua i Django trí do chód a athfhabhtú chun deireadh a "
"chur le haon rabhaidh díghrádaithe."

msgid ""
"When you are sufficiently confident your app works with the new version of "
"Django, you're ready to go ahead and :doc:`deploy </howto/deployment/index>` "
"your upgraded Django project."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn tú sách muiníneach go n-oibríonn d’aip leis an leagan nua de "
"Django, tá tú réidh le dul ar aghaidh agus : doc: `do thionscadal Django "
"uasghrádaithe a imscaradh </howto/deployment/index>`."

msgid ""
"If you are using caching provided by Django, you should consider clearing "
"your cache after upgrading. Otherwise you may run into problems, for "
"example, if you are caching pickled objects as these objects are not "
"guaranteed to be pickle-compatible across Django versions. A past instance "
"of incompatibility was caching pickled :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` "
"objects, either directly or indirectly via "
"the :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_page` decorator."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag úsáid caching a sholáthraíonn Django, ba cheart duit smaoineamh "
"ar do thaisce a ghlanadh tar éis uasghrádú. Seachas sin d'fhéadfadh "
"fadhbanna a bheith ort, mar shampla, má tá rudaí picilte á chaitheamh agat "
"mar ní ráthaítear go mbeidh na rudaí seo comhoiriúnach le picilí ar fud "
"leaganacha Django. Cás neamhchomhoiriúnachta a bhí roimhe seo ná rudaí "
"roghnaithe: class: `~django.http.http.httpResponse` a chaitheamh, go díreach "
"nó go hindíreach tríd an maisitheoir: :func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_page`."

msgid "How to install Django on Windows"
msgstr "Conas Django a shuiteáil ar Windows"

msgid ""
"This document will guide you through installing Python 3.14 and Django on "
"Windows. It also provides instructions for setting up a virtual environment, "
"which makes it easier to work on Python projects. This is meant as a "
"beginner's guide for users working on Django projects and does not reflect "
"how Django should be installed when developing changes for Django itself."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The steps in this guide have been tested with Windows 10. In other versions, "
"the steps would be similar. You will need to be familiar with using the "
"Windows command prompt."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh tástáil ar na céimeanna sa treoir seo le Windows 10. I leaganacha "
"eile, bheadh na céimeanna cosúil leis. Caithfidh tú a bheith eolach ar an "
"ordú Windows a úsáid a bhaint as pras."

msgid "Install Python"
msgstr "Suiteáil Python"

msgid ""
"Django is a Python web framework, thus requiring Python to be installed on "
"your machine. At the time of writing, Python 3.14 is the latest version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To install Python on your machine go to https://www.python.org/downloads/. "
"The website should offer you a download button for the latest Python "
"version. Download the executable installer and run it. Check the boxes next "
"to \"Install launcher for all users (recommended)\" then click \"Install "
"Now\"."
msgstr ""
"Chun Python a shuiteáil ar do mheaisín téigh chuig https://www.python.org/"
"downloads/. Ba chóir go dtabharfadh an suíomh Gréasáin cnaipe íoslódála duit "
"don leagan Python is déanaí. Íoslódáil an suiteálaí inúsáidte agus rith é. "
"Seiceáil na boscaí in aice le “Suiteáil lainseálaí do gach úsáideoir "
"(moltar)” ansin cliceáil “Suiteáil Anois”."

msgid ""
"After installation, open the command prompt and check that the Python "
"version matches the version you installed by executing:"
msgstr ""
"Tar éis é a shuiteáil, oscail an ordú go pras agus seiceáil go bhfuil an "
"leagan Python ag teacht leis an leagan a shuiteáil tú trí:"

msgid "``py`` is not recognized or found"
msgstr "Ní aithnítear ná ní aimsítear ``py``"

msgid ""
"Depending on how you've installed Python (such as via the Microsoft Store), "
"``py`` may not be available in the command prompt."
msgstr ""
"Ag brath ar an gcaoi a bhfuil Python suiteáilte agat (mar shampla trí "
"Microsoft Store), b'fhéidir nach mbeidh `py`` ar fáil sa phras ordaithe."

msgid ""
"You will then need to use ``python`` instead of ``py`` when entering "
"commands."
msgstr ""
"Ansin beidh ort ``python`` a úsáid in ionad ``py`` agus orduithe á iontráil "
"agat."

msgid "For more details, see :doc:`python:using/windows` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach:doc: `python:using/windows` doiciméadú."

msgid "About ``pip``"
msgstr "Maidir le ``pip``"

msgid ""
":pypi:`pip` is a package manager for Python and is included by default with "
"the Python installer. It helps to install and uninstall Python packages "
"(such as Django!). For the rest of the installation, we'll use ``pip`` to "
"install Python packages from the command line."
msgstr ""
":pypi: Is bainisteoir pacáiste é `pip` do Python agus tá sé san áireamh de "
"réir réamhshocraithe leis an suiteálaí Python. Cuidíonn sé le pacáistí "
"Python a shuiteáil agus a dhíshuiteáil (mar shampla Django!). Maidir leis an "
"gcuid eile den suiteáil, úsáidfimid ``pip`` chun pacáistí Python a shuiteáil "
"ón líne ordaithe."

msgid "Setting up a virtual environment"
msgstr "Timpeallacht fhíorúil a bhunú"

msgid ""
"It is best practice to provide a dedicated environment for each Django "
"project you create. There are many options to manage environments and "
"packages within the Python ecosystem, some of which are recommended in the "
"`Python documentation <https://packaging.python.org/guides/tool-"
"recommendations/>`_. Python itself comes with :doc:`venv <python:tutorial/"
"venv>` for managing environments which we will use for this guide."
msgstr ""
"Is é an cleachtas is fearr timpeallacht thiomnaithe a sholáthar do gach "
"tionscadal Django a chruthaíonn tú. Tá go leor roghanna ann chun "
"timpeallachtaí agus pacáistí a bhainistiú laistigh den éiceachóras Python, "
"moltar cuid acu sa doiciméadú Python'_ < https://packaging.python.org/guides/"
"tool-recommendations/>. Tagann Python féin le:doc: `venv` chun "
"timpeallachtaí <python:tutorial/venv> a bhainistiú a úsáidfimid don treoir "
"seo."

msgid ""
"To create a virtual environment for your project, open a new command prompt, "
"navigate to the folder where you want to create your project and then enter "
"the following:"
msgstr ""
"Chun timpeallacht fhíorúil a chruthú do do thionscadal, oscail ordú nua "
"leid, déan nascleanúint chuig an bhfillteán inar mian leat do thionscadal a "
"chruthú agus ansin cuir isteach iad seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"This will create a folder called 'project-name' if it does not already exist "
"and set up the virtual environment. To activate the environment, run:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthóidh sé seo fillteán ar a dtugtar 'ainm tionscadail' mura bhfuil sé ann "
"cheana féin agus bunóidh sé an timpeallacht fhíorúil ar bun. Chun an "
"timpeallacht a ghníomhachtú, rith:"

msgid ""
"The virtual environment will be activated and you'll see \"(project-name)\" "
"next to the command prompt to designate that. Each time you start a new "
"command prompt, you'll need to activate the environment again."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear an timpeallacht fhíorúil i ngníomh agus feicfidh tú “(ainm "
"tionscadail)” in aice leis an ordú pras chun é sin a ainmniú. Gach uair a "
"thosaíonn tú pras ordaithe nua, beidh ort an timpeallacht a ghníomhachtú "
"arís."

msgid "Install Django"
msgstr "Suiteáil Django"

msgid ""
"Django can be installed easily using ``pip`` within your virtual environment."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir Django a shuiteáil go héasca ag baint úsáide as ``pip`` laistigh "
"de do thimpeallacht fhíorúil."

msgid ""
"In the command prompt, ensure your virtual environment is active, and "
"execute the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Sa ordú leid, cinntigh go bhfuil do thimpeallacht fhíorúil gníomhach, agus "
"déan an t-ordú seo a leanas:"

msgid "This will download and install the latest Django release."
msgstr "Íoslódóidh agus suiteálfaidh sé seo an eisiúint Django is déanaí."

msgid ""
"After the installation has completed, you can verify your Django "
"installation by executing ``django-admin --version`` in the command prompt."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis don tsuiteáil a bheith críochnaithe, is féidir leat do shuiteáil "
"Django a fhíorú trí ``django-admin --version ``a fhorghníomhú sa phras "
"ordaithe."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`database-installation` for information on database installation "
"with Django."
msgstr ""
"Féach: ref: `suiteáil bunachar sonraí` le haghaidh faisnéise maidir le "
"suiteáil bunachar sonraí le Django."

msgid "Colored terminal output"
msgstr "Aschur críochfoirt daite"

msgid ""
"A quality-of-life feature adds colored (rather than monochrome) output to "
"the terminal. In modern terminals this should work for both CMD and "
"PowerShell. If for some reason this needs to be disabled, set the "
"environmental variable :envvar:`DJANGO_COLORS` to ``nocolor``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann gné cáilíochta beatha aschur daite (seachas monacrómach) leis an "
"gcríochfort. I gcríochfoirt nua-aimseartha ba chóir go n-oibreodh sé seo do "
"CMD agus PowerShell araon. Más gá é seo a dhíchumasú ar chúis éigin, "
"socraigh an t-athróg comhshaoil: envvar: `DJANGO_COLORS` go `nocolor``."

msgid ""
"On older Windows versions, or legacy terminals, :pypi:`colorama` 0.4.6+ must "
"be installed to enable syntax coloring:"
msgstr ""
"Ar leaganacha Windows níos sine, nó críochfoirt oidhreachta, "
"caithfear :pypi: `colorama` 0.4.6+ a shuiteáil chun dathú comhréireachta a "
"chumasú:"

msgid "See :ref:`syntax-coloring` for more information on color settings."
msgstr ""
"Féach: ref: `syntax-coloring` le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoi "
"shocruithe dathanna."

msgid "Common pitfalls"
msgstr "Gaillteanna coitianta"

msgid ""
"If ``django-admin`` only displays the help text no matter what arguments it "
"is given, there is probably a problem with the file association in Windows. "
"Check if there is more than one environment variable set for running Python "
"scripts in ``PATH``. This usually occurs when there is more than one Python "
"version installed."
msgstr ""
"Mura dtaispeánann ``django-admin ``ach an téacs cabhrach is cuma cad iad na "
"hargóintí a thugtar air, is dócha go bhfuil fadhb ann leis an gcomhlachas "
"comhaid i Windows. Seiceáil an bhfuil níos mó ná athróg comhshaoil amháin "
"atá leagtha síos chun scripteanna Python a reáchtáil i `PATH``. Tarlaíonn sé "
"seo de ghnáth nuair a bhíonn níos mó ná leagan Python amháin suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"If you are connecting to the internet behind a proxy, there might be "
"problems in running the command ``py -m pip install Django``. Set the "
"environment variables for proxy configuration in the command prompt as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag nascadh leis an idirlíon taobh thiar de seachfhreastalaí, "
"d'fhéadfadh fadhbanna a bheith ann leis an ordú `` py -m pip install "
"Django`` a rith. Socraigh na hathróga timpeallachta le haghaidh cumraíochta "
"seachfhreastalaí sa leid ordaithe mar seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"In general, Django assumes that ``UTF-8`` encoding is used for I/O. This may "
"cause problems if your system is set to use a different encoding. Recent "
"versions of Python allow setting the :envvar:`PYTHONUTF8` environment "
"variable in order to force a ``UTF-8`` encoding. Windows 10 also provides a "
"system-wide setting by checking ``Use Unicode UTF-8 for worldwide language "
"support`` in :menuselection:`Language --> Administrative Language Settings --"
"> Change system locale` in system settings."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, glacann Django leis go n-úsáidtear ionchódú `UTF-8` le "
"haghaidh I/O. D'fhéadfadh fadhbanna a bheith ina chúis leis seo má tá do "
"chóras socraithe chun ionchódú difriúil a úsáid. Ligeann leaganacha le "
"déanaí de Python an athróg comhshaoil: envvar: `PYTHONUTF8` a shocrú d'fhonn "
"ionchódú ``UTF-8`` a chur i bhfeidhm. Soláthraíonn Windows 10 socrú ar fud "
"an chórais freisin trí sheiceáil ``Úsáid Unicode UTF-8 le haghaidh "
"tacaíochta teanga ar fud an domhain`` in:menuselection: `Teanga -> Socruithe "
"Teanga Riaracháin -> Athraigh an chórais áitiúil' i socruithe an chórais."

msgid "How to create database migrations"
msgstr "Conas imirce bunachar sonraí a chruthú"

msgid ""
"This document explains how to structure and write database migrations for "
"different scenarios you might encounter. For introductory material on "
"migrations, see :doc:`the topic guide </topics/migrations>`."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo conas imirce bunachar sonraí a struchtúrú agus a "
"scríobh do chásanna éagsúla a d'fhéad Le haghaidh ábhar tosaigh maidir le "
"himirce, féach:doc: `an treoir ábhair `</topics/migrations>."

msgid "Data migrations and multiple databases"
msgstr "Imirce sonraí agus bunachair sonraí iolracha"

msgid ""
"When using multiple databases, you may need to figure out whether or not to "
"run a migration against a particular database. For example, you may want to "
"**only** run a migration on a particular database."
msgstr ""
"Agus bunachair sonraí iolracha á úsáid agat, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort a fháil "
"amach cibé acu imirce a reáchtáil i gcoinne bunachar sonraí áirithe nó Mar "
"shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat imirce a reáchtáil** ar bhunachar sonraí "
"áirithe."

msgid ""
"In order to do that you can check the database connection's alias inside a "
"``RunPython`` operation by looking at the ``schema_editor.connection.alias`` "
"attribute::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn é sin a dhéanamh is féidir leat ainm an nasc bunachar sonraí a "
"sheiceáil taobh istigh d'oibríocht ``RunPython`` trí fhéachaint ar an tréith "
"`schema_editor.connection.alias``:"

msgid ""
"You can also provide hints that will be passed to "
"the :meth:`allow_migrate()` method of database routers as ``**hints``:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat leideanna a sholáthar freisin a chuirfear ar aghaidh chuig an "
"modh:meth: `allow_migration () `de ródairí bunachar sonraí mar `**hints``:"

msgid "``myapp/dbrouters.py``"
msgstr "``myapp/dbrouters.py``"

msgid "Then, to leverage this in your migrations, do the following::"
msgstr "Ansin, chun é seo a ghiaráil i do imirce, déan an méid seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"If your ``RunPython`` or ``RunSQL`` operation only affects one model, it's "
"good practice to pass ``model_name`` as a hint to make it as transparent as "
"possible to the router. This is especially important for reusable and third-"
"party apps."
msgstr ""
"Mura ndéanann d'oibríocht `` RunPython`` nó `` RunSQL`` difear ach do mhúnla "
"amháin, is dea-chleachtas é `` model_name`` a chur ar aghaidh mar leid chun "
"é a dhéanamh chomh trédhearcach agus is féidir don ródaire. Tá sé seo "
"tábhachtach go háirithe maidir le haipeanna ath-inúsáidte agus tríú páirtí."

msgid "Migrations that add unique fields"
msgstr "Imirce a chuireann réimsí uathúla leis"

msgid ""
"Applying a \"plain\" migration that adds a unique non-nullable field to a "
"table with existing rows will raise an error because the value used to "
"populate existing rows is generated only once, thus breaking the unique "
"constraint."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear ascnamh “gnáth” i bhfeidhm a chuireann réimse uathúil neamh-"
"neamhnithe le tábla le sraitheanna atá ann cheana féin, ardófar earráid mar "
"ní ghintear an luach a úsáidtear chun sraitheanna atá ann cheana a líonadh "
"ach uair amháin, rud a bhriseann an srian uathúil."

msgid ""
"Therefore, the following steps should be taken. In this example, we'll add a "
"non-nullable :class:`~django.db.models.UUIDField` with a default value. "
"Modify the respective field according to your needs."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, ba chóir na céimeanna seo a leanas a dhéanamh. Sa sampla seo, "
"cuirfimid neamh-nullable:class: `~django.db.models.uuidfield` le luach "
"réamhshocraithe. Athraigh an réimse faoi seach de réir do riachtanas."

msgid ""
"Add the field on your model with ``default=uuid.uuid4`` and ``unique=True`` "
"arguments (choose an appropriate default for the type of the field you're "
"adding)."
msgstr ""
"Cuir an réimse ar do mhúnla le `default=uuid.uuid4`` agus ``Unique=True`` "
"argóintí (roghnaigh réamhshocrú cuí don chineál réimse atá á chur leis)."

msgid ""
"Run the :djadmin:`makemigrations` command. This should generate a migration "
"with an ``AddField`` operation."
msgstr ""
"Rith an t-ordú:djadmin: `makemigrations`. Ba chóir go gcruthódh sé seo "
"imirce le hoibríocht `AddField`."

msgid ""
"Generate two empty migration files for the same app by running "
"``makemigrations myapp --empty`` twice. We've renamed the migration files to "
"give them meaningful names in the examples below."
msgstr ""
"Ginigh dhá chomhad imirce folamh don aip céanna trí `makemigrations myapp --"
"empty` a reáchtáil faoi dhó. Rinneamar athainmniú na comhaid imirce chun "
"ainmneacha bríocha a thabhairt dóibh sna samplaí thíos."

msgid ""
"Copy the ``AddField`` operation from the auto-generated migration (the first "
"of the three new files) to the last migration, change ``AddField`` to "
"``AlterField``, and add imports of ``uuid`` and ``models``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cóipeáil an oibríocht `AddField` ón imirce uathoibríoch a ghintear (an chéad "
"cheann de na trí chomhad nua) go dtí an imirce deireanach, athraigh "
"``Addfield`` go `AlterField`, agus cuir allmhairí `uuid`` agus `samhlacha "
"``. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``0006_remove_uuid_null.py``"
msgstr "``0006_remove_uuid_null.py``"

msgid ""
"Edit the first migration file. The generated migration class should look "
"similar to this:"
msgstr ""
"Cuir an chéad chomhad imirce in eagar. Ba chóir go mbeadh cuma cosúil leis "
"seo ar an rang imirce ginte:"

msgid "``0004_add_uuid_field.py``"
msgstr "``0004_add_uuid_field.py``"

msgid ""
"Change ``unique=True`` to ``null=True`` -- this will create the intermediary "
"null field and defer creating the unique constraint until we've populated "
"unique values on all the rows."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh ``unique=True`` go ``Null=True`` - cruthóidh sé seo an réimse null "
"idirghabhálaí agus cuirfidh sé siar an srian uathúil a chruthú go dtí go "
"mbeidh luachanna uathúla curtha againn ar na sraitheanna go léir."

msgid ""
"In the first empty migration file, add "
"a :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` "
"or :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operation to generate a "
"unique value (UUID in the example) for each existing row. Also add an import "
"of ``uuid``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Sa chéad chomhad imirce folamh, cuir a:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` nó:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` oibríocht chun luach uathúil (UUID "
"sa sampla) a ghiniúint do gach sraith atá ann cheana. Cuir allmhairiú ``uuid "
"``leis freisin. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``0005_populate_uuid_values.py``"
msgstr "``0005_populate_uuid_values.py``"

msgid ""
"Now you can apply the migrations as usual with the :djadmin:`migrate` "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Anois is féidir leat na himirce a chur i bhfeidhm mar is gnách leis an "
"ordú:djadmin: `migrate`."

msgid ""
"Note there is a race condition if you allow objects to be created while this "
"migration is running. Objects created after the ``AddField`` and before "
"``RunPython`` will have their original ``uuid``’s overwritten."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil coinníoll rása ann má cheadaíonn tú rudaí a "
"chruthú agus an imirce seo á rith. Beidh a “uuid” bunaidh forscríofa ag "
"rudaí a cruthaíodh tar éis an ``Addfield`` agus roimh ``Runpython``."

msgid "Non-atomic migrations"
msgstr "Imirce neamh-adamhacha"

msgid ""
"On databases that support DDL transactions (SQLite and PostgreSQL), "
"migrations will run inside a transaction by default. For use cases such as "
"performing data migrations on large tables, you may want to prevent a "
"migration from running in a transaction by setting the ``atomic`` attribute "
"to ``False``::"
msgstr ""
"Ar bhunachair sonraí a thacaíonn le hidirbhearta DDL (SQLite agus "
"PostgreSQL), rithfidh imirce taobh istigh d'idirbheart de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Maidir le cásanna úsáide mar imirce sonraí a dhéanamh ar "
"tháblaí móra, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat imirce a chosc ó rith in idirbheart "
"tríd an tréith ``atomic` a shocrú do `False``:"

msgid ""
"Within such a migration, all operations are run without a transaction. It's "
"possible to execute parts of the migration inside a transaction "
"using :func:`~django.db.transaction.atomic()` or by passing ``atomic=True`` "
"to ``RunPython``."
msgstr ""
"Laistigh d'imirce den sórt sin, reáchtáiltear gach oibríocht gan idirbheart. "
"Is féidir codanna den imirce a fhorghníomhú taobh istigh d'idirbheart ag "
"baint úsáid:func: `~django.db.transaction.atomic () `nó trí `Atomic=True`` a "
"chur chuig `RunPython``."

msgid ""
"Here's an example of a non-atomic data migration that updates a large table "
"in smaller batches::"
msgstr ""
"Seo sampla d'imirce sonraí neamh-adamhacha a nuashonraíonn tábla mór i "
"mbaisceanna níos lú:"

msgid ""
"The ``atomic`` attribute doesn't have an effect on databases that don't "
"support DDL transactions (e.g. MySQL, Oracle). (MySQL's `atomic DDL "
"statement support <https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/en/atomic-ddl.html>`_ "
"refers to individual statements rather than multiple statements wrapped in a "
"transaction that can be rolled back.)"
msgstr ""
"Níl éifeacht ag an tréith `atomic` ar bhunachair sonraí nach dtacaíonn le "
"hidirbhearta DDL (m.sh. MySQL, Oracle). (Tagraíonn “tacaíocht ráiteas DDL "
"adamhach” MySQL < https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/en/atomic-ddl.html> do "
"ráitis aonair seachas ráitis iolracha atá fillte in idirbheart is féidir a "
"rolladh ar ais.)"

msgid "Controlling the order of migrations"
msgstr "Ord na n-imirce a rialú"

msgid ""
"Django determines the order in which migrations should be applied not by the "
"filename of each migration, but by building a graph using two properties on "
"the ``Migration`` class: ``dependencies`` and ``run_before``."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann Django an t-ord ina gcaithfear imirce a chur i bhfeidhm ní trí ainm "
"comhaid gach imirce, ach trí graf a thógáil ag baint úsáide as dhá airíonna "
"ar an aicme ``Imigration``: `dependencies`` agus ``run_before ``."

msgid ""
"If you've used the :djadmin:`makemigrations` command you've probably already "
"seen ``dependencies`` in action because auto-created migrations have this "
"defined as part of their creation process."
msgstr ""
"Má d'úsáid tú an t-ordú:djadmin: `makemigrations` is dócha go bhfaca tú "
"``dependencies`` i ngníomh cheana féin toisc go bhfuil sé seo sainmhínithe "
"ag imirce uathoibríoch mar chuid dá bpróiseas cruthaithe."

msgid "The ``dependencies`` property is declared like this::"
msgstr "Dearbhaítear an maoin `spleáchais ``mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Usually this will be enough, but from time to time you may need to ensure "
"that your migration runs *before* other migrations. This is useful, for "
"example, to make third-party apps' migrations run *after* "
"your :setting:`AUTH_USER_MODEL` replacement."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth beidh sé seo go leor, ach ó am go ham b'fhéidir go gcaithfidh tú a "
"chinntiú go ritheann d'imirce* roim* imirce eile. Tá sé seo úsáideach, mar "
"shampla, chun imirce feidhmchláir tríú páirtí a reáchtáil* tar éis "
"d'athsholáthar your:setting: `AUTH_USER_MODEL`."

msgid ""
"To achieve this, place all migrations that should depend on yours in the "
"``run_before`` attribute on your ``Migration`` class::"
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a bhaint amach, cuir na himirce go léir ar chóir a bheith ag "
"brath ar leatsa sa tréith ``run_before ``ar do rang ``Immigration``:"

msgid ""
"Prefer using ``dependencies`` over ``run_before`` when possible. You should "
"only use ``run_before`` if it is undesirable or impractical to specify "
"``dependencies`` in the migration which you want to run after the one you "
"are writing."
msgstr ""
"Is fearr leat ``dependencies`` a úsáid seachas ``run_before ``nuair is "
"féidir. Níor cheart duit ``run_before ``a úsáid ach mura bhfuil sé "
"inmhianaithe nó neamhphraiticiúil ``spleáchais`` a shonrú san imirce a "
"theastaíonn uait a reáchtáil tar éis an ceann atá á scríobh agat."

msgid "Migrating data between third-party apps"
msgstr "Sonraí a imirce idir apps tríú páirtí"

msgid ""
"You can use a data migration to move data from one third-party application "
"to another."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat imirce sonraí a úsáid chun sonraí a aistriú ó fheidhmchlár "
"tríú páirtí amháin go ceann eile."

msgid ""
"If you plan to remove the old app later, you'll need to set the "
"``dependencies`` property based on whether or not the old app is installed. "
"Otherwise, you'll have missing dependencies once you uninstall the old app. "
"Similarly, you'll need to catch :exc:`LookupError` in the "
"``apps.get_model()`` call that retrieves models from the old app. This "
"approach allows you to deploy your project anywhere without first installing "
"and then uninstalling the old app."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé ar intinn agat an sean-aip a bhaint níos déanaí, beidh ort an maoin "
"`spleáchais ``a shocrú bunaithe ar cibé an bhfuil an sean-aip suiteáilte nó "
"nach bhfuil. Seachas sin, beidh spleáchais in easnamh agat nuair a "
"dhíshuiteálann tú an sean-aip. Ar an gcaoi chéanna, beidh ort: exc: "
"`LookuPerror` a ghabháil sa ghlao ``apps.get_model () ``a aisghabhann "
"samhlacha ón sean-aip. Ligeann an cur chuige seo duit do thionscadal a "
"imscaradh áit ar bith gan an sean-aip a shuiteáil agus ansin a dhíshuiteáil."

msgid "Here's a sample migration:"
msgstr "Seo imirce samplach:"

msgid "``myapp/migrations/0124_move_old_app_to_new_app.py``"
msgstr "``myapp/imirceach/0124_move_old_app_to_new_app.py``"

msgid ""
"Also consider what you want to happen when the migration is unapplied. You "
"could either do nothing (as in the example above) or remove some or all of "
"the data from the new application. Adjust the second argument of "
"the :mod:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` operation accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh freisin ar cad ba mhaith leat a tharlóidh nuair nach gcuirtear an "
"imirce i bhfeidhm. D'fhéadfá aon rud a dhéanamh (mar atá sa sampla thuas) nó "
"cuid de na sonraí nó go léir a bhaint as an bhfeidhmchlár nua. Coigeartaigh "
"an dara argóint den oibríocht: mod: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` dá réir."

msgid "Changing a ``ManyToManyField`` to use a ``through`` model"
msgstr "Athrú ```ManyTomanyField`` chun samhail ``trí ``a úsáid"

msgid ""
"If you change a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` to use a "
"``through`` model, the default migration will delete the existing table and "
"create a new one, losing the existing relations. To avoid this, you can "
"use :class:`.SeparateDatabaseAndState` to rename the existing table to the "
"new table name while telling the migration autodetector that the new model "
"has been created. You can check the existing table name and constraint name "
"through :djadmin:`sqlmigrate` or :djadmin:`dbshell`. You can check the new "
"table name with the through model's ``_meta.db_table`` property. Your new "
"``through`` model should use the same names for the ``ForeignKey``\\s as "
"Django did. Also if it needs any extra fields, they should be added in "
"operations after :class:`.SeparateDatabaseAndState`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For example, if we had a ``Book`` model with a ``ManyToManyField`` linking "
"to ``Author``, we could add a through model ``AuthorBook`` with a new field "
"``is_primary``, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, dá mbeadh samhail ``Leabhar`` againn le ``ManyTomanyField`` ag "
"nascadh le ``Author ``, d'fhéadfaimis samhail tríd ``Authorbook`` a chur "
"leis le réimse nua ``is_primary``, mar shampla:"

msgid "Changing an unmanaged model to managed"
msgstr "Samhail neamh-bhainistithe a athrú go bainistithe"

msgid ""
"If you want to change an unmanaged model (:attr:`managed=False "
"<django.db.models.Options.managed>`) to managed, you must remove "
"``managed=False`` and generate a migration before making other schema-"
"related changes to the model, since schema changes that appear in the "
"migration that contains the operation to change ``Meta.managed`` may not be "
"applied."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat samhail neamhbhainistithe (:attr: `managed=false "
"<django.db.models.Options.managed>`) a athrú go bainistithe, ní mór duit "
"`Managed = False`` a bhaint agus imirce a ghiniúint sula ndéanann tú "
"athruithe eile a bhaineann le scéim ar an tsamhail, ós rud é nach féidir "
"athruithe scéime atá le feiceáil san imirce ina bhfuil an oibríocht chun "
"`Meta.Managed ``a athrú."
